window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"title":"Chapter 1","paragraphs":["Continental Integration Gallery","Sometimes in life, you find yourself in a situation you never could have anticipated.","Most of the time, you can overcome such situations by thinking on your feet or drawing upon past experience.","But what happens when something occurs that goes far beyond anything like that?","What are you supposed to do then?","What else? You search for a solution by any means necessary.","\"Fuck. What the hell is this?\"","A harsh curse escaped my mouth at the sight before me.","Then again, anyone who saw the situation I was in would probably react the same way.","There was a forest in front of me.","A forest behind me.","A forest to my left and right.","Nothing but forest in every direction.","The trees were so enormous that they even blocked out the sun.","Where was this place, and why was I here?","I could not make sense of the situation at all.","[Welcome to the Continental Integration Gallery.]","\"Ah, shit! You scared me.\"","Just as my mind was going blank, a strange message appeared before my eyes.","It floated in midair like a hologram.","My surprise lasted only a moment before the message transformed into something else.","[Day 114 of Praying for a Full Recovery.][1]","[IThinkImGoingInsaneIThinkImGoingInsaneIThinkImGoingInsaneIThinkImGoingInsane][12]","[Whatever You Do, Don’t Click the Post Below!!!][52]","[This Is the One for Today!][105]","[Is this... the Continental Gallery...?][8]","[I Started Dating My Childhood Friend! AMA!!][10]","[Is there no one willing to engage in a profound discussion with this lady? It is a grave matter.][2]","It had transformed into the most horrifying embodiment of chaos imaginable.","Had I drunk too much last night?","I was seeing things the moment I woke up.","Yet no matter how many times I rubbed my eyes, the window floating in the air remained.","It was enough to drive me insane.","\"Am I... dreaming right now?\"","I had absolutely no idea what was going on.","Half mesmerized, I moved my finger.","Could I actually open these?","It looked remarkably similar to the online galleries I had often seen on the internet.","Among the collection of chaotic posts, I selected the one with the highest number of comments.","[This post does not exist or has been deleted.]","\"...?\"","It left me with an even greater mystery than the chaos itself.","Had I known this would happen, I would have clicked it sooner.","Still, thanks to that, I began to understand the situation I was in.","I folded my arms and started browsing through the gallery.","I had never been a particularly devoted gallery user, but I had looked through them a few times when I needed information.","Even though this one appeared like a hologram, it was extremely simple to use.","Whether I gestured with my hand or merely moved my eyes, it responded exactly as I intended.","Title: Day 114 of Praying for a Full Recovery","Starlight Princess","Day 114 of praying for a full recovery.","└ Hang in there.","I selected the post with the fewest comments, but it contained only a short message and an equally short reply.","That alone was not enough to judge anything.","Before that, however, I needed to determine whether my current location was safe.","’I have no idea what’s going on, but I should be careful.’","There was no telling what might emerge from the forest.","I would be in serious trouble if something like a bear suddenly appeared.","Fortunately, a little light filtered through the trees here and there, so I could at least see what was ahead.","I started walking.","\"Hmm?\"","Then I noticed a peculiar plant.","The densely packed trees concealed it from view, but they could not hide its faint glow.","I also needed somewhere to conceal myself.","Moving cautiously, I slipped between the trees and settled into place.","’That looks strange.’","At first glance, it seemed like an ordinary plant, but its petals were shaped exactly like crescent moons.","Even without any light falling upon it, it shimmered like a crescent moon in the night sky.","It was an incredibly beautiful flower.","’Beautiful things usually contain poison.’","So I did not touch it.","Things like that were exactly what you were never supposed to mess with in an unfamiliar forest.","If you do not know what it is, do not eat it.","Especially mushrooms.","You would be better off eating bugs or insects instead.","I sincerely hoped things would not deteriorate to that point, but given my current circumstances, I had to consider the possibility.","’Are there any rules?’","I raised my head and opened the gallery.","Apparently, merely thinking about it was enough to bring it up.","When I checked the post at the very top, I found a notice prominently displayed.","Title: Notice","Don’tAbandonTheHero (Head Admin)","Posts that cause discomfort or disgust to others are prohibited!Obscene photographs and videos are prohibited!Posts that create tension between nations are prohibited!Excessive socializing and hostility toward newcomers are prohibited!Violating any of the above rules will result in a ban!Let us preserve peace within the gallery!Heroes are not harmful! Please do not abandon them!","(Most important!)","└ Forget everything else. What’s with the last rule? LMAO","└ What’s the hero doing right now? Sleeping?","└ For real, I heard people saying the hero is useless now that the world is at peace.","└ Rumor has it the Empire sent an execution squad after them, lol.","└ Damn, that’s pitiful. LMAO","The orange-colored name probably meant that person was some kind of administrator.","I remembered hearing something like that before.","The notice was fairly straightforward.","It did not seem like there would be any reason to ban someone as long as they did not cross the line.","The gallery was also extremely easy and convenient to use.","Users could take and upload photographs and videos, and they could even trade with one another.","However, direct trades between users, rather than auctions, were limited to those with registered usernames.","Apparently, it was meant to prevent illegal transactions.","More importantly, because personal relationships between users posed a risk, private conversations during trades were limited to three minutes.","’Users can trade with each other?’","Of everything I had discovered, that was the best news.","I did not even know where I was right now.","Money and everything else could go to hell.","What mattered was obtaining supplies necessary for survival.","Even finding food would be difficult.","I also needed a weapon to protect myself, tools for making fire, and countless other things.","However, trades tended to be one-sided.","That was especially true when one side was desperate.","After thinking it over again and again, I created a registered username.","Before worrying about trading, I first needed to determine where I was.","Title: Woke Up in a Forest. Where Am I?","Wild Grylls","(A photo of a forest densely packed with trees.)","I drank last night and woke up here. ;;","Does anyone know where this is?","For now, I uploaded a post to the gallery.","At the very least, I already understood that this was another world.","The problem was figuring out where in that world I had landed.","I did not even have the luxury of wondering why I had been brought here.","I needed to survive first.","Only then could I take my time thinking about everything else.","There was no point in anything if I died.","But thanks to the post, I realized one thing.","I had just done something incredibly stupid.","Obviously, if I posted nothing but a random picture of a forest, it would be difficult for anyone to identify which forest it was.","Still, the fact that they had bothered to comment at all meant they were at least somewhat helpful bastards.","So I made another post.","Title: What’s the Most Famous Forest on the Continent?","Wild Grylls","└ ? What is this guy even trying to do?","└ This is like posting a picture of someone’s leg and asking us to guess who it belongs to, lol.","└ Want me to upload a picture of my leg? Try guessing who I am.","└ You’re a woman.","└ Correct.","└ Actually, I’m a man, lol.","└ You bastard.","Hmm.","Nothing but completely useless comments.","Assholes.","└ Let’sGrowTrees: Obviously, it’s Alfheim!","└ Get lost, knife-ears.","└ Let’sGrowTrees: Knife-ears? We merely stated the truth!","└ Says the knife-ear bastards who destroyed their own forest and started invading other people’s territory.","└ Let’sGrowTrees: The Mother of Nature has spoken. Every forest is Alfheim!","└ PassingDwarf: Because of those bastards, all the firewood disappeared. Fuck.","└ Knife-ears really stick their noses into everything. Nothing but trouble.","└ Didn’t they invade the underground a hundred years ago because they wanted to grow the World Tree’s roots? Lol.","└ These days, those bastards are worse than demons, lmao.","Guys.","Could you please leave some normal comments?","I had hoped the registered user called \"Let’sGrowTrees\" would be useful, but apparently not.","Every forest was Alfheim.","Alfheim was elven territory.","Therefore, every forest belonged to the elves.","They were spreading that absurd logic around.","’What is this, imperialism?’","Weren’t elves supposed to be a race that loved nature?","The fact that other races existed was shocking enough, but their mentality was even more surprising.","One thing was certain.","Nothing good would come from getting involved with that race.","I asked another question.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there any forest the elves hate?","└ PassingDwarf: Yeah, there is. It’s called the Forest of Four Seasons. Famous for being a goddamn nightmare.","└ Wild Grylls: What kind of place is it?","└ PassingDwarf: Is your head an anvil? Did someone hit it with a hammer?","What the hell?","This bastard started insulting me out of nowhere.","My head did hurt as though someone had smashed it with a hammer, probably because I had drunk so much last night.","But I had not actually been hit.","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah, I told you I woke up in a forest. ;; My head hurts too, so maybe you’re right.","└ PassingDwarf: ;;","└ Boo! Trash!","└ Still, the OP is kind of pitiful. What the hell did you do?","└ Wild Grylls: All I did was drink. Though I did drink quite a lot.","└ PassingDwarf: Fuck, then it’s your own fault. ;; What kind of idiot can’t even find his way home?","└ An alcoholic getting scolded by a dwarf, damn.","Was that really the issue?","I had woken up in another world.","What was I supposed to do about that?","Fortunately, PassingDwarf went on to explain the Forest of Four Seasons in detail.","Apparently, it was the most dangerous forest on the continent.","Just as its name suggested, it contained spring, summer, autumn, and winter.","At first, I had no idea what that meant.","But it did not take long for me to understand why it was called the Forest of Four Seasons.","’Each region has its own season? What kind of bullshit is that...?’","And that was not all.","The forest was rich in mana, so all kinds of dangerous monsters lurked within it.","Worse still, anyone who entered completely lost their sense of direction and could never find their way out.","Because of that, criminals were often thrown into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Not a single person had ever emerged alive.","└ PassingDwarf: On the bright side, it has plenty of elixirs and medicinal herbs.","└ Wild Grylls: But I don’t know which plants are medicinal.","└ PassingDwarf: Then I guess you die, lol. Eat a mushroom and drop dead.","└ Wild Grylls: You bastard.","\"Haah...\"","A frustrated sigh escaped me.","I sincerely hoped this was not the Forest of Four Seasons.","If it really was...","I had no idea what I would do.","Still, he said there were many medicinal herbs, so perhaps I could survive by using them somehow.","Thinking about returning home could wait until after I escaped the forest.","There was nothing I could accomplish by staying rooted here.","’In that case...’","I glanced between my legs.","More precisely, at the ground beneath them.","The plant with the distinctive crescent-shaped petals.","Could this be a medicinal herb as well?","Since I knew nothing about this world, asking the gallery seemed like a reasonable idea.","Online galleries had been useful whenever I posted questions before.","A Continental Integration Gallery ought to be even more useful.","Title: Anyone Know What Herb This Is?","Wild Grylls","(A picture of the crescent-shaped plant.)","I don’t know what kind of herb this is. Anyone recognize it?","Less than three seconds after I uploaded the post—","└ Heavenly Demon: Would you be willing to trade it with this lady? It is an urgent matter.","Someone with the registered username Heavenly Demon immediately left a comment.","Wasn’t \"Heavenly Demon\" the sort of title that only appeared in martial arts novels?","I immediately checked the user’s post history.","I had no intention of trading with some lunatic.","[Heavenly Demon]","[Posts: 2,548] [Comments: 3,817]","[Is there no one willing to engage in a profound discussion with this lady? It is a grave matter.] — 10 minutes ago","[My body grows heavier by the moment.] — 30 minutes ago","[The heavens are the heavens, and the earth is the earth. To think I failed to comprehend such a simple truth.] — 1 hour ago","It was filled with ordinary shitposts.","Hardly any of the posts had many comments, either.","’What is this? Some role-playing freak?’","Her manner of speech was unbearably lofty, yet she spent her time browsing a gallery.","The two things did not seem to fit together.","Still, I should at least hear her out.","First, I checked the comments.","└ How much money do you need? Just name your price.","└ Sword Master: Is that thing valuable?","└ Starlight Princess: That herb is useless to me... I need something containing the energy of the sun...","└ PassingDwarf: Good sir, would you perhaps be interested in a sword personally crafted by a dwarf?","Oh my.","What was going on?","After I briefly checked Heavenly Demon’s posts, an enormous number of comments had appeared.","Even PassingDwarf, who had been so abrasive until moments ago, had suddenly become polite.","Was this herb really that valuable?","└ Heavenly Demon: Silence!! This lady claimed it first, yet you are all consumed by greed!!","└ Yeah, that means nothing~","└ Claimed it first, my ass, lol. The OP will choose whoever they like.","└ Move aside, old hag~","└ Fuck, is that really a New Moon Spirit Herb? Why is one of those there?","└ GiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMeGiveItToMe","Heavenly Demon, who had left the first comment, was eventually buried beneath the flood.","Even when she repeatedly tried to make her presence known, it was useless.","Since users could trade with one another, I occasionally saw astronomical amounts being offered.","Of course, I had no idea how valuable this world’s currency was.","Still, one thing was obvious.","’I should choose the person who looks the most desperate.’","And among them, one user continued stubbornly asserting her presence.","As anyone could have guessed, it was Heavenly Demon.","She must have truly been in a hurry, because she was posting comments at an astonishing speed.","Watching her made me feel a little sorry for her.","’Judging from her posts, maybe she really is sick.’","Starlight Princess also seemed ill, but she had already made it clear that the herb was useless to her.","After thinking it over again and again, I decided to choose Heavenly Demon.","Countless trade requests had already arrived, but I ignored them all and selected her.","Having something taken away from you even after you claimed it first was a filthy, despair-inducing feeling.","I knew that all too well.","Apparently, the administrators possessed more authority than I had expected.","Or perhaps they were simply that wary of illegal transactions and excessive socializing.","I was doing neither, so I sent the request without hesitation.","What I needed right now were survival supplies.","’What will she give me?’","I waited with anticipation.","[Heavenly Demon has accepted your request.]"]},{"title":"Chapter 2","paragraphs":["Fortuitous Encounter (1)","If someone asked who the strongest person on the continent was, who would come to mind?","It was one of those debates that frequently broke out not only in the Continental Integration Gallery, but also in everyday life.","Some would name Ash, the Sword Master of the Empire.","Others would point to Kadir, the Archmage of the Kingdom.","Some would choose the princess of the demon race, while others would name the vanished Hero.","Everyone had a different answer depending on their nationality, birthplace, background, and personal connections.","Even so, the fact that those people were extraordinarily powerful remained unchanged.","Title: Who Is the Strongest Person on the Continent?","Ash of the Messiah EmpireKadir of the Iris KingdomKeirin of MephistoThe Missing Hero","└ Heavenly Demon: Strange. Why is this lady not included in the poll?","└ Who are you?","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady is the rightful successor and ruler of the Divine Cult—the Heavenly Demon.","└ Yeah, but who the hell is that? LMAO.","However, rumors originating from the gallery were never particularly trustworthy.","In other words, they were unofficial.","More than anything, the very idea of the Heavenly Demon browsing an online gallery was ridiculous.","Why would someone powerful enough to bring every master of the Central Plains to their knees and unite the martial world spend her time on a gallery?","And she invested a considerable amount of time into it, too.","Hardly a day passed without the Heavenly Demon uploading some meaningless shitpost.","Most people were unaware of it, but a monster lived in \"Jung,\" the nation known for its mysticism.","Jung was far more isolationist than other countries, so very little information about it was available.","However, not even its isolationist policies could block access to the gallery.","└ If she really is the Heavenly Demon, then she’s not wrong. She’s absurdly strong.","└ How strong?","└ She’d probably crush every one of them in a one-on-one fight, lol. Every master in the Central Plains got wrecked by the Heavenly Demon.","└ Then why hasn’t anyone heard about her? I think I’ve seen similar stories on the gallery before.","└ Why don’t you try investing in stocks based entirely on rumors too?","└ Ah.","└ Heavenly Demon, who do you think is the strongest person on the continent?","└ Heavenly Demon: Naturally, it is this lady.","└ LMAO. Why even ask her? Of course she’d say herself.","└ Heavenly Demon: Then allow this lady to ask in return. What realm have those people reached? Have they attained the Transformation Realm?","└ Sword Master: I’m a Sword Master.","└ Allfather: I’m a Tenth-Circle mage.","└ PrincessPickMe: I’m a Ninth-Circle mage!","└ Heavenly Demon: What are those things? This lady is unfamiliar with the language of the Western Lands.","└ Look at this ancient hag, lmao.","As a result, the gallery users treated Heavenly Demon as either a role-playing freak or an out-of-touch old-timer.","In truth, users from the Central Plains were generally unfamiliar with the languages and slang of other countries.","Everything on the gallery was automatically translated.","However, proper nouns and slang could not always be translated into the corresponding terms of another country.","It was a consequence of Jung’s isolationism.","Ironically, that was also why so many people from there used the gallery.","└ Heavenly Demon: When this lady entered the martial world, she was also granted the title of the Greatest Beauty Under Heaven.","└ If you’re really the Heavenly Demon, do something about the emperor. Apparently, using the gallery is punishable by death.","└ Heavenly Demon: To think he would dare obstruct this lady’s hobby. He clearly does not fear the heavens.","After that post, rumors spread that the emperor of Jung had been assassinated.","Gallery usage also suddenly became legal and unrestricted.","Thanks to that, everyone reached the point where they began wondering whether Heavenly Demon might actually be the real Heavenly Demon.","Title: Heavenly Demon, Read This","If you’re really the Heavenly Demon, prove it by showing your face. Then we’ll believe you.","└ Heavenly Demon: You dare demand that this lady reveal her august countenance? How insolent.","└ Are you ugly or something? An old hag? LMAO.","As time passed, Heavenly Demon became increasingly famous.","Not as the actual Heavenly Demon, but as an old role-player who had become completely consumed by her character.","Someone even commented that if the real Heavenly Demon ever saw her posts, she would tear out the impersonator’s organs and personally have her ripped apart by horses.","It was understandable.","Almost everything Heavenly Demon posted was complete nonsense.","The prevailing opinion was that no one could write that many posts unless they had a truly absurd amount of free time.","\"Strange. Why does no one believe this lady?\"","Meanwhile, the real Heavenly Demon stared at the gallery with a puzzled expression.","Skin as white as milk.","Full lips.","A breathtakingly beautiful face and voluptuous curves that could not be concealed even by her black martial robes.","She was Yu So-Wol, the sole being who reigned as the one true \"Demon\" beneath the heavens.","She was also the user called Heavenly Demon, who diligently browsed the gallery every day.","\"This lady has proven everything already. Tsk, tsk.\"","Yu So-Wol clicked her tongue.","Despite that, there was not a trace of irritation on her face.","If anything, she looked amused.","After all, the gallery was the Heavenly Demon’s only hobby.","One might wonder why a grand figure like the Heavenly Demon would waste her time browsing a gallery.","But in the end, she was human too.","Even after defeating every master in the Central Plains and claiming the title of Greatest Under Heaven, she still could not escape boredom.","She had become so overwhelmingly powerful that no one even dared challenge her anymore.","So, under the pretense of entering secluded cultivation, she shut herself away in the mountains.","Title: Upvote If You Think the Heavenly Demon Is Weak as Shit LMAO","└ LMAO.","└ Upvoted, lmao.","└ Agreed, hahaha.","\"Hehe. These bastards deserve to be chewed to pieces. To think they dare mock this lady.\"","This was exactly what she liked.","People who hid behind anonymity and spouted whatever nonsense came to mind.","Back in the Divine Cult, most followers could not even bring themselves to meet her eyes.","Naturally so.","Yu So-Wol was the sole supreme ruler beneath the heavens.","They were too busy worshipping her.","But the gallery was different.","Using anonymity as a shield, people hurled insults at her so outrageous that they could never have spoken them aloud.","Sometimes, they even made sexually suggestive remarks.","Yu So-Wol generously ignored those.","They were strangers whose faces she did not even know.","’Truthfully, this lady would like to fight the masters of the Western Lands...’","Still, there was one thing that bothered her.","Whenever people discussed the strongest person on the continent, she was always excluded.","The other nations had interacted extensively, so the names of their strongest warriors had become widely known.","The Central Plains were different.","Because of their isolationist policies, they remained frogs trapped at the bottom of a well.","She had considered visiting the Western Lands herself, but strangely enough, her followers had desperately opposed it.","\"You cannot.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"If Heaven personally leaves, countless problems will arise.\"","\"How so?\"","\"If you remain absent for too long, the believers will fall into confusion. Wicked martial artists may also use the opportunity to attack. More importantly...\"","\"More importantly?\"","\"Shouldn’t those arrogant barbarians come here themselves? It would make no sense for the Supreme One to personally visit them.\"","\"Hmm. That is true.\"","Thus, the Heavenly Demon was persuaded by her trusted strategist, the \"Demon Brain.\"","However, the Demon Brain’s actual reasoning was entirely different.","Things would become a complete disaster the moment she fought one of the masters from another country.","The Central Plains had not even been fully stabilized yet.","What would happen if they dragged foreign barbarians into the mess as well?","The Heavenly Demon Divine Cult, which they had struggled so hard to establish, might collapse.","It was a perfectly realistic judgment.","└ Is that bastard insane? LMAO.","└ SmartDemon: If that happened, my head would explode.","Title: I’m Going Insane Because of the Woman I Serve","SmartDemon","That woman has nothing but martial arts in her head, and she’s trying to cause trouble again. Thank god I barely managed to stop her. Otherwise, I would’ve run away immediately.","└ Hang in there, man. What do you do for a living?","└ SmartDemon: In the language of the Western Lands... a secretary? A steward? Just think of it as something like that.","└ Sounds rough working for a boss like that.","└ SmartDemon: Haah... Fuck, I want to quit so badly.","└ Why don’t you?","└ SmartDemon: It’s a lifetime position, lol. I started serving her under her parents.","A suspiciously meaningful post appeared on the gallery shortly afterward, but the Heavenly Demon ignored it.","Things like that happened all the time.","Afterward, she remained inside the Divine Cult, briefly emerged because of the emperor, and then returned to her ordinary days.","Being Yu So-Wol the \"human,\" who traded vicious insults with others, was far more entertaining than being Yu So-Wol the \"Heavenly Demon,\" whom everyone revered.","Then, one day, she attained a sudden enlightenment and entered secluded cultivation.","However, she soon encountered a completely unexpected obstacle.","\"Cough!\"","Splatter!","When Yu So-Wol coughed, a large mouthful of pitch-black blood spilled out.","It was a considerable amount.","She wiped the blood from her lips and stared ahead with a complicated expression.","\"To think this lady would suffer qi deviation...\"","That was right.","While deeply immersed in cultivation, she had fallen into qi deviation.","└ But if he’s a secretary, does he actually crawl under the desk?","Since her condition was practically terminal, she emptied her mind and wrote a post on the gallery.","Title: Is There No One Willing to Engage in a Profound Discussion with This Lady? It Is a Grave Matter.","Heavenly Demon","The title says everything.","└ Heavenly Demon Death Beam!!","└ Taaaang!","One might ask how the sole supreme ruler beneath the heavens could possibly suffer qi deviation.","However, this was a kind of trial.","It was like an insect shedding its skin, where success meant survival and failure meant death.","To begin with, anyone could suffer qi deviation.","Being the Heavenly Demon did not make her an exception.","’My internal energy... is becoming far too powerful.’","The Heavenly Demon was strong.","The problem was that she was far too strong.","Yu So-Wol looked down at her hand.","Cracks spread across it like a spiderweb, making it seem as though it might shatter at any moment.","Her body could no longer withstand the power contained within it and was collapsing under its own strength.","There were only two ways to overcome this.","Either she had to bring the energy inside her under control, or neutralize it with a powerful elixir.","However, despite repeatedly attempting the former, her internal energy only continued to grow stronger without diminishing in the slightest.","’The heavens are the heavens, and the earth is the earth...’","Even so, she continued browsing the gallery until the bitter end.","In truth, she had already half given up.","As long as her internal energy continued growing stronger, it was only a matter of time before her frail shell failed to endure it and burst apart.","\"Hehe.\"","Yu So-Wol laughed.","Her expression was filled with pity, as though she were looking at some pathetic idiot.","To think the only thing she could rely on at a time like this was the gallery.","Her self-mockery soon turned into self-loathing.","That only caused her qi deviation to worsen, but she had already reached a state of resignation.","’Is this how it ends...?’","She might as well browse the gallery one last time.","She had no desire to die alone in silence.","Yu So-Wol had initially been furious, but it did not take long for anxiety to replace her anger.","The competition had become far too fierce.","She had already sent a trade request long ago.","However, Wild Grylls had not accepted it.","’How disgraceful.’","Yu So-Wol let out a bitter laugh.","She had behaved disgracefully until the very end.","Still, it was unbearably frustrating.","She had wanted to die in battle, not perish in such a miserable fashion.","The energy within her grew increasingly uncontrollable, while the life remaining to her dwindled by the moment.","Just as Yu So-Wol was about to lament her fate and close her eyes—","The moment her request was accepted, a rectangular window appeared in front of her.","It was an empty chat box.","[Wild Grylls: Hey, hey. You’re Heavenly Demon, right?]","A brief greeting filled the empty space.","It sounded frivolous, yet it was surprisingly polite.","Yu So-Wol cleared her throat without realizing it and sent a reply.","[Heavenly Demon: Indeed. This lady is the one and only Heaven of the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult—the Heavenly Demon. Do you truly intend to trade with this lady?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. You left the first comment, didn’t you? First come, first served.]","[Heavenly Demon: Thank you. It is rare to find someone who understands proper manners.]","[Wild Grylls has sent you a trade request. Would you like to accept?]","A hand of salvation had descended from the heavens.","Yu So-Wol’s eyes gradually widened.","Why?","Why had he chosen her out of so many people?","Her thoughts were lengthy, but her actions were swift.","She hurriedly accepted the request.","Fortunately, Wild Grylls did not appear to be ill-mannered.","The Heavenly Demon sighed inwardly in relief.","The gallery was much like a cesspit.","Countless people hid behind anonymity and revealed their desires without restraint.","Yet within that cesspit, she had discovered such courtesy.","It felt like finding a single rose blooming amid filth.","[Heavenly Demon: Is there anything you desire? This lady will obtain anything within her power.]","Her options were currently limited because she needed to remain in secluded cultivation.","However, once she returned to the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult, she intended to grant him anything he wished.","Even the Heavenly Demon did not forget debts of gratitude or grudges.","If he desired it, she was even willing to pass down a secret martial arts manual.","[Wild Grylls: For now, I need a tool for making fire and a compass. A weapon to protect myself and some simple food. That should be enough.]","The Heavenly Demon was puzzled.","That was all he wanted?","What was the New Moon Spirit Herb?","It was one of the greatest medicinal herbs in existence, something people would gladly pay a fortune to obtain.","It was possible.","The Heavenly Demon turned her head toward the corner of the cave.","There lay a secret manual containing the insights she had gained, a large pile of fasting pills, and even her cherished sword.","She could satisfy two of his conditions.","She did not possess a tool for making fire, but there was another method.","[Heavenly Demon: What realm have you reached? Have you entered the Transformation Realm?]","[Wild Grylls: I’m just an ordinary person...]","\"Damn.\"","In that case, she could not teach him how to use the Samadhi True Flame.","Yu So-Wol hurriedly moved on to the next matter.","[Heavenly Demon: Is that truly all you require? As you surely know, the New Moon Spirit Herb is an exceedingly precious medicinal herb.]","[Wild Grylls: Even so, can it be worth more than my life? I only need what I actually need.]","[Heavenly Demon: Hmm... Very well. Given this lady’s current circumstances, there are some things that will be difficult to obtain immediately. However, they can be acquired with time.]","[Wild Grylls: I’m in a difficult situation too, so I’m in a hurry. Can you provide them or not?]","[Heavenly Demon: Regrettably, this lady can only satisfy two of your requests at present. A weapon and food.]","[Wild Grylls: Hmm...]","[Heavenly Demon: However, once this lady descends from the Divine Cult, the other two items shall also be delivered.]","Yu So-Wol grew increasingly anxious.","As her internal energy continued to intensify, cold sweat began pouring down her body.","Furthermore, trades were limited to three minutes.","Once those three minutes passed, the two users would be unable to trade again for an entire day.","[Wild Grylls: Okay, got it.]","[Heavenly Demon: Truly?]","[Wild Grylls: You said you’d give them to me, so I’ll trust you. If you don’t, then I’ll stop trusting you afterward.]","\"Ah...\"","What an exceptionally courteous young man.","Yu So-Wol was deeply moved.","He was both a fortuitous encounter and a benefactor who had appeared at her most desperate moment.","She had never experienced anything like this, not when she first entered the martial world nor when she unified the Central Plains.","It felt as though everything in the world had grown brighter.","Even though she sat inside a dark cave, her conversation with Wild Grylls shone as brightly as the sun.","’Ah. This is no time for that.’","Yu So-Wol hurriedly gathered her sword and fasting pills.","If she successfully entered the next realm, she would no longer need either of them.","As someone who had used the gallery for a long time, she already knew how trading worked.","All she had to do was hold or touch the object she wished to send.","[Wild Grylls has registered an item for trade.]","[Heavenly Demon has registered items for trade.]","[Would you like to complete the trade?]","She accepted immediately.","The other side must have accepted just as quickly, because the message changed at once.","[The trade has been completed.]","[Wild Grylls: Mine arrived. Did yours?]","Yu So-Wol did not see the message.","She was too busy hurriedly stuffing the New Moon Spirit Herb into her mouth.","She felt truly apologetic toward Wild Grylls, but her life was in danger.","The moment she consumed the herb, she entered meditative circulation.","As expected, the instant she absorbed the herb’s energy, her internal energy—which had burned like an active volcano—gradually began to stabilize.","Even Yu So-Wol herself was surprised.","At this rate, she would be able to break through her shell and ascend to the next realm.","Relief washed over her, but she did not lose focus.","She had no desire to waste this hard-earned opportunity through carelessness.","’Just a little more... Just a little more.’","Wooooong—","Yu So-Wol’s body slowly rose into the air as she continued circulating her energy.","Her beautiful ebony hair floated around her as though drifting underwater, while a faint light seeped from her body.","Crack!","Like a bird breaking free from its egg, Yu So-Wol underwent a similar transformation.","Her body had already experienced Bone and Marrow Cleansing once, yet it was undergoing the process again.","The cracked layers of her skin fell away as new flesh emerged beneath them.","Her bones and body shifted into a form more suitable for the power she now possessed.","A realm liberated from all demonic limitations—","The Realm of Transcending Demonhood.","In the Central Plains, it was known as the Profound Realm.","Yu So-Wol’s closed eyes slowly opened.","They were not the eyes of someone who had just stared death in the face.","Her black pupils were as calm as a still lake and as gentle as a spring breeze.","The Heavenly Demon, Yu So-Wol, had broken free of her shell once more and taken the world into her eyes anew.","\"Phew...\"","Yu So-Wol released a long breath.","It was a sigh filled with countless complicated emotions.","She then looked down at her hand.","Smooth, pale skin had grown over it.","It was the very image of a delicate jade hand.","She was satisfied.","A smile naturally appeared on her lips.","She had no idea how she could possibly repay this grace.","’Ah. Damn. I never thanked him.’","Yu So-Wol hurriedly accessed the gallery.","Too much time had passed, and her conversation with Wild Grylls had already ended.","All she could do now was write a public post.","Even after reaching the Realm of Transcending Demonhood, Yu So-Wol the human had not disappeared.","Quite the opposite.","Meeting a benefactor in her moment of crisis had only strengthened her human side.","She wanted to repay this kindness by any means possible.","But how could she repay such grace?","She had never been indebted to anyone in her entire life.","She had accumulated more grudges than she could count, but this was the first time anyone had ever shown her such kindness.","Her heart pounded, and a smile unconsciously formed on her lips.","Even she did not notice her own reaction.","Title: Wild Grylls, Read This","Heavenly Demon","Thanks to you, this lady has received a debt of gratitude that will take a lifetime to repay.","This lady shall obtain anything you desire, so name whatever you wish.","If you desire it, this lady can personally grant you a secret martial arts manual.","Ah, and lest there be any misunderstanding, the items you requested will be delivered without fail.","\"...Why are you not answering?\"","Yu So-Wol voiced her disappointment.","Only a few minutes had passed, but to her they felt unbearably long.","’Could it be because I failed to thank him immediately?’","Yu So-Wol’s concern deepened.","***","The Heavenly Demon had even addressed him as \"young master.\"","It was a form of address bordering on the highest possible level of respect.","Several comments appeared afterward, but none came from the person she wanted.","Yu So-Wol waited endlessly for her benefactor to respond.","Yet even after several minutes passed, Wild Grylls left no comment.","Meanwhile, Wild Grylls was—","\"Woof! Woof! Grrrr! Woof!\"","\"Whoa! Fuck!\"","—being chased by a beast.","Contrary to the Heavenly Demon’s assumptions, he was in absolutely no position to access the gallery."]},{"title":"Chapter 3","paragraphs":["Fortuitous Encounter (2)","What was the most dangerous thing in the wilderness?","The three great poisons—poisonous plants, venomous insects, and venomous snakes?","Correct.","Or perhaps mushrooms, the ultimate gamble?","Also correct.","Maybe starvation or dehydration?","That was correct too.","Beyond the protective boundaries of civilization, everything in the wilderness was dangerous.","Even the ground beneath your feet could not be trusted.","And when judged individually, humans were incredibly weak creatures.","Without tools, a person probably could not even defeat a large dog.","\"Woof! Woof! Woof!\"","\"Woof! Woof!\"","A pack of massive dogs was barking viciously in front of me.","The problem was that they were not merely large dogs.","They were almost as big as cattle.","As expected of a fantasy world, even the stray dogs had absurdly high specs.","’At least they can’t come any closer because of their size...’","Taking their enormous bodies into account, I had deliberately entered a densely wooded area.","The place where I had found the herb had also been decent, but it was open on all sides.","The trees there were thinner too.","So I had fled in a hurry.","I had not forgotten the sword and bundle of food I received from the Heavenly Demon.","Now, I was holding my ground with my back against a gigantic rock wall.","The wild dogs did not seem willing to force their way between the trees.","They merely watched me from outside.","In other words, they were intelligent.","They knew I currently had the advantage.","’What should I do?’","Was my only option to remain here?","I sincerely hoped those damn dogs would give up and leave.","However, one should always prepare for the worst.","I immediately accessed the gallery.","Since they had not attacked yet, I planned to ask for help.","Title: Urgent—How Do I Deal With These Damn Dogs?","Wild Grylls","(A picture of enormous dogs glaring between the trees.)","What am I supposed to do with these bastards? Anyone have a method?","└ Aren’t those Mad Dogs? Why are they so huge?","└ Even a Sword Expert would have trouble fighting those things.","└ Farewell. I’ll pray for your soul.","└ The moment one bites you, you’ll probably die of rabies, lmao.","└ Wild Grylls: Stop answering my question with more questions, you bastards.","These people were completely useless.","I frowned.","As time passed, these Mad Dogs would continue looking for an opportunity.","I had to come up with something.","└ Heavenly Demon: No! You must not die! Please survive long enough for this lady to repay her debt!","└ Why does she sound so desperate? LMAO.","└ Anyone would think they were lovers, lol.","The Heavenly Demon’s not-quite-encouragement was somewhat comforting.","It did not provide any practical help, though.","Still, the growing number of comments meant more people were seeing the post.","Hopefully, at least one useful person would appear.","I did not know what a Sword Expert was, but I could tell that these creatures were monsters by my standards.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Ah! I’ve encountered those monsters many times! Their noses are their weak point. If you stab one in the nose with a sword, it should lose consciousness for several seconds!","└ How does the head admin know that?","└ Aren’t those monsters difficult to encounter?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Because I’m the Hero! I know how to deal with every monster and demonic beast!","Fortunately, the passing head administrator kindly explained their weakness.","Just as I was about to feel encouraged—","└ Sword Master: But to actually do what the head admin suggested, wouldn’t you need to be at least a high-level Sword Expert? As far as I know, anyway.","└ The most useless theory in the world: \"As far as I know,\" lmao.","└ What happens if he fails?","└ Sword Master: They’ll enter a berserk state, smash through the trees, and then he’ll die.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: That’s why you have to cut off their heads or stab their hearts before that happens! I can do it!","Holy shit.","The head admin was apparently a monster wearing human skin.","And how did Sword Master know all this?","└ Wild Grylls: Fuck, is there no method for an ordinary person? All I have is the sword the Heavenly Demon gave me.","└ Ordinary people never encounter those things. ;; OP, are you really in the Forest of Four Seasons? Are you perhaps a criminal?","└ No, that can’t be it. They gouge out criminals’ eyes before throwing them into the Forest of Four Seasons so they can’t use the gallery.","└ That’s insanely brutal. ;;","└ Doesn’t gallery access stop working inside the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ It’s \"doesn’t,\" not \"don’t.\"","└ Yeah, I heard the mana there gets tangled and blocks access.","└ Just hit them in the head. No matter how big they are, dogs are still dogs.","A great deal of useless nonsense appeared, but the conclusion was simple.","Hit them in the head.","Truly valuable information.","It was about as insightful as saying, \"Humans die if they do not drink water.\"","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady’s sword is a masterpiece among masterpieces. Severing the heads of those wild dogs should be effortless. Trust this lady.","└ Sword Master: How good is it? Better than Durandal or Excalibur?","└ Heavenly Demon: What are those? In any case, this lady’s sword was forged from Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron.","└ Ten-thousand-year cold iron, lmaoooo.","└ Does Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron grow on trees or something? LMAO.","Thus spoke the Heavenly Demon:","Her sword was a masterpiece among masterpieces.","After reading her words, I looked down at the weapon.","It certainly did not look ordinary.","I could tell that it had been meticulously maintained.","I also had the advantage of the terrain.","I should be able to fight them.","’It’s do or die.’","I looked at the largest dog standing in the center.","There were three of them in total, and the one in the middle was by far the biggest.","It was probably the leader.","Without hesitation, I charged toward it.","\"Woof! Woof!\"","The two dogs guarding either side of the leader immediately began squeezing through the gaps between the trees.","\"It was a trap, you bastards!\"","I had only pretended to target the leader.","Instead, I turned toward one of its subordinates.","The one on the left came first.","More than half its body had already emerged between the trees.","I swung the sword down vertically toward its head.","I knew absolutely nothing about swordsmanship, so rather than cutting, I simply struck downward with all my strength.","Swish—","\"Hmm?\"","Something was strange.","I had definitely swung the sword, yet the blade seemed to pass straight through the dog’s head.","For a moment, I wondered whether I had struck an illusion.","But the result appeared soon afterward.","Split!","The dog’s head suddenly split vertically down the middle.","Thud!","It collapsed with its tongue hanging out.","Even its tongue had been divided cleanly in half.","I stared down at the dog in bewilderment.","I had felt almost no resistance in my hands.","At most, it had felt like cutting tofu with a knife.","The sheer unreality of it left me dazed.","\"Grrrwoof!\"","Ah.","Right.","There was still another one.","The instant I heard the sound behind me, I swung the sword reflexively.","It had come from so close that my body moved before I could think.","Splatter!","Fortunately, the dog never managed to pounce on me.","Instead, its head and torso separated and fell to the ground.","Just like before, I barely felt the blade cut through anything.","I stared blankly between the two corpses.","Whatever else might be true, I had realized one thing.","The Heavenly Demon was a god.","And this sword was invincible.","\"Grrrr...!\"","\"Ah. You were still here.\"","Only the leader remained.","It glared at me warily, every muscle in its body tense.","A taut silence stretched between us through the thick trees.","Which of us would retreat first?","Naturally, it was the leader.","It glanced back and forth at the corpses of its subordinates, then slowly began to back away.","It must have realized that as long as I had the sword, it was the one at a disadvantage.","Smart bastard.","\"Phew!\"","The danger had finally passed.","I let out a long breath filled with all the tension that had built up inside me.","What would have happened if I had not received the Heavenly Demon’s sword?","Or if I had never happened to discover that herb in the first place?","I still did not have a compass, so wandering around recklessly was difficult.","I would have to wait until the Heavenly Demon sent one.","’Ah. Before that, I should thank her.’","Without delay, I wrote a post on the gallery.","Title: The Heavenly Demon Is a God","Wild Grylls","(A picture of the dead dogs on the ground and my hand gripping the sword tightly.)","And this sword is invincible.","└ Holy shit, he actually killed those things?","└ That sword really is insanely good, lmao.","└ Sword Master: Those were extremely clean cuts. Even with an excellent sword, achieving that would be difficult.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: You’re alive! What a relief! It seems there will be nothing to mourn today!","└ Heavenly Demon: Are you injured anywhere?","└ Wild Grylls: I’m fine, thanks to you. Thank you for the excellent sword.","└ Heavenly Demon: That is a relief. This lady feared that something terrible had happened to you.","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady is proficient with every weapon. If one had to be chosen, however, it would be the sword.","Come to think of it, Sword Master also seemed rather old-fashioned.","Unlike most users, they used proper punctuation and spacing.","I generally did not care about such things, but when the other person showed me courtesy, I tended to respond in kind.","At least halfway.","Concern practically dripped from the Heavenly Demon’s comments.","How could such a warmhearted person possibly be the Heavenly Demon?","It made no sense.","Her manner of speaking also reminded me of my late grandmother, which made her feel even more familiar.","Leaning against the rock wall, I began browsing the gallery while resting.","└ Sword Master: If you have nothing else to do, would you be interested in learning swordsmanship? You seem to have talent.","└ Heavenly Demon: Silence! This lady shall personally bestow a secret manual upon him! How dare you interfere!","└ Sword Master: Come on, don’t be so strict. Do you use a sword as well, Heavenly Demon?","└ Wild Grylls: I need survival supplies more than swordsmanship right now...","└ Sword Master: That is true. I’ll give it some thought and return later.","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady shall descend the mountain at once. The items you requested will be delivered without fail.","That was enough gallery browsing for now.","I rose to my feet.","If I remained here too long, other beasts might be drawn by the smell of blood.","It had not exactly been a fierce battle, but the tension had drained a considerable amount of my strength.","It would be better to keep moving.","’I need somewhere to hide until the compass arrives...’","Rrrrrrrumble!","Without warning, the ground began to shake.","I blinked, then hurriedly sprang upright.","A natural disaster immediately after a beast attack?","What kind of absurd cosmic persecution was this?","But something was strange.","The moment I pulled my back away from the wall, the vibrations seemed to weaken.","Before I could identify the source of that unnatural sensation, the wall behind me began to change.","Grrrrrrind!","\"...Oh, dear God.\"","The wall was rising.","Literally.","The entire wall was lifting into the air.","A gigantic slab of rock tore itself from the ground like an uprooted tree.","It did not take me long to realize that the \"rock wall\" I had been leaning against was actually a leg.","I stared as what had appeared to be an ordinary rocky hill transformed into a two-legged giant.","Then I accessed the gallery.","└ Holy shit, isn’t that a Stone Guardian?","└ Why the fuck is a Guardian there? LMAO.","└ Isn’t that thing difficult even for a Sword Master to kill?","└ Dude, what are you doing? Run!","Everyone was screaming at me to flee.","I immediately turned and ran.","But I did not forget the bundle of food on the ground.","It was a gift from the Heavenly Demon.","I could never abandon it.","Title: What the Hell Is This Thing?","Wild Grylls","(A picture of an enormous stone giant towering above the forest.)","└ You get fifty thousand gold if you kill that thing, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: FUcKyOUiDoNtNeEdIt","└ He’s still browsing the gallery while running. ;;","└ Someone translate that.","└ Doesn’t it say, \"Fuck you, I don’t need it\"?","└ Seems right, lmao.","└ This lunatic, hahaha.","I barely managed to escape.","To catch my breath, I leaned against a tree.","I could still hear heavy thuds in the distance, but they were gradually fading.","It was not coming after me.","’This is driving me insane.’","The moment I overcame one crisis, another appeared.","What kind of ridiculous forest was this?","’This can’t actually be the Forest of Four Seasons, can it?’","I desperately hoped not.","After all, they had said the gallery could not be accessed from inside the Forest of Four Seasons.","I took several ragged breaths, then opened the gallery again.","The notifications had been ringing nonstop even while I ran, so I could not help checking.","└ Sword Master: Defeating that creature is simple. Cut off one of its legs and it will lose its balance. Then drive your sword into the core in its chest.","└ Why are you explaining it like a recipe for instant noodles? LMAO.","└ \"See? Easy, isn’t it?\"","[You Can Do It Too! Advanced Swordsmanship Lecture 15] — 2 hours ago","[You Can Do It Too! Advanced Swordsmanship Lecture 14] — 1 day ago","[You Can Do It Too! Advanced Swordsmanship Lecture 13] — 2 days ago","Sword Master was also surprisingly far from normal.","What exactly did this person do?","Just as I had with the Heavenly Demon, I searched through Sword Master’s posting history.","\"...\"","Oh, fuck.","They were obsessed with swords.","Every single post was a swordsmanship lecture.","They were insane in an entirely different way.","They had fewer posts than the Heavenly Demon, but unlike her endless stream of shitposts, every one of these was filled with effort and detail.","An unnecessarily diligent lunatic.","There was no better way to describe Sword Master.","Among all those posts, one stood out above the rest.","Title: Looking for a Life Partner","Sword Master","Requirement: Must be stronger than a Sword Master.","└ How hard do you hit?","└ Sword Master: Not telling.","There was not a single normal person in this gallery."]},{"title":"Chapter 4","paragraphs":["Crisis (1)","Why was the Messiah Empire called an \"empire\"?","There were several reasons, but the answer was simple.","It possessed the largest territory, the greatest wealth, and overwhelming military power.","Of those, military strength was inevitably influenced by the power of exceptional individuals.","And the Empire possessed a Sword Master.","What was a Sword Master?","A monster who stood at the pinnacle of swordsmanship and was regarded not merely as a tactical weapon, but as a strategic one.","Sword Masters were famous for splitting the earth with one strike and cleaving mountains with the next.","The existence of a Sword Master was precisely why other nations could not recklessly defy the Empire.","Title: Are Sword Masters Supposed to Be Rare?","I thought they were everywhere in the old days.","└ Yeah, they were back then.","└ Why aren’t they now?","└ Ash is gatekeeping the title. She says anyone weaker than her has no right to call themselves a Sword Master, lmao.","└ Fuck, is she the level cap? LMAO.","└ Hahahaha.","└ The Sword Saints of the past would only qualify as modern Sword Masters.","└ Are there no Sword Masters among races other than humans?","└ There are. They just all got wrecked by Ash.","└ Is she even human? LMAO.","At the age of fifteen, Ash made a declaration.","And everyone accepted it.","Anyone who desired both her beauty and her hand in marriage had only to defeat her.","After she became an adult, of course.","Three years passed.","She reached adulthood and waited with anticipation, but no man capable of defeating her appeared.","Five years passed.","She was approaching the ideal age for marriage and began growing anxious, but she patiently continued to wait.","Ten years passed.","Her family began begging her to marry someone.","That was when she first sensed that something had gone terribly wrong.","In truth, the rank of Sword Master was not exclusive to the Empire.","It was simply that the Empire’s Sword Master was the strongest.","Overwhelmingly so.","Ash Menethil, the Sword Master of the Empire, was renowned as the greatest swordswoman of the age.","She was famous not only for her strength, but also for her snow-white hair, blue eyes, and exceptional beauty.","Her looks had blossomed brilliantly from an early age, stealing the hearts of countless men.","Naturally, marriage proposals poured in even while she was still young.","\"I will marry a man stronger than me!\"","Title: ???: \"I’ll Marry a Man Stronger Than Me\"","Fifteen years had passed since then.","No man had managed to defeat her.","└ She’s become a total auntie now, lmao. Wait, someone’s knocking at my door.","└ Only a cold, lifeless comment remains.","└ What happens if you call Ash an auntie to her face?","└ Not sure, but apparently some brat heard her age and teased her by calling her one, lol.","└ Couldn’t an elf or demon take her?","└ There’s no one clearly stronger than Ash, lol.","└ Humans are surprisingly powerful, anyway. Their average is low as hell, but their peak is absurdly high.","└ Just how strong is she?","Fifteen years passed.","Her abilities continued to rise, yet still no man appeared who could defeat her.","She had undergone Bone and Marrow Cleansing and retained the beauty of a woman in her twenties, but her actual age was now in her thirties.","She had long since passed the usual age for marriage, so very few men dared approach her.","Of course, some men were captivated by her beauty and proposed anyway.","The problem was that every last one of them was weaker than Ash.","She did not want to abandon her final shred of pride and the conviction she had upheld for so long.","So she endured.","And endured.","Men also found women stronger than themselves intimidating, so they understood her position.","\"This can’t continue.\"","She could not simply wait forever.","Ash decided to personally train disciples.","She would raise promising candidates herself.","Surely, at least one of them would succeed.","Not a single one did.","They all lost to Ash and married other women.","People in this world generally married young, so they all ran off before reaching her level.","\"I’ll share all my knowledge with the gallery.\"","Feeling a growing sense of crisis, Ash began carefully uploading her swordsmanship expertise to the gallery.","She hoped to create a virtuous cycle.","It actually worked.","The general level of martial ability across the continent steadily rose.","At this rate, a man stronger than Ash would surely emerge from one kingdom or another.","Would that not cause international problems?","Her path to marriage was completely blocked.","International relations could go fuck themselves.","Yet even then, no man appeared who could defeat her.","Instead, mass-produced Sword Masters simply began appearing everywhere.","To make matters worse, Ash’s strength continued increasing even when she did nothing but breathe.","\"Why? Why is there no one? Why the hell?!\"","Ash could not understand it.","Why was there such a complete lack of talent?","She had tried everything imaginable, yet no man capable of defeating her emerged.","After examining the problem, she finally realized something far too late.","\"I get stronger just by breathing? Are you kidding me?!\"","That was right.","The woman praised as a heavenly genius was also a natural disaster in another sense.","Mana accumulated inside her simply through breathing, and she possessed the talent to channel it into her sword effortlessly.","Her obsession with marriage had distracted her, but had she trained consistently, she would have reached the rank of Grand Sword Master at a remarkably young age.","Yet Ash was already always included whenever people debated the strongest person on the continent.","She had no need to become any stronger.","\"Fuck my life.\"","Everything suddenly felt meaningless.","A crushing wave of emptiness washed over her.","In the end, Ash abandoned every one of her official positions and withdrew from public life.","The Emperor personally begged her to remain, but she rejected every request.","She did permit the Empire to continue using her name whenever necessary.","Still, a symbolic figurehead had value precisely because people could see her.","The fact that the Empire itself trembled at the mere possibility of losing Ash demonstrated once again just how great her presence was.","And so, after a total of twenty years had passed, the reclusive Ash was—","\"Hehehe.\"","—lying on her bed and eating a banana.","She giggled foolishly.","Her snow-white hair had been tied into a messy bun, and she wore the simple, comfortable clothes of a complete shut-in.","The round glasses on her face completed the image of an unemployed recluse.","These days, she spent her time diligently lurking on the gallery and enjoying her peaceful, if questionable, life.","Smack!","\"Ow!\"","\"You little brat! I told you to go outside!\"","A powerful slap landed on the back of Ash, who had been endlessly browsing the gallery.","Her body was as hard as forged iron, yet the blow stung strangely badly.","\"Look at your younger sister! She’s thirty and pregnant again! She’s about to have her fifth child—her fifth! You were even the captain of the Imperial Guard, so why aren’t you married?!\"","\"Ah, Mom...\"","Naturally, it hurt because the blow was filled with a mother’s love.","Ash rubbed her stinging back and looked at her mother.","Though her face was marked by many wrinkles, her features closely resembled Ash’s.","She must have been stunning in her youth.","Ash was already in her thirties, but her mother had given birth to her at nineteen.","For this era, that was perfectly normal.","\"What am I supposed to do when there isn’t a man I like...?\"","\"Lower your standards! Where in the world are you going to find a man stronger than you?!\"","\"...\"","Ash had no answer to her mother’s criticism.","It was, in fact, mostly correct.","Even among all races, Ash was exceptionally powerful.","She was stronger than elves and demons alike.","Of course, there was probably some man somewhere in the world who was stronger than her.","She simply had not found him.","\"My goodness, this mother’s heart is going to burst. What good is being a Sword Master or whatever if you’re still unmarried at thirty-five? I’m already in my mid-fifties, so please listen to me!\"","\"Well... my younger sister married well, didn’t she? Mom, we’re nobles now. Nobles.\"","Ash’s family had originally been commoners.","They rose in status when Ash became the greatest swordswoman on the continent.","The title she received was none other than countess.","Considering that marquises generally governed the borderlands, it was among the highest honors the Emperor could grant.","Her younger sister was also beautiful and had married well.","The fact that she already had five children made it obvious that she and her husband were very affectionate.","Unlike her older sister, she had found her perfect match.","Ash was jealous.","\"What good does that do when my eldest daughter is in this state? At least go outside and exercise!\"","\"I get stronger just by breathing...\"","\"Do you seriously expect me to believe that nonsense? Get out!\"","\"Yes, ma’am!\"","No matter how old a child became, they remained a child in their parent’s eyes.","At her mother’s shout, Ash hurriedly climbed out of bed.","She picked up a practice sword and headed toward the estate’s exit.","Then, after pretending she was going outside, she turned around.","Training was annoying.","Because she became stronger merely by breathing, she felt no need to do it.","’I should upload another post.’","She returned to her bed and accessed the gallery.","Her role there was simple.","Title: You Can Do It Too! Advanced Swordsmanship Lecture 15","Sword Master","Today’s advanced lesson is about parrying. What is parrying, you ask—","Uploading swordsmanship knowledge to the gallery had become part of her daily routine.","Originally, she had posted these lessons to raise the continent’s overall level of swordsmanship.","Now, it felt more like a job.","She had not always been so deeply immersed in the gallery.","In the past, she had merely lurked from time to time.","But after belatedly discovering the truth about her constitution and falling into despair over the feeling that the world itself had deceived her, she became completely addicted to it.","└ What do you think about quick-draw swordsmanship?","└ Sword Master: You should learn the fundamentals instead of wasting your time practicing that nonsense.","└ But it looks cool.","└ Sword Master: Do it after you become a Sword Master.","└ But Sword Masters are strong no matter what they do, lmao.","There were occasionally some complete idiots, but Ash always responded politely.","Why did she bother maintaining such decorum in a gallery where everyone openly displayed their desires?","’This is the only way to keep people from suspecting me.’","It was because of Ash’s usual personality.","She was rather rough and outspoken by nature.","That had allowed her to get along well with nobles despite being born a commoner, but none of that mattered here.","More importantly, she had been using the gallery for far too long.","Her activity was nothing compared to the truly hardcore gallery addicts, but she had still been around for years.","She was someone who had consistently used the gallery for a very long time.","She had even drawn suspicion when she first began uploading swordsmanship knowledge.","’I’d rather kill myself than die of embarrassment.’","There was always a chance someone might discover her identity, so she deliberately adopted a calm and refined manner of speech.","For the same reason, she never uploaded photographs or videos when posting swordsmanship lessons.","Fortunately, as a genius among geniuses, she seemed to possess considerable talent for writing as well.","Her explanations were so excellent that the lack of visual material caused no problems.","\"Ah. I want to get married.\"","Ash muttered while scratching her firm abdominal muscles.","Even though she had long since passed the usual age of marriage, she had not given up.","She was still willing to accept a challenger.","The Empire simply rejected them on her behalf because she was living in seclusion.","Since the gallery served as her main window into the outside world, she remained completely unaware of that fact.","\"Could this one be strong?\"","When browsing the gallery, she occasionally encountered people who showed promise or boasted about their strength.","She had wanted to meet some of them personally, but their lack of ability was usually exposed before long.","└ Fuck, how are you supposed to dodge that? Are you joking?","└ Sword Master: Why would you be unable to dodge it? Flexibility is essential. To think you do not even understand that. You were nothing but a loudmouthed insect.","└ Damn, she went straight for the throat, lmao.","It usually went something like that.","Most of them had theories that were complete garbage.","Others simply lacked knowledge.","Still, not everyone was an idiot.","There was one famous user who had caught Ash’s attention.","’Just how strong is this Heavenly Demon?’","Heavenly Demon constantly produced posts that were no better than excrement.","The users treated her like any other eccentric gallery addict.","Ash had initially done the same.","However, some of Heavenly Demon’s occasional remarks were deeply connected to martial arts.","Others scoffed at them, but Ash did not.","In fact, she hated Heavenly Demon several times more than everyone else did.","’That bastard made me even stronger...’","A genius recognized another genius.","Heavenly Demon’s posts had influenced Ash considerably.","It was almost like having enlightenment forcibly injected into her.","Every time Ash read one of Heavenly Demon’s posts, the mana within her visibly increased.","It did not happen only once or twice.","At first, she dismissed it as a coincidence.","But after experiencing it several times, she realized the truth.","That Heavenly Demon bastard was carelessly scattering her own enlightenment everywhere.","The amusing part was that most users failed to recognize its true value.","’Judging by the way she talks, she’s definitely a woman...’","Had Heavenly Demon been a man, Ash would have found him by any means necessary.","Someone capable of reaching such profound insights had to possess extraordinary strength.","However, Heavenly Demon constantly referred to herself as \"this lady,\" and everything about her speech suggested she was female.","An elderly woman, at that.","One thing was certain.","She was older than Ash.","’...Not that I’m in any position to say that.’","Ash also freely distributed her swordsmanship knowledge through the gallery.","Swordsmanship was traditionally highly secretive.","Yet because she spread techniques that anyone could learn, everyone’s abilities began rising.","The nation that benefited most was the Iris Kingdom, the Empire’s eternal rival.","Originally, the Iris Kingdom was a country where mages were stronger than knights.","Thanks to Ash’s trolling, however, its knights had now caught up to the continental average.","\"Bring me this user called Sword Master at once!\"","\"Your Majesty, it is impossible to identify the personal information of gallery users.\"","\"Y-You... You...! Urgh! Ugh!\"","\"Y-Your Majesty!\"","Naturally, the Emperor of the Empire had erupted in fury.","But there was no way to capture an anonymous gallery user.","It was one of the reasons Ash had resigned as captain of the Imperial Guard.","How could she continue serving while enduring that level of awkwardness?","If the Empire encountered a problem, the Emperor had to come and find her personally.","From Ash’s perspective, this allowed her to enjoy a comfortable life.","Title: The Heavenly Demon Is a God","Wild Grylls","(A picture of dead dogs lying on the ground and a hand tightly gripping a sword.)","And this sword is invincible.","\"Hmm?\"","Ash was diligently browsing the gallery while avoiding her mother’s eyes when a registered user caught her attention.","It was the person who claimed to have suddenly awakened in a forest.","At first, she had assumed it was another ordinary shitpost.","Then he found some herb called the New Moon Spirit Herb, and the entire gallery erupted into chaos.","That was when she began taking a slight interest in him.","She wondered what kind of person he was.","’Is the New Moon Spirit Herb really that valuable?’","For the record, Ash knew nothing about it.","Her body had no need for medicinal elixirs.","Later, he encountered Mad Dogs as large as cattle.","She had wondered how things would end, only for him to kill two of them.","’Those cuts... are incredibly clean.’","Ash looked surprised.","Interest glimmered in her blue eyes behind her round glasses.","Even from the photograph, the severed surfaces were extraordinarily smooth.","No matter how good the weapon was, most people could not even cut tofu in a perfectly straight line.","There had been no wavering in his strike.","He claimed to be an ordinary person, which only made him more intriguing.","More importantly—","└ Sword Master: If you have nothing else to do, would you be interested in learning swordsmanship? You seem to possess talent.","└ Heavenly Demon: Silence! This lady shall personally pass down a secret manual to him! How dare you interfere!","Heavenly Demon was interested in him.","That Heavenly Demon, who was usually too busy posting garbage!","She fussed over him as though warning everyone not to touch something she had already claimed.","She failed to realize that her behavior only drew more attention.","’Would you look at that?’","Ash flashed a broad, healthy smile.","That reaction made her want to tease Heavenly Demon even more.","Heavenly Demon was famous for doing whatever she pleased without caring about anyone else.","And now she was reacting like this?","Ash wanted to provoke her even more.","It would also be useful to learn more about Wild Grylls.","Ash waited for him to upload another post.","Title: Found a Cave. Should I Go Inside?","Wild Grylls","(A picture showing the entrance of a dark cave.)","It’s getting dark, so I need somewhere to rest. Should I go in? What if there’s a bear?","└ You’d better pray it’s only a bear. It could be a dungeon, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: What comes out of a dungeon?","└ No idea, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: You bastard.","└ It’s basically a real-life loot box, lmao.","Ash had initially thought he was pretending, but it seemed he was genuinely surviving in the wilderness.","Adventurers who wandered the world occasionally posted on the gallery.","But none of them did so completely unequipped like Wild Grylls.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Since there are no torches, it probably isn’t a dungeon! Still, you should throw a rock inside just in case!","└ Wild Grylls: What if a monster comes out?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Then you fight it!","└ Wild Grylls: The head admin says anything she wants because she’s strong. ;; Fine, I’ll try it.","Five minutes passed.","Title: This Cave Belongs to Me Now","Wild Grylls","(A picture of the surprisingly comfortable cave interior and a thumbs-up.)","I can do whatever I want with it.","└ Was there nothing inside?","└ Wild Grylls: Nope. It’s a little damp, though.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Be careful! The owner may return later!","└ Wild Grylls: I’m tired, so I’m going to sleep for now.","Ash was not quite sure what to make of him.","If Wild Grylls needed something, she could give it to him then.","Afterward, he appeared to have genuinely fallen asleep, because he stopped posting.","Ash continued browsing the gallery.","Even though it was nighttime where Wild Grylls was, it was still daytime in the Empire.","She had plenty of energy left.","Eventually, the sun began to set, and evening arrived.","It seemed he had managed to secure a cave where he could stay for at least one day.","Ash chuckled.","There was something strangely entertaining about it.","After spending every day watching idiots upload meaningless posts, this felt refreshingly different.","Still, none of it would matter if he died.","Later, she should tell him to read the survival-related posts she had uploaded.","’What sorts of things would he need to survive?’","[Someone Help Me. Urgent.]","\"Hmm?\"","A new post from Wild Grylls appeared.","Even the title looked ominous.","Ash immediately opened the post at the top of the page.","What could possibly have happened?","\"Eek?\"","She could not help crying out in shock.","Title: Someone Help Me. Urgent.","(A picture of a right arm riddled with holes and bleeding heavily.)","(A picture of the Mad Dog leader from earlier lying dead with its head severed.)","Fuck, this bastard was inside the cave. I’m losing too much blood. Can anyone help?","Wild Grylls’s right arm had been mangled.","Severely.","It was not merely punctured.","The wounds were so deep that bone was visible.","At this point, excessive blood loss was a more immediate concern than infection.","└ Put a gore warning on this.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m about to fucking die, and that’s what you care about?","└ Not my problem, lol.","└ But isn’t this actually dangerous?","An emergency had occurred."]},{"title":"Chapter 5","paragraphs":["Crisis (2)","Contrary to the notice posted by the head administrator, the gallery had a few unspoken rules.","No matter how difficult someone’s circumstances were or how pitiful their story sounded, never help them carelessly.","Even if someone was injured, never rush to help them.","The reason these rules came into existence was very simple.","Title: F king Scammer Bastard**","(Photo of a sickly young girl lying in bed)","You all know this picture, right? It’s that registered user who said his daughter had an incurable disease and begged everyone to help him.","Turns out this bastard was abusing his own daughter and deliberately starving her. ;;","Then he claimed he had no money and begged for donations, so I supported him, only to get scammed.","└ That’s roughly what happened. Hang in there.","└ Wild Grylls) Thanks for the f**king exposition, asshole.","└ Why are you making such a big deal out of this?","└ Even a potion would have trouble healing wounds that bad, wouldn’t it? There’s also a risk of infection.","└ Wild Grylls) Then what should I do?","└ Cut it off.","└ That’s f**king extreme. Lmao.","\"F**k.\"","I understood their reasoning, but it was still a shitty rule. I spat out a curse.","You could say I had let my guard down. I had been so exhausted that I closed my eyes for just a moment, and this was what happened.","Fortunately, it had bitten my arm instead of my throat. I had used that opportunity to cut the beast’s head off with my sword.","’Should I just cut it off?’","I stared at my mangled right arm. It was riddled with puncture wounds and had also been badly torn apart.","That son of a bitch had bitten down on my arm and violently shaken its head. I had barely stopped it from ripping my arm off completely.","’I need to stop the bleeding.’","I looked around the cave. Since it had been used by wild dogs, there wasn’t much inside.","There were only bones that presumably belonged to other animals. I should have seen this coming after finding those.","’Should I sell the sword for now?’","I felt truly sorry toward the Heavenly Demon, but I was in a situation where I might have to sell the sword and use the money to obtain medicine.","My life was in immediate danger. The gallery didn’t seem willing to help me, either.","Identifying myself? Who would believe me if I said I came from another world? They would just treat me like a lunatic.","For now, making a trade was my best option. Suppressing the burning pain in my arm, I searched through the comments.","’Let’s find a registered user first. Who should I choose...?’","[SwordMaster has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","It happened while I was hesitating and dripping with cold sweat. A trade request suddenly appeared.","It came from the registered user who constantly gave bizarre advice and was also an industrious madman.","For a moment, I wondered why this person was helping me. Then another wave of pain surged through my right arm, and I hurriedly accepted.","[SwordMaster: You’re the person who injured their arm, right?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes.]","[SwordMaster: I’ll give you a potion. Apply it to the wound and you should be fine.]","[SwordMaster has registered an item for trade.]","[SwordMaster: You don’t have to give me anything in return, so hurry up and take it.]","A wingless angel was right here!","After a brief moment of emotion, I immediately completed the trade.","I closed the gallery and looked at the ground. Whenever a trade was completed, the item would usually appear on the floor.","’...What is this?’","I blinked.","Inside a small cylindrical glass bottle was a liquid that glowed golden.","At least it definitely wasn’t anything strange. It didn’t sparkle like starlight, for one thing.","Before I could even wonder what it was, I picked up the bottle.","With one arm ruined, even removing the cap was an ordeal.","Splash—","\"Aaaaaaargh...!\"","Even though I had taken a deep breath before pouring it on, it stung like hell. Tears instantly welled up in my eyes.","You might say that a grown man shouldn’t scream over something like this, but fuck, it hurt so badly I thought I was going to die.","It was roughly five times more painful than applying cauterizing medicine to a mouth ulcer. The injured area was much larger, too.","\"Ughhh... Oh, ooh?!\"","Still, its effectiveness was equal to or perhaps even greater than that medicine.","In other words, it healed quickly. The puncture wounds riddling my arm closed in an instant.","I hadn’t been able to completely wash away the blood, but I could clean it later.","\"Whoa...\"","I moved my restored right arm around in every direction. It had healed perfectly.","Not only had it recovered, but it even felt sturdier than before. I could only describe it as a miracle.","After a brief moment of amazement, I immediately connected to the gallery again.","Title: Is SwordMaster a God?","(Photo of an unharmed right arm)","(Photo of a glass bottle containing golden liquid)","Is SwordMaster a god? Is SwordMaster a god? Is SwordMaster a god? Is SwordMaster a god?","I would like to express my gratitude to Lord SwordMaster for granting me a new arm. By the way, what is this yellow liquid?","└ Oh? Your arm is completely healed? Lmao.","└ I was about to give you something too. Too bad.","└ Bullshit. Lmao.","└ What the hell did he give you to completely heal an arm that had been torn apart?","I stared at the golden liquid remaining in the bottle. About one-third of it was left. I had saved it just in case.","└ SwordMaster) It’s nothing special. I just received it as a gift from my boss, I guess? I have plenty at home.","└ Wild Grylls) So what’s it called?","└ SwordMaster) An elixir. Oh, and since there’s still a risk of infection, you should drink the rest.","└ Wild Grylls) Yes, sir!","Following SwordMaster’s advice, I drank everything that remained.","It had a strangely familiar taste, with a fizzy sensation like carbonation.","You know that orange-flavored medicine you used to drink whenever you got sick as a child? It tasted similar to that.","└ An elixir? You gave him an elixir?","└ Come on, don’t bullshit us. Why would you give him that?","└ An elixir really was the only solution, though.","└ Just how rich is this guy? He received that as a gift from his boss?","Good point. I was curious about that too.","The gallery’s reaction was strange. Everyone was losing their minds over it.","Puzzled, I posted another question.","└ Wild Grylls) I’m kind of an idiot, so is an elixir expensive?","└ Of course it’s expensive. ;;","└ Even the lowest-grade elixir costs about as much as one month of living expenses for an ordinary family.","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t know how much that is.","└ He really was an idiot.","└ Lmaoooo.","└ Wild Grylls) Excuse me, but is there anything I can do for you?","└ SwordMaster) Become strong and marry me.","└ Wild Grylls) Wha...?","└ Lmaoooo, look how flustered he is.","└ This bastard proposes to everyone who shows even the slightest potential. Lmao.","Ah, right.","SwordMaster wasn’t exactly a normal person either.","I suddenly felt strangely deflated.","At least I understood that elixirs were expensive. They weren’t all absurdly costly simply because they were called elixirs, though. Apparently, their value depended on the ingredients.","The better the ingredients were, the more intense the golden glow became, but I didn’t really understand any of that.","There was only one thing I knew for certain.","I owed SwordMaster my life.","He wanted to repay the favor somehow.","’I should be the one receiving help right now, not repaying anyone...’","Still, I should at least leave a comment. The least I could do was express my gratitude.","└ SwordMaster) I was kidding. Just read my posts from the beginning. They’ll help you.","└ I don’t know about anything else, but this guy’s posts are genuinely useful. Read them no matter what.","└ Seriously, they’re top-tier.","└ The Empire’s in tears. Lmao.","\"Are they really that good?\"","Since I still didn’t understand how this world worked, it didn’t really sink in.","Even so, I owed him a debt of gratitude, so it was only right to do as he asked. It would be rude not to.","Besides, the only weapon I had was a sword. If I wanted to make proper use of it, reading his posts was probably a good idea.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Ah...! It looks like everything got resolved while I was asleep! That’s a relief!","└ The sucker has arrived!","└ Oh, the sucker’s here.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) I’ll delete the post with your injury in a minute! It was way too gruesome!","Just as things had finally settled down, the head admin appeared. Everyone immediately started teasing them, calling them a sucker.","Wondering why they kept calling the admin that, I tilted my head. Another user quickly explained.","└ Grylls, whatever you do, don’t take advantage of the head admin.","└ Wild Grylls) Why? What happened?","└ They can’t say no whenever someone asks for help. They’ll agree to anything like a complete pushover.","└ Didn’t they once give away their entire fortune because of that?","└ Though, to be fair, their entire fortune was only ten gold. Lmao.","\"So they really are a pushover.\"","They were genuinely too kind. Now I understood.","Of course, that didn’t mean I was going to ask the head admin for anything.","Even if I did, I’d make it a fair trade. I had a conscience too.","’If I find any medicinal herbs later, I’ll give them to SwordMaster.’","For now, it was time to clean up.","I dragged away the dog’s corpse, which was still bleeding warmly.","The smell of blood might attract other beasts, so I also needed to block the cave entrance.","’I’ll stay here until the Heavenly Demon comes back with the rest.’","After carrying the corpse a fair distance away, I gathered nearby rocks and sealed the entrance.","Once I finished cleaning up, I opened my bundle of provisions.","It was the same food I’d eaten before going to sleep.","\"No matter how I look at it, this thing looks exactly like a rice ball.\"","The size certainly matched one.","The taste didn’t.","I shoved the rice-ball-sized lump into my mouth and forced myself to chew while making the ugliest face imaginable.","Did the Heavenly Demon really consider this food?","The sharp aroma of medicinal herbs pierced my nose.","And the taste?","Absolutely awful.","Bitter beyond belief.","There wasn’t even the slightest hint of sweetness.","\"Well... at least it’s food.\"","I’d have to ask the Heavenly Demon later.","Just what the hell had he made this out of for it to taste this terrible?","Strangely enough, it didn’t make my throat feel dry.","It was simply unbelievably disgusting.","After finishing the entire thing, I leaned back against the cave wall.","Way too much had happened today.","\"At least now I know this isn’t a dream.\"","What had I possibly done to wake up in a place like this?","And what was this gallery, anyway?","The sudden wave of reality almost made me cry, but I held it back.","First, I needed to figure out what kind of world this was.","Which meant I had to log back into the gallery.","Right now, the gallery was the only thing I could rely on.","[A Ridiculously Hot Demi-Human Big Sister Photo] [Image]","\"...\"","That was the very first post waiting for me.","I froze.","Then, out of pure reflex, I looked around to make sure nobody was nearby.","Even though I already knew I was alone.","\"Hmm... it’s the top post, so...\"","After successfully convincing myself with some shameless mental gymnastics, I clicked on it.","\"GYAAAAAH!!!\"","I suffered severe internal damage.","***","Title: You Crazy Bastards","Wild Grylls","Where the hell did you freaks even get a picture like that? Are you all insane?!","└ Welcome. Lmaoooo.","└ Ah, another victim today.","└ So? Isn’t our dwarf big sister gorgeous? Give us your review.","└ Wild Grylls) Shut the hell up.","└ Isn’t this the registered user who posted earlier saying his arm was ruined?","└ His arm’s already healed and he’s back to work. Lmao.","└ Naturally. A man can’t skip his daily routine. Lmao.","└ Men truly live tragic lives.","As expected...","This gallery really was a gathering place for lunatics.","***","\"Looks like he’s fine after all.\"","Ash smiled as she watched Wild Grylls completely lose his mind after opening the post.","The elixir she had given him was one of the many gifts bestowed upon her by the Emperor.","She couldn’t even remember when she’d received it.","Besides, she had enough elixirs to practically trip over them.","If she ever ran out, she could simply ask the Emperor for more.","\"I wonder how the Heavenly Demon will react?\"","More than anything else, she was curious about his reaction.","The injury photo Wild Grylls had uploaded had already been deleted by the head admin.","From the Heavenly Demon’s perspective, the whole situation would be incredibly confusing.","’What on earth happened for Grylls to suddenly start praising me?’","That was probably what he’d be wondering.","\"An ordinary person? Don’t make me laugh.\"","Ash snorted.","Wild Grylls was far too skilled in a fight to be called ordinary.","If he had really been just a normal civilian, Mad Dog would have killed him without him putting up even the slightest resistance.","Instead, he had sacrificed one arm to launch a counterattack.","He had potential.","\"And he’s entertaining.\"","The more support she gave him, the more noticeably he grew.","That said, he wasn’t the type to simply accept handouts over and over again.","He always tried to repay what he’d received somehow.","It was... admirable.","Smiling with her trademark broad grin, Ash focused on the gallery once more.","Maybe Wild Grylls needed something.","Or perhaps he had another question.","Watching him had become a new source of amusement.","[Guys, I’m Screwed.] [0]","\"There it is!\"","What was he asking this time?","Ash immediately clicked on the post.","She had no idea what kind of disaster had happened now, but checking came first.","***","Title: Guys, I’m Screwed","Wild Grylls","I need to take a dump, but I don’t have any toilet paper.","I’m screwed.","└ Can’t you just use leaves?","└ Wild Grylls) I’m worried I’ll get a rash from poisonous plants. ;;","└ Then wipe with the monster you just killed. Skin it with your sword.","└ Wild Grylls) Oh! G-good idea.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) No! If you wipe yourself with Mad Dog hide, bacteria could infect you!","└ How does the mod even know that?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) U-Um...?","└ Wild Grylls) Then what the hell am I supposed to do?","Wild Grylls had encountered an entirely different kind of life-threatening crisis.","Just as he was about to sacrifice his pants...","\"He’s just as much of an idiot.\"","Ash couldn’t help letting out a laugh.","\"Should I wipe with my pants? It’s not like there’s anyone else here anyway. Dear God... please.\"","But for Wild Grylls, who had been dropped into the wilderness with nothing, this was a genuinely serious problem.","He couldn’t exactly relieve himself inside the cave.","Even if he did, cleaning it up afterward would be a nightmare.","Right now, collective wisdom was his only hope.","The situation was so urgent that he couldn’t even think straight.","└ PassingDwarf) I’ve got a pair of ripped underwear. Want it?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah, yeah! Hurry up and send it!","└ PassingDwarf) Just so you know, I’m a guy.","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t care! It’s an emergency, damn it!","└ This guy’s the real deal. Lmao.","└ PassingDwarf) You actually sound serious, so I just sent you some toilet paper instead.","└ Wild Grylls) Oh, thank God! Thank you so much!","└ Lmaoooo. What kind of religion is that?","└ Wild Grylls) Anyone who helps someone in an emergency is basically a god.","└ That’s the dumbest thing I’ve heard... but you’re not wrong.","Thanks to PassingDwarf’s toilet paper, the crisis was finally resolved.","It had been a ridiculous commotion, but the gallery users all came to realize one thing after witnessing Wild Grylls’ desperate situation.","└ Grylls really has absolutely nothing, huh? His life’s insanely chaotic.","└ At least he’s not like those scammer bastards.","└ Poor guy. Lmao.","At the very least...","Everyone now knew he wasn’t a scammer."]},{"title":"Chapter 6","paragraphs":["The Forest of Four Seasons (1)","Human Park Jong-hyeok.","He had overcome the greatest crisis of his life.","Thanks to PassingDwarf, I had managed to survive the emergency, but the problem still wasn’t completely resolved.","I had no idea what effect those Cocoa Puffs had on me, but my stomach kept hurting.","And it was definitely the kind of stomachache that meant I needed to take a dump.","’There’s no way the Heavenly Demon gave me something spoiled.’","It might have tasted bitter, but there had been no sour or rotten smell, so it definitely hadn’t gone bad.","My body probably just couldn’t handle it.","Besides, feces were nothing more than bodily waste, so it didn’t mean there was anything seriously wrong with me.","The real problem would be if nothing came out at all.","That would mean I hadn’t eaten anything.","It wasn’t diarrhea either, so there was no immediate danger of dehydration.","For now, I could dismiss it as a minor incident.","’I guess I should wait until the Heavenly Demon gives me the other supplies.’","I stored the toilet paper I had received from PassingDwarf in a corner.","Even the toilet paper was different from what I knew.","Its texture was somewhat rough, and it wasn’t very absorbent, so cleaning myself had been difficult.","Still, having some was far better than having none.","Toilet paper could be used for all kinds of things.","’More importantly, where the hell am I?’","I didn’t mean the forest.","I meant this world.","There was no internet, yet somehow the gallery existed.","It even floated in front of me like a status window, so I had countless questions.","After wondering what I should investigate first, I decided to begin with the structure of this world.","There seemed to be many different races, so it would be best to learn about them in advance.","’The races are roughly divided into humans, elves, dark elves, beastfolk, demons, and dwarves.’","There were four human nations, one nation where the races were evenly mixed, and one nation belonging to each of the remaining races.","There were also regions that weren’t recognized as proper nations.","Most of those were inhabited by humans.","I wondered why humans were the most numerous, but I could learn that gradually.","For now, obtaining basic common knowledge was more urgent than learning every detail.","That way, people wouldn’t treat me like a lunatic when I finally went outside.","***","Title: Listen Up, Knife-Ears","Fucking stop cutting down trees and planting new ones wherever you want. You’re only making things harder for the rest of us.","└ LetUsGrowTrees) Why? If there are more trees in the world, wouldn’t that mean more resources for everyone?","└ You bastards dig up all our trees and then plant your own.","└ Then you claim those trees belong to you and insist the land is yours too—","└ Average knife-ear behavior. Lmao.","└ LetUsGrowTrees) We don’t plant them indiscriminately. We only plant them on suitable land! It’s even depicted in the World Tree’s watermelon diagram.","└ Won’t someone kill this knife-ear bastard? Is persuasion impossible?","└ Nope. The Elf Queen is insane too, so there’s no reasoning with her.","└ Isn’t this going to cause an actual war eventually?","└ The Elf Queen may be insane, but she still has enough sense to know exactly how far she can push things. Lmao.","What surprised me was how elves were treated.","The elves I knew were a proud race that loved nature.","But judging by how the gallery viewed them...","They had practically been branded as the most hated race in the world.","***","Title: Typical Knife-Ears","In the past, they kept bragging about being superior until the other races beat the shit out of them.","After losing, they tried scheming behind everyone’s backs and got beaten again.","Now they secretly plant trees on other people’s land, get caught, and get beaten again.","Do these bastards have no ability to learn?","└ Watch your mouth. We once fought against the entire world.","└ And you lost to the humans, didn’t you? Want to lose again?","└ LetUsGrowTrees) We have no intention of fighting. We are a race that loves peace.","└ Bullshit. Then why do you throw tantrums over territory?","└ LetUsGrowTrees) Because those lands originally belonged to us elves. Isn’t it only natural that we reclaim them?","└ Hahaha. Lmao.","└ From their perspective, that actually makes sense. They’re a long-lived race.","└ For humans, it would probably be the equivalent of something that happened ten years ago.","└ The young ones these days... keep causing trouble... I am truly sorry...","└ Goodness, elder. You must be having a hard time.","└ I heard the Grand Council suffers because of the Elf Queen. Lmaoooo.","└ Shouldn’t it normally be the other way around?","└ The Queen is just that much of a lunatic. ;;","└ Ordinary madness is meaningless before true madness.","Hmm...","I decided to move on.","Even after leaving the forest, I should avoid getting involved with elves whenever possible.","The registered user named LetUsGrowTrees appeared frequently in posts related to elves.","Judging by how many people recognized them, they seemed to be a famous user like the Heavenly Demon or SwordMaster.","However, because they had accumulated so much dislike, they rarely received a positive response.","’That should be enough for now. Should I check the swordsmanship posts?’","Since survival was my priority, I should only spend a little time studying common knowledge.","However, I couldn’t wander around recklessly before obtaining a compass either.","I opened the post written by SwordMaster.","It was the introductory section on basic swordsmanship.","***","Title: You Can Do It Too! Basic Swordsmanship Lecture 1","SwordMaster","Before getting to the main point, anyone who still doesn’t know how to fight properly should carry a shield along with their sword.","I recommend learning how to fight first before devoting yourself to swordsmanship.","You think a shield looks uncool?","Keep acting recklessly and you might end up dying a stupid death.","Right now, you’re a pathetic weakling who doesn’t know anything, so shut up and carry a shield.","Also, anyone who cannot use mana should first learn a mana cultivation method.","***","One good thing about the gallery was that I could use it to tell the time.","Since new posts constantly appeared, it was easy to estimate how much time had passed.","There were simply far too many of them.","Even while posts came flooding in like a tidal wave, it was strange that my own posts never seemed to get buried.","Everything was fine, except for one problem.","How the hell was I supposed to learn a mana cultivation method?","I blinked.","I already knew that mana existed in this world and that people could become stronger through it.","But that was all.","I had no idea where I could obtain a mana cultivation method.","’Even the popular posts are filled with nothing but weird garbage...’","I scratched my head.","The gallery was useful, but it was far too disorganized.","Other than popular posts, the auction house, and the marketplace, nothing was properly categorized.","It seemed I would have to find someone like SwordMaster and ask directly.","Searching through the gallery myself was far too inefficient.","’There are about thirty minutes left before I can trade with the Heavenly Demon again.’","***","Title: Does Anyone Know How Mana Cultivation Works?","Wild Grylls","’Maybe it’s because I’m a registered user?’","That thought occurred to me after posting the question.","Anonymous users vastly outnumbered registered users.","Registered users were an insignificant minority.","Then again, anonymity was important in a gallery.","By using a fixed username, they had already abandoned half of that anonymity.","If their true identity were ever exposed, they would instantly create enough embarrassing history to last a lifetime.","While I was distracted by those thoughts, an alert sounded.","Someone had left a comment.","I checked it immediately.","It was the Heavenly Demon.","└ Heavenly Demon) A mana cultivation method would be the same as an internal energy cultivation technique in the Central Plains, would it not?","└ Yeah, that’s right.","└ Heavenly Demon) In that case, this lady shall teach you.","└ How good is the mana cultivation method you know?","└ Heavenly Demon) It is a cultivation technique capable of shattering the heavens and making the earth tremble.","└ Lmaoooo. Look how grandiose that sounds.","└ This reeks of a scam. Lmao.","I wasn’t so sure.","At the very least, I didn’t think she was lying.","The reason was the sword.","Before coming here, the only sword I had ever held was a bamboo sword during kendo practice.","Even so, I could tell that the sword given to me by the Heavenly Demon was terrifyingly powerful.","There was a high chance that the Heavenly Demon was also a superhuman worthy of possessing such a weapon.","Ironically, that was precisely why I hesitated to learn from her.","└ Wild Grylls) I feel like I’m receiving too much from you already, so it’s okay.","└ Heavenly Demon) You are this lady’s benefactor and a fortuitous encounter. Please allow this lady to repay the favor.","└ Wild Grylls) I only need a compass and something to start a fire...","└ Heavenly Demon) That will not be nearly enough.","Now I felt even more guilty.","I had only found that Moonlight Spirit Herb or whatever it was by coincidence.","I hadn’t even known whether the Heavenly Demon had truly been in danger.","One coincidence had simply piled on top of another, so I couldn’t help hesitating.","’...No. What am I thinking in my current situation?’","I should accept her kindness as far as my conscience allowed.","Still, I shouldn’t take advantage of her generosity.","I had a conscience, and I planned to repay her however I could.","I typed an affirmative response.","└ Wild Grylls) All right. But please write it in a private post. It might attract unnecessary attention otherwise.","└ Heavenly Demon) Very well. First, assume the lotus position.","The lotus position?","I tilted my head.","I vaguely recognized it as a term that might appear in a martial arts novel.","That was the extent of my knowledge.","└ Wild Grylls) What’s the lotus position?","└ Heavenly Demon) ?","└ Lmaoooo. She’s flustered.","└ Isn’t this the first time we’ve ever seen that old fossil get confused? Lmao.","In the end, we decided that I would learn the mana cultivation method later.","Even the Heavenly Demon seemed too bewildered to continue.","I asked in the comments whether the lotus position was absolutely necessary for mana cultivation.","Most of the replies only made fun of me.","After a moment of confusion, I searched for it in the gallery.","Apparently, the posture was common enough that there were even photographs demonstrating it.","I opened a random post and tried to imitate the position.","I was supposed to place my feet on top of my thighs.","\"Aaaaaagh!\"","A girlish scream burst from my mouth.","I hurriedly tried to untangle my legs, but only twisted them further and nearly burst into tears.","It felt as though every joint in my legs was being wrenched out of place.","Collapsed on the ground, I trembled violently.","Was the lotus position truly mandatory?","I would have to ask the Heavenly Demon.","└ It’s just the standard procedure.","└ Wild Grylls) Standard procedure?","└ You do it even if you don’t know why. Lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;","└ Wild Grylls) Heavenly Demon, do I really have to sit in the lotus position? It hurts like hell. ;;","└ Heavenly Demon) Why would it hurt? This lady cannot understand.","└ It does hurt when you try it for the first time. Lmao.","└ Work on your flexibility, dude. Lmao.","Either way, it seemed I would have to practice the lotus position gradually.","Improving my flexibility in my current situation would be difficult.","Instead, I continued reading SwordMaster’s post.","Rather than wielding only a sword, I should use a shield as well.","The explanation was convincing, and it was well suited to my current circumstances, so I accepted the advice without much resistance.","’The problem is where I’m supposed to find a shield.’","Cutting down a tree and making one myself wasn’t necessarily a bad choice.","The sword was exceptionally sharp, after all.","However, with no immediate source of water, using my energy to cut down a tree would be inefficient.","’Oh, right. I should ask the Heavenly Demon whether she can give me water too. Asking for a shield would be shameless.’","At times like this, I wished the gallery had private one-on-one messages.","Apparently, the feature had once existed, but I didn’t know why it had been removed.","It was probably because users had formed cliques.","For now, I placed several of the bitter pellets on my palm.","I wanted to identify their purpose first.","└ So she really was an old fossil. Lmao.","It seemed I should speak to her more respectfully.","At the very least, she appeared to be older than me.","The Heavenly Demon herself didn’t seem particularly bothered, but there was no harm in earning her goodwill.","***","Title: Heavenly Demon, What Are These Things You Gave Me Earlier?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of several pellets resting on a palm)","Putting aside how terrible they taste, I hope this isn’t rude, but they haven’t gone bad, right?","└ Heavenly Demon) They are fasting pills. They are somewhat bitter, but they have not spoiled.","└ Wild Grylls) They’re way more than somewhat bitter.","└ Heavenly Demon) Hmm. They suited this lady’s palate.","└ Grandma taste buds. ;;","└ Excuse me, but how old are you?","└ Heavenly Demon) I do not know. Age is unimportant anyway, is it not?","└ Old people always answer like that.","└ Wild Grylls) How many of these should I eat each day?","└ Heavenly Demon) As far as this lady knows, one is normally consumed per meal.","\"Eh?\"","I had eaten an entire handful at once.","There wouldn’t be any side effects, would there?","└ Wild Grylls) I ate a lot of them... There aren’t any side effects, right?","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady shall ask and return.","└ Your dick is going to explode now. Lmao.","└ Boom. Lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) Don’t say things like that, even as a joke.","I was genuinely afraid it might happen.","My body had already begun to feel strangely energized.","You might think having more strength was a good thing, but the problem was that it was excessive.","My body felt hot enough for me to notice.","If I became sick in this situation, it would be disastrous.","I desperately prayed that nothing would happen.","After some time passed, the Heavenly Demon returned.","└ Heavenly Demon) I asked one of my close aides. There are no side effects. On the contrary, they are beneficial to the body. In particular, they are said to remove accumulated impurities.","└ Wild Grylls) Impurities?","└ Heavenly Demon) In ordinary people such as yourself, they are usually expelled as feces.","└ Wild Grylls) What about the sudden surge of strength?","└ Heavenly Demon) They possess effects similar to a medicinal elixir, so that is only natural.","What a relief.","So there was no chance of my Big Johnson exploding.","I breathed a sigh of relief and rubbed my chest. Apparently, the heat spreading through my body was also a sign that I was absorbing the energy.","The fasting pills were a type of emergency ration, but they were extremely suitable for my current situation.","’She said one was the minimum, so I’ll have to eat more if I want enough nutrients.’","Either way, I had no choice but to keep eating these horribly bitter pellets.","I wasn’t in any condition to hunt right now.","Even if I successfully hunted something, meat alone wouldn’t provide every nutrient I needed.","└ You expect us to believe those tiny pellets have effects comparable to an elixir? What a joke. Lmao.","└ Heavenly Demon) They were specially made for this lady’s training, so that is only natural.","└ Then make one for me too.","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady shall make you a strangely shaped fasting pill. 凸","Considering the sword and the quality of the food she ate, the Heavenly Demon was clearly someone of high status.","Then why was someone like her using the gallery?","Well, regardless of the reason, she had helped me enormously.","Without her, I would probably have died already.","While browsing the gallery, a good idea suddenly occurred to me, so I posted another question.","***","Title: How Much Is a Mad Dog Corpse Worth?","Wild Grylls","Could I buy at least one crappy shield with it?","└ You could probably get a used shield.","└ Wild Grylls) A new one would be too much, right?","└ Yeah. Mad Dog hide isn’t particularly valuable.","└ Wild Grylls) Roughly how much is it worth? I want to trade it for something.","└ Just put it up at the auction house.","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t need money. It’s annoying to carry around.","└ Ah, right. You’re a newbie. You don’t need to carry it. Items can be stored directly inside the gallery.","Still, considering the gallery had saved one person’s life and allowed them to form a valuable connection, the flaws were understandable.","Besides, because of the terrifying transaction fees, plenty of users preferred direct trades over the auction house.","Stored inside the gallery?","After reading the reply, I investigated the system in more detail.","Apparently, users could deposit physical currency directly into the gallery, and it would be categorized according to each nation’s currency.","Exchange rates were applied automatically.","The greatest drawback, however, was the transaction fee.","The fees were far more brutal than those of an ordinary auction house, so the system wasn’t entirely convenient.","Nevertheless, its overwhelming advantage was that it completely ignored normal distribution and transportation.","That was why so many people used it.","’Wait. Then I could’ve just listed the Moonlight Spirit Herb in the auction house?’","This was why information was important.","└ Wild Grylls) Then where do all the transaction fees go? To the head admin?","└ Yeah. The auction house and everything else are managed by the head admin. But for some reason, the head admin is always broke.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) The fees are donated to the underprivileged or used to improve the gallery!","The head admin, who had remained silent until then, suddenly appeared.","Their answer practically radiated kindness.","└ Head admin... I’m underprivileged too... Could you give me ten thousand gold...?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Ah...! I don’t have any money right now...!","└ Don’t fucking give it to him.","└ This is exactly why we need a deputy admin. Why won’t the mod appoint one?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) It’s better if I handle all the difficult work myself! Deputy admins don’t get paid!","Just how many times had the head admin been stabbed in the back for even the anonymous users to stop them?","Most replies to the anonymous user pretending to be poor warned the head admin not to give them anything, even as a joke.","It was clear that public opinion toward the head admin was extremely positive.","More importantly, how was a head admin chosen in the first place?","’I can figure that out later.’","For now, I needed to put the Mad Dog corpse up for auction.","I left the cave.","I had dumped the corpse a considerable distance away.","Since I had memorized the route, there shouldn’t have been any problems.","\"Chomp. Chomp. Munch, munch.\"","\"...\"","\"Crunch! Crack!\"","Correction.","There was a problem.","Something was enjoying the Mad Dog corpse as though it were filming a gourmet eating show.","A bear.","No, an owl.","Its face clearly belonged to an owl, but its body was larger than a bear’s.","I hurriedly took a picture and uploaded it.","***","Title: What the Hell Is This Thing?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of something happily devouring the Mad Dog corpse)","I came back to retrieve the Mad Dog’s corpse, but this fat bastard is eating it.","Does anyone know what this thing is?","└ Fuck, that’s an owlbear.","└ Forget that it’s an owlbear. Why is it so huge?","└ Fucking hell. That house is walking around. Lmaoooo.","└ One hit from those claws and you’re dead.","So that was an owlbear.","The moment I learned what it was, I slowly began backing away.","Was this what people meant by doing all the work only for someone else to reap the reward?","At least I had survived, so I supposed I should be grateful.","’Fuck. I need to get out of here quickly.’","Wild dogs were one thing.","A bear was something else entirely.","And its size was absurd.","I slowly retreated until I had put enough distance between us, then sprinted back toward the cave.","What would have happened if I had arrived a little earlier?","Just imagining it made my blood run cold.","’What should I do? Should I defend myself from inside the cave?’","Unknown dangers lurked outside, but remaining inside the cave was also frightening because of the owlbear.","I had barely escaped the greatest crisis of my life, only for another one to appear.","The only thing I could rely on was the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","[The Heavenly Demon has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","While I was trembling with anxiety, the Heavenly Demon sent me a trade request.","Considering the time, it made sense.","I hurriedly accepted her proposal.","At the same time, the familiar empty trade window appeared.","[The Heavenly Demon has registered items for trade.]","[Heavenly Demon: These are the compass and ignition stone you requested. The ignition stone can be recharged using internal energy.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. But I don’t know how to use internal energy. Do you have anything else?]","[Heavenly Demon: Hmm? If you cannot use internal energy, how are you accessing the gallery? The matter of the lotus position was strange as well.]","Judging by what she said, one apparently needed to know how to use internal energy—or mana—to access the gallery.","I couldn’t explain it properly either.","The moment I opened my eyes in this world, all kinds of bizarre phenomena had simply started happening.","Explaining every detail would be difficult, so I answered as briefly as possible.","[Wild Grylls: It’s difficult to explain my circumstances in detail. I’m also short on time.]","[Heavenly Demon: Hmm. Very well. In any case, pressing the button on the ignition stone will produce a flame, so you should still be able to use it. Do you require anything else?]","[Wild Grylls: I’m sorry to ask, but could you give me a little water as well...?]","[Heavenly Demon: If it is your request, then gladly.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh! Thank you!]","I thanked the Heavenly Demon and accepted the trade items.","The relief supplies appeared on the ground.","There was a compass, an ignition stone, and a large water bottle.","Every item had a distinctly Eastern design.","I examined the ignition stone first.","\"The button is... here.\"","Whoosh!","When I pressed it, a small flame appeared along its edge.","This was more than enough.","Next came the compass.","With a compass, escaping the forest would become much easier.","The reason people became lost in forests was because they couldn’t maintain a sense of direction.","With this one item, everything would be—","\"Huh?\"","Before I could finish the thought, confusion escaped my mouth.","My eyes widened.","A compass needle should normally settle in one fixed direction.","This one didn’t.","It spun around and around without stopping.","Had the Heavenly Demon given me a broken compass?","Slightly flustered, I posted on the gallery.","***","Title: Heavenly Demon, I Think the Compass Is Broken","Wild Grylls","(Video of a compass needle spinning helplessly after losing all sense of direction)","The needle keeps spinning around. Why is it doing this...?","I think you gave me a broken one.","└ Heavenly Demon) Hmm? That should not be possible. It was functioning properly when this lady sent it.","Why had a perfectly functional compass suddenly started behaving like this?","This only made my situation more difficult.","└ Maybe something went wrong during the trade?","└ No, that probably isn’t it. Trading works more like teleportation.","└ Compasses don’t normally break without warning.","└ It’s spinning pretty well.","└ Just like your life?","└ Lmao.","The other users were equally confused.","Why would a compass that had been working perfectly suddenly behave like that?","Of course, it was possible that an unlikely coincidence had caused it to break immediately after the trade.","I needed another one to confirm it.","└ Wild Grylls) Can someone lend me a compass? I’ll return it as soon as the trade cooldown ends.","└ StarlightPrincess) I’ll give you one.","└ SpeargirlPrincess) I’ll give you one too!","└ PraiseTheSun) Me too.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) I’d like to give you one as well, but I’m sad to say I don’t have any.","Perhaps they sensed that something unusual was happening.","Several registered users who rarely commented appeared all at once.","It seemed I had captured their interest in only a short time.","The Moonlight Spirit Herb had probably played a large role in that.","Thanks to them, I obtained compasses of all kinds.","They were surprisingly varied.","***","Title: Fuck, They’re All Doing the Same Thing","Wild Grylls","(Video of several compass needles spinning in circles)","They’ve all completely lost their sense of direction like a bunch of outsiders.","Why the hell is this happening?","└ Heavenly Demon) How strange.","└ SwordMaster) That is strange.","└ SpeargirlPrincess) That’s strange.","└ PassingDwarf) What’s wrong with those things? Did you pour alcohol on the compasses?","└ Wild Grylls) Fuck off.","└ There is exactly one situation where something like this can happen.","└ What is it?","└ When you enter the Forest of Four Seasons. I heard both magnetism and mana are distorted there, so compasses don’t work.","└ Bullshit. If that were true, he wouldn’t be able to access the gallery either.","└ Still, the Forest of Four Seasons is the only explanation, isn’t it?","└ There’s no way every compass suddenly broke.","└ Where the hell is the original poster? Lmaoooo.","└ Got drunk and wandered into the Forest of Four Seasons. Lmaoooo.","Every compass behaved exactly the same way.","They all spun endlessly.","While everyone was trying to understand what was happening, several users began exchanging theories in the comments.","None of them sounded entirely certain.","There were two main possibilities.","The compasses were malfunctioning because I was inside the Forest of Four Seasons.","Or that was impossible, because entering the Forest of Four Seasons should have made it impossible to access the gallery.","Either way, my feelings could be summarized in a single thought.","’...I think I might be completely fucked.’","The situation was taking a very strange turn."]},{"title":"Chapter 7","paragraphs":["The Forest of Four Seasons (2)","Title: Who’s the Highest-Ranking God in This World?","Wild Grylls","└ Why do you ask?","└ Wild Grylls) So I can curse them out.","└ He just openly declared his intent to commit blasphemy. Lmao.","└ So that’s why you were dropped into the Forest of Four Seasons. Lmaoooo.","└ You’re being punished. Lmao.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Blasphemy is bad!","It felt as though the hope I had barely managed to cling to was collapsing before my eyes.","I folded my arms and stared down at the ground.","The compasses I had received from the registered users were lined up there.","Every single needle spun around and around as if they were broken.","└ At least he’s not a scammer. He’s just a little mentally unstable.","There was no way all of them had broken at once.","The problem was most likely the place I was currently in.","’Am I really inside the Forest of Four Seasons?’","I raised my head and checked the gallery.","Word must have spread because nearly every post was about me.","Many users claimed this phenomenon would be impossible anywhere other than the Forest of Four Seasons.","However, just as many argued that I shouldn’t be able to access the gallery if I were truly there.","***","Title: What If Wild Grylls Faked Everything?","Did this bastard deliberately break all the compasses?","└ It’s \"deliberately,\" not \"on purposefully.\"","└ If he faked it, every one of his posts has been way too intense.","└ First there was a Mad Dog, then a Guardian, and then an owlbear.","└ Look at that lineup. Lmaoooo.","└ Even the owlbear was fucking enormous. There’s no way this was staged.","└ The Moonlight Spirit Herb seems real too. Look at the post the Heavenly Demon made.","I wished it were fake too.","A sigh escaped me in frustration.","Just like the compass needles spinning in circles, my thoughts felt as though they were doing the same.","In other words, I felt like I was going insane.","I had no idea what the hell I was supposed to do now.","’Still, there’s some hope left.’","It hadn’t been confirmed that this was the Forest of Four Seasons.","The world was vast, and there were probably many regions that had yet to be fully explored.","This could be one of those places.","Everyone described the Forest of Four Seasons as an utterly inhospitable realm beyond human limits.","As someone who had always lived under the protection of civilization, I needed to escape somehow.","Doing something was better than sitting still and doing nothing.","***","Title: Can Someone Tell Me the Characteristics of the Forest of Four Seasons?","Wild Grylls","└ Why do you want to know?","└ Wild Grylls) I want to check whether I’m really there.","└ It has spring, summer, autumn, and winter weather all at once.","└ More precisely, it contains every kind of climate. I heard there’s even a desert.","└ Wild Grylls) Why the fuck is there a desert inside a forest? You said it was a forest.","└ We don’t know either.","└ For reference, the Forest of Four Seasons is about the size of a small country.","└ Wild Grylls) That information is fucking useless.","└ I said it was just for reference. Lmao.","What kind of ridiculous forest was this?","For now, confirming my location came first.","Going outside was dangerous, but with the compasses useless, staying still wouldn’t accomplish anything.","It would be best to use the cave as a base and gradually expand the range of my exploration.","’I’ll need paper and a pen too.’","I intended to draw a rough map.","Even if the compass was useless, having a map would still be better than having nothing.","I could get lost halfway through and fail to find my way back.","I needed to prepare for the worst.","’I’ll do everything I can.’","I had heard that the most important thing in a survival situation was the will to live.","There were probably more cases where people gave in to despair, did nothing, and truly ended up with nothing.","Danger was everywhere, but I would have to accept some risk.","I turned and looked toward a corner of the cave.","’There probably isn’t anywhere safer than this cave right now...’","Since there was a good chance I would have to remain in this forest for several days, finding water took priority over escaping.","A person could survive for three weeks without food, but without water, they would die in three days.","Even though I could receive help through the gallery, I intended to handle whatever I could by myself.","’There might come a time when no one can help me during a real emergency.’","I had realized that after being bitten by the Mad Dog.","That time, I had safely overcome the crisis thanks to SwordMaster’s kindness.","There was no guarantee something similar wouldn’t happen again.","In fact, it was highly likely.","If I couldn’t receive help during a life-or-death moment, I would die.","’That means I need to become friendly with the registered users...’","I had no idea what any of them actually did.","I reviewed the few registered users I had formed some connection with.","The Heavenly Demon was clearly someone important.","SwordMaster was rich and a master swordsman.","PassingDwarf was a dwarf.","That was all I knew for now.","I had no idea who the registered users who gave me compasses were.","’StarlightPrincess seems like a sick person.’","I meant physically sick, not mentally.","That wasn’t what I was implying.","Since people prayed for her recovery every day, she was probably suffering from some illness.","Perhaps she had a chronic disease.","As for the others...","I couldn’t tell from their posts.","Everything was too chaotic to reach any firm conclusions.","***","Here’s My Asshole","└ Lmaoooo. Did Speargirl lose again today?","└ SpeargirlPrincess) Those motherless bitches conceded two goals in stoppage time. Haha.","└ No wonder all the lunatics started appearing.","***","Title: Asshole Reveal","SpeargirlPrincess","(Photo of an emblem bearing a deer pattern)","Or maybe not.","I made an uncomfortable expression at the outrageously explicit title.","This SpeargirlPrincess person was definitely obsessed with sports.","Among all her posts, most were related to sports.","[I want to cry. Why am I a Speargirl fan?]","[These fucking bastards. They conceded in the dumbest way possible.]","[As expected of Evers!! I knew I could trust you!]","[This is seriously fucking awful. You call that a team?]","[LiverMidTable! LiverMidTable! LiverMidTable!]","A very familiar scent drifted through this unfamiliar gallery.","Most sports had a tendency to cause mental illness.","It was a taste I knew well.","I had once been deeply addicted to both soccer and baseball, only to develop stress-induced hair loss.","After that, I attained enlightenment and recovered.","’To become friendly with this person...’","That would probably be difficult for now.","It might have been possible on Earth, but here, I didn’t even know what kinds of sports existed.","For now, I stopped investigating the personalities of the registered users.","I needed to explore the surroundings before sunset.","Holding the Heavenly Demon’s sword, I placed several fasting pills into my mouth.","The moment I bit down, bitterness spread across my tongue.","I quickly took a sip of water to wash away the taste.","I had no idea how long I would have to keep eating these things.","’All right. I’m ready.’","Before leaving the cave, I posted one more message.","I also remembered to put a handful of fasting pills into my trouser pocket, just in case.","***","Title: Preparations Complete","Wild Grylls","(Photo showing the cave entrance)","I’m going to explore and check whether this is really the Forest of Four Seasons.","└ Isn’t that too dangerous?","└ You ran into an owlbear earlier. ;;","└ The compasses are acting strangely, so exploring is probably the right choice.","└ Heavenly Demon) Be careful.","└ SwordMaster) Good luck.","└ PassingDwarf) You should’ve waited a little longer. I was going to give you a used shield.","└ Wild Grylls) Later. I’m planning to run immediately if anything dangerous happens anyway.","└ The next day, Grylls never posted again.","└ T_T","└ Wild Grylls) Fuck off.","Everyone seemed to be cheering me on.","Of course, most of those encouraging me were registered users.","The others were closer to saying, \"Why should I care?\"","A few comments went far beyond the line, but they were deleted shortly afterward.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Severe insults and abuse directed at someone working hard to survive will result in a ban!","└ Wild Grylls) Thank you. ;;","I wasn’t sure whether this counted as working hard to live.","I had only ended up here by accident.","In any case, I had now uploaded what could potentially be my final post.","Taking a deep breath, I stepped outside the cave.","The familiar scenery greeted me.","It was a warm forest.","’At least the weather being warm is one good thing among all this misfortune.’","If it had been cold, the difficulty would have increased even further.","I looked around and began walking.","I headed in the opposite direction from where the owlbear had been eating the Mad Dog’s corpse.","To avoid getting lost, I used the sword to leave marks along the way.","’Focus on the sounds.’","The chirping of insects.","The rustling of bushes in the wind.","The distant roars of animals.","I concentrated on my hearing so I wouldn’t miss a single sound.","My heart pounded from tension.","This was an environment where a single moment of carelessness could decide whether I lived or died.","The sword was the only thing I could trust.","Rustle—","An ominous sound reached my ears, which had become hypersensitive from tension.","It came from directly above me.","I immediately snapped my head upward.","There was no time to raise it slowly.","\"HSSSSSSS!\"","A gigantic snake lunged at me with its jaws stretched wide open.","Its long, sharply protruding venomous fangs looked terrifying.","I didn’t even have time to scream.","I hurriedly twisted my face aside.","The snake’s jaws barely grazed past me.","Without wasting another moment, I swung the sword down at the snake’s body.","Thud!","\"What...?\"","Something completely unexpected happened.","This was the Heavenly Demon’s sword—the same sword that had cleanly sliced the Mad Dog in half.","Yet the blade only sank halfway into the snake before becoming lodged.","Its scales were far tougher than I had imagined.","\"HSSSSSS!\"","The venomous snake thrashed wildly in pain.","At the same time, it opened its enormous jaws and lunged at me.","It was as large as an anaconda.","If it managed to bite me even once, I was finished.","I hurriedly tried to move my right hand, only to freeze.","Squeeze!","\"Ghk?!\"","The snake had already wrapped its body around my right arm.","When the hell had it done that?","I was startled only for a moment.","Just before it could bite me, I grabbed it by the neck.","Snake scales were normally smooth and unpleasant to touch, but this one was different.","It felt like gripping a solid sheet of iron.","Squeeeeeze!","\"Agh!\"","The pressure around my right arm intensified.","But my left hand wasn’t free either.","The moment I released the snake’s neck, it would obviously bite me.","Maintaining this position was my best option.","’What should I—ah!’","Something entered my field of vision amid the chaos.","The section of the snake’s body that had been cut halfway through.","It was between the part wrapped around my right arm and the snake’s head.","I immediately slammed both arms downward as if I were swinging a jump rope.","The half-severed section dropped beneath my feet.","Now it was time to use my strength.","Stomp!","\"Huaaaaaagh!\"","\"HSSSSSSS!\"","I planted my foot on the middle of its body and pulled as though I intended to tear the half-severed section apart completely.","The snake writhed in agony, shaking its head from side to side.","Venom sprayed dangerously from its fangs.","My right arm wasn’t faring any better.","The snake tightened its grip even further, as if determined to crush the bones completely.","It had become a game of chicken to see which of us would die first.","Then I encountered an unexpected obstacle.","’Fuck! Why are these scales so damn tough?!’","This was a snake that even the Heavenly Demon’s sword had failed to cut cleanly.","Of course it was tough.","Did that mean I intended to give up?","Absolutely not.","If I wanted to survive, I had to rip this bastard in half and kill it.","Riiip! Tear!","The result of our struggle gradually began to show.","Its body started splitting apart.","The cut made by the sword slowly widened.","I pulled with every ounce of strength I had.","Since I was using both my hands and my foot, I could exert far more force.","Riiip! Riiiiiip!","At last, the long and brutal struggle came to an end.","The snake’s body tore in half.","I felt the strength rapidly drain from the severed body now that it had lost the commands from its head.","I immediately shook my right arm free.","The section wrapped around my arm fell away, and I drove the sword downward at once.","Stab!","The Heavenly Demon’s sword pierced directly through the snake’s head.","Even with a blade embedded in its skull, the snake continued to writhe.","Breathing heavily, I collapsed onto the ground.","Just in case, I didn’t pull the sword out.","I had heard somewhere that snakes were bizarre animals capable of continuing to move even after only their heads remained.","Even now, despite the sword piercing through its skull and being driven deep into the ground, it continued twitching.","What a tenacious creature.","Throb! Throb!","\"Ow...\"","I looked down at my aching right arm.","The snake’s coils had left clear marks.","There was also heavy bruising beneath the skin.","Considering my bones had nearly been crushed, it was a relatively minor injury.","’What the hell are those scales made of for them to be this tough?’","Even the Heavenly Demon’s sword had barely penetrated them.","I uploaded pictures to the gallery.","I planned to rest for about thirty seconds before continuing onward.","I had lost far too much strength.","***","Title: Even the Snakes Are Fucking Huge Here","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the snake’s head)","(Photo of the snake’s body separated from its head)","I seriously thought I was going to die.","I freaked out when the sword didn’t cut through it in one strike. ;;","└ Whoa, that’s fucking disgusting. Is it venomous?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. It tried to kill me with its fangs at first, then wrapped itself around my right arm. I thought my bones were going to break.","└ You cut the Mad Dog in half, but couldn’t cut through some snake in one swing? How did you kill it?","└ Wild Grylls) I tore apart the section the sword had already cut. It was fucking tough, though.","└ Holy shit.","└ Doesn’t that look like a Steel-Scaled Serpent?","└ If it really is one, isn’t it insanely expensive?","└ Yeah. Both the venom and the scales should be valuable.","So this thing was called a Steel-Scaled Serpent.","It certainly lived up to its name.","I watched the comments descend into chaos again, then simply closed the gallery.","There was no point paying attention to them right now.","The snake was too large to drag back to the cave.","It would be better to list it directly in the auction house.","’I should learn from what happened with the Mad Dog.’","Without hesitation, I opened the auction house.","All kinds of items were listed there.","Occasionally, I saw strange things like an elf’s underwear or socks that hadn’t been washed for several days.","The world truly was vast, and there was no shortage of idiots and perverts.","I let out a hollow laugh.","Unlike direct trades, anyone could list items in the auction house.","That was probably why things like this appeared.","’The fee is... What the hell? Forty percent?’","So this was what people meant when they said the fees were murderous.","Even so, the auction house remained popular because of its advantage of completely bypassing transportation and distribution.","I placed my hand on the body rather than the head and registered it in the auction house.","The listing name was \"Snake I Just Killed,\" and the minimum bid was five gold.","I had been struggling with how to dispose of the corpse anyway, so I would benefit as long as someone bought it.","’At least the listing fee isn’t very high.’","The gallery had given me a small amount of money when I first created my registered account.","Thanks to that, I didn’t have to worry about being unable to afford the listing fee.","That was fortunate.","[Note: Fees may vary depending on the item’s weight.]","I didn’t care.","I completed the listing and stood up.","The snake’s body disappeared after being registered in the auction house.","Only the head remained.","The head was still moving, so I couldn’t list it.","The safest option was probably to cover it with dirt.","’This is difficult right from the start.’","Why did my life have to be so miserable?","Rubbing my still-throbbing arm, I continued onward.","I prayed that nothing else would happen.","Trickle, trickle—","Before long, I heard a sound that instantly sharpened my senses.","Running water.","Water was one of the most important resources for survival.","I hurried toward the sound.","I might be able to secure drinking water.","And if I followed the stream downstream, it might lead me out of the forest.","That was what I thought.","\"...What the hell is this?\"","At least, I would have thought so if there hadn’t been a desert on the other side of the stream.","I was more dumbfounded than alarmed.","No matter how many times I rubbed my eyes and looked again, it was unmistakably a desert.","A vast expanse of reddish sand stretched out before me.","I was clearly standing inside a forest.","So why was there a desert on the other side of a stream?","It felt as though every law of common sense was collapsing at once.","I stood there blankly for a while before opening the gallery.","***","Title: Guys, Let Me Show You Something Amazing","Wild Grylls","(Photo showing the stream and the forest)","Here we have a forest and a river!","(Photo showing a vast desert beyond the stream)","And beyond the river, we have a desert!","Think it’s fake?","(Video alternating between the forest, stream, and desert)","Wow, fuck!","Where do you think I am?","Aren’t. You. Just. Dying. To. Know?","└ Wow. That. Is. So. Amazing.","└ ??? You really were inside the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ Then how are you using the gallery?","└ Lmaoooo. This is seriously spectacular.","└ So it was real. Lmaoooo.","└ Heavenly Demon) What a beautiful place.","└ Wild Grylls) Ma’am?","└ The Heavenly Demon clearly has no idea what this place is. Lmaoooo.","└ Why does she sound like such an old person? Lmao.","└ PassingDwarf) Are you experiencing hallucinations?","└ Wild Grylls) I sobered up a long time ago. ;;","└ PassingDwarf) Drink again. Then you’ll sober up from this.","└ Fighting poison with poison. Lmao.","Not a single one of the comments was helpful.","I sighed in frustration.","\"Hah...\"","My current feelings could be summarized in a single word.","\"Fuck.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 8","paragraphs":["The Forest of Four Seasons (3)","The Continental Integrated Gallery could be accessed anytime and anywhere as long as certain conditions were met.","The first condition was that the mana in the atmosphere had to be stable.","If the atmospheric mana was unstable, accessing the gallery became difficult.","The second condition was that the user had to be capable of controlling mana at will.","This was connected to the next requirement.","The final condition was knowing the access formula.","The calculations were so simple that even a child could perform them.","Therefore, if the mana was unstable, the user couldn’t control mana, and they didn’t even know the access method, using the gallery should have been impossible.","***","Title: What If All of This Is Actually a Dream?","Wild Grylls","What if I’m actually dreaming?","Maybe the gallery and all of you are nothing more than parts of my dream.","I need to wake up soon. Lmao.","└ He’s finally lost his mind. Lmaoooo.","└ Hang in there, dude.","└ StarlightPrincess) Stay strong.","└ Damn, things must be bad if even that person is telling him to stay strong.","└ Bro, you should start over from day one of survival. Lmao.","└ SpeargirlPrincess) Are you really inside the Forest of Four Seasons? I still can’t believe it.","└ You have to believe it. There’s nowhere else like that except the Forest of Four Seasons.","└ SpeargirlPrincess) But he’s been using the gallery nonstop.","└ That’s what we’re wondering too. Lmao.","└ The common sense of this world is collapsing in real time.","└ All-Father) May I use you as research material?","└ Wild Grylls) What are you planning to do with it?","└ All-Father) I intend to write a paper.","└ Wild Grylls) Do whatever you want.","└ He’s given up. Lmaoooo.","Wild Grylls.","Every compass had malfunctioned, and now he had even provided undeniable proof that he was inside the Forest of Four Seasons.","Most of the evidence was impossible to dispute.","And yet, someone who ignored every condition required to access the gallery had appeared.","At first, everyone had assumed he was merely another ordinary registered user.","But as time passed, he gradually began attracting the gallery’s attention.","He had suddenly discovered a Moonlight Spirit Herb.","He had fought and defeated a Mad Dog.","He had even been bitten by another Mad Dog while sleeping—","***","Title: Isn’t There Something Strange About the Snake Grylls Uploaded?","Isn’t that thing actually a Steel-Scaled Serpent?","Aside from the fact that it’s fucking enormous, it looks exactly like one.","└ What’s a Steel-Scaled Serpent?","└ Exactly what the name says. It’s a snake with scales as hard as steel. Even a Sword Expert would barely be able to kill one.","└ Is it expensive?","└ If processed properly, it’s extremely useful. Think of it as fabric with the durability of iron.","└ Why is that Steel-Scaled Serpent so huge? It’s as big as an anaconda. ;;","└ How large are they normally?","└ About the size of an ordinary snake. That’s why they’re usually relatively easy to kill, but I don’t know about that monster.","└ How much would it be worth?","└ The minimum price would probably be around one hundred gold.","The snake Wild Grylls had listed in the auction house caused another major stir.","Unlike direct trading, the auction house was open to a much wider range of users.","Direct trades were restricted to registered users, but anyone could register items or place bids in the auction house.","One might ask whether that meant drugs and other dangerous goods could also be sold.","Fortunately, such trades rarely occurred, if only because of the murderous fees.","Even if someone attempted it, the head admin immediately issued a permanent ban and stopped the problem before it could spread.","└ Whoa, it passed five hundred gold.","└ What happens if it’s a scam?","└ Grylls listed it for only five gold and left, so he isn’t responsible for the bidding war.","└ Besides, who takes responsibility for something bought through an auction house? Lmao.","└ Considering the fees, he listed it absurdly cheaply.","Even while Wild Grylls was drowning in despair, the excitement surrounding the auction didn’t fade.","Since it used a bidding system rather than an instant-purchase option, it was only natural that countless users would flock to it.","The structure also encouraged fierce competition once the fees were taken into consideration.","└ Damn! It passed one thousand gold!","└ A sucker has appeared. Lmao.","└ Even that price is cheap, though. Assuming it’s genuine.","└ But is it really genuine?","└ If it turns out to be fake, people will probably go insane trying to hunt Grylls down. Lmao.","└ But Grylls is in the Forest of Four Seasons. Can anyone even catch him?","└ Good point. Lmaoooo.","└ Pleasure without responsibility. Lmao.","└ Doesn’t he have neither responsibility nor pleasure?","└ True. Lmaoooo.","└ Wild Grylls) Huh? What the hell? Why did it become so expensive? ;;","└ The man himself has appeared!","└ Grylls, is that really a Steel-Scaled Serpent?","└ Wild Grylls) How would I know? I listed it immediately because I was worried something else would eat it later.","└ Don’t tell me it was delivered straight from the wild.","└ Wild Grylls) It was still twitching until right before I put it in the auction house. Lmao.","└ Kyaaaaaaagh!","└ Gyaaaaaaagh!","From Wild Grylls’ perspective, he had only listed the snake because he wanted to dispose of it quickly.","The reaction left him bewildered.","More importantly, he couldn’t care less whether it was a Steel-Scaled Serpent or anything else.","How could he pay attention to the auction house when he didn’t even know how he was going to survive?","He felt like crying.","***","Title: Upvote If Grylls Makes You Want to Kill Yourself","I’ll start. Lmaoooo.","└ Wild Grylls) Upvoted. Lmaoooo.","└ Why is the original poster joining in? Lmaoooo.","└ I didn’t think he’d actually appear.","└ Grylls must be completely broken. Lmao.","Of course his mind was breaking.","Every hope he had of escaping had vanished.","Getting lost in an ordinary forest was already life-threatening.","This was the Forest of Four Seasons, a place described as a hellscape beyond human limits.","Compasses didn’t work, and even space itself was distorted.","His chances of survival were already extremely low.","***","Title: Where Is Grylls Originally From?","Now that I think about it, I’m curious.","What the hell did he do to end up inside the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ Wild Grylls) I’m originally from Earth. I drank alcohol, woke up, and found myself here.","└ Where is Earth? I’ve never heard of it.","└ Wild Grylls) Another world.","└ ...?","└ You didn’t enter the forest because you developed a mental illness, did you?","└ Another world. Lmaoooo.","└ Does that world have a gallery too?","└ Wild Grylls) It does. The galleries are more specialized, though.","└ Oh! Are you interested in becoming a deputy admin?","└ Wild Grylls) What’s a deputy admin? Do they do the same work as the head admin?","└ Yeah, except they have less authority and don’t get paid. Lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) Fuck no.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) I can handle all the difficult work by myself!","Perhaps his mind had truly snapped, because Wild Grylls answered every question with complete sincerity.","He began with the claim that he came from another world, then proceeded to talk about that world.","Of course, the gallery users didn’t seem to believe him.","They simply treated him like a lunatic.","└ SwordMaster) So that was your character concept. Understood.","└ Wild Grylls) It’s not a character concept. ;;","└ SwordMaster) Who would believe that a single bomb could destroy an entire city?","└ Wild Grylls) I find it harder to believe that a person can destroy a mountain.","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady is capable of doing so.","└ SpeargirlPrincess) I can do it too!","└ All-Father) I am also capable of it.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) I could do it if I really exerted myself!","└ Wild Grylls) Is everyone here a monster or something? ;;","└ PassingDwarf) What you said sounds interesting. Do you know how to make one?","└ Wild Grylls) How the hell would I know that?","└ PassingDwarf) Then what can you do?","└ Wild Grylls) Eat, shit, and laze around?","└ PassingDwarf) Then just die and become fertilizer.","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah... I guess I should...","└ PassingDwarf) Ah, fuck. Sorry. Don’t actually die. I’ll send you some alcohol later.","└ Look how he panicked when Grylls sounded like he might really kill himself. Lmaoooo.","Or they assumed it was simply an elaborate character act.","From their perspective, that was only natural.","The fact that Wild Grylls had fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons and the claim that he came from another world were separate matters.","It wasn’t especially important either.","The most important issue at the moment was the Steel-Scaled Serpent listed in the auction house.","└ How did you kill that? You said you were an ordinary person.","└ Wild Grylls) The sword couldn’t cut through it, so I just tore it apart.","└ And you call that an ordinary person?","└ He’s saying he tore through a steel plate with his bare hands. Lmaoooo.","└ Wild Grylls) No, it wasn’t that extreme. The sword had already cut partway through it, so I targeted that section. It was huge, but I could still grip its neck with one hand.","└ And then you ripped it apart in that state?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah.","└ Fuck, that still doesn’t make sense.","└ Are all ordinary people in your world like that?","No matter how anyone looked at it, his answer didn’t sound like something an ordinary person could do.","Still, it wasn’t entirely impossible.","People often displayed several times their normal strength when their lives were in danger.","The gallery users could accept it as something along those lines and move on.","└ The bidding stopped at eleven hundred gold. Looks like it’ll be sold soon.","└ How much time is left?","└ Ten minutes.","└ Grylls set the duration to six hours because he wanted to sell it quickly.","└ Wild Grylls) Huh? You could set the auction duration?","└ He didn’t know. Lmaoooo.","└ He must have been in a real hurry. Lmao.","└ Still, selling it quickly is better for Grylls.","└ Otherwise, something might eat it again like last time. Lmaoooo.","***","Title: Fuck, Fuck, Fuck. I Shouldn’t Have Bought This","(Video of a headless snake body violently twitching)","First of all, it really is a Steel-Scaled Serpent.","Did this thing seriously come straight from the source? Fuck.","└ Ugh... You should add a gore warning.","└ The twitching is kind of cute. Lmao.","└ ?","└ Sir?","└ Since it doesn’t have a head, it probably wasn’t delivered completely fresh. Lmaoooo.","└ It was just extremely fresh. Lmao.","└ If it had still been alive, the auction house wouldn’t have accepted it. Lmao.","The Steel-Scaled Serpent that had caused such an uproar was eventually sold for approximately eleven hundred gold.","It was an extraordinarily high price.","Even after accounting for the auction house’s murderous fees, Wild Grylls had earned a large amount of money in an instant.","The item had also been confirmed as genuine.","At the same time, the gallery’s trust in Wild Grylls increased.","He seemed to have something slightly wrong with his head, but he was honest.","That became the general opinion of him.","***","Title: Are There Any Survival Experts Here?","Wild Grylls","Title: Are There Any Survival Experts Here?","Wild Grylls","If there are, please give me some tips.","I want to live.","└ There used to be a lot of them, but there aren’t any these days.","└ Wild Grylls) Why?","└ They all died. Lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;","└ Several famous users entered the Forest of Four Seasons and then disappeared, right?","└ Yeah.","└ Grylls started inside it from the very beginning. Lmaoooo.","└ Hardcore mode from the start.","└ Wild Grylls) None of you bastards are helpful.","While Wild Grylls lamented through tear-filled eyes, another commotion was unfolding elsewhere.","It was the home of the being who had once shaken the entire Central Plains—the Heavenly Demon—and a paradise for those rejected by society.","The Demonic Cult.","Even the imperial family of the Central Plains watched it closely.","\"Heavenly One! You absolutely must not enter the Forest of Four Seasons!\"","\"This lady intends to rescue her benefactor. Why do you stand in her way? Do you truly wish to die?\"","The Heavenly Demon, Yu So-wol, threatened the man before her with an icy expression.","Her gaze alone carried enough force to make it seem as though she could tear a person apart.","That pressure was no mere illusion.","It affected the man before her considerably, making his insides feel not only overturned but tightly twisted.","He felt as though he might lose consciousness at any moment, yet he forced himself to endure and spoke.","\"That is not my intention. It is simply that the Forest of Four Seasons is a forbidden realm from which even the Heavenly One would struggle to escape.\"","\"Demonic Brain. You know well what realm this lady has reached.\"","\"Of course. You have transcended the principles of martial arts and earned the qualification to ascend.\"","He had noticed it the moment he faced her.","The Heavenly Demon, Yu So-wol, had entered a realm beyond all conventional standards.","Previously, she had been like the sun suspended high in the sky.","Now, she seemed to have become the sky itself.","Even before this breakthrough, Yu So-wol had stormed the imperial palace alone and taken the Emperor’s head.","Now that she had reached an even greater realm, no one could stop her.","\"However, the Forest of Four Seasons mentioned by the Heavenly One is nature itself, something that surpasses even the heavens. Every force of nature has converged there, transforming the entire region into a forbidden realm.\"","\"Explain it simply.\"","\"It would be easiest to think of the entire region as being filled with formations. Even if one breaks a formation, nature’s powerful regenerative force restores it almost immediately, and it returns in a different form.\"","Once someone entered the Forest of Four Seasons, they could never leave.","The Demonic Brain had just explained why.","The entire region was a barrier.","Even if one formation was destroyed, another formation with a different pattern appeared.","The forest itself was a living barrier.","No matter how many times it was broken through, it regenerated.","Therefore, no matter how powerful Yu So-wol had become, she would likely be unable to conquer the Forest of Four Seasons.","\"Can even your mind find no solution?\"","\"Regrettably, the reality is that this foolish mind of mine cannot comprehend something even the heavens themselves cannot read.\"","\"Hmm.\"","Yu So-wol withdrew her pressure and stopped threatening him.","If the Demonic Brain, the Demonic Cult’s greatest strategist, spoke so firmly, there truly was no current solution.","Forcing the issue would produce nothing.","Nor could she kill a trusted adviser over it.","It would be better to work the Demonic Brain to the bone until he found a way to conquer the Forest of Four Seasons.","\"Very well. Investigate the Forest of Four Seasons. This lady’s benefactor is trapped there.\"","\"I shall obey. Then what will the Heavenly One do from this point onward?\"","\"This lady requires time to organize her enlightenment, and she shall also help her benefactor survive. By any chance...\"","Yu So-wol almost asked whether the Demonic Brain used the gallery, but stopped herself.","She remembered all the thoughtless garbage posts she had written.","The Heavenly Demon, Yu So-wol, felt not even the slightest shame.","The human Yu So-wol, however, did.","She was embarrassed.","Of course, her garbage posts were closer to diary entries than anything else.","She had also included various realizations she had attained.","Even so, she couldn’t ask.","After hesitating, Yu So-wol changed the subject.","\"If anything may aid his survival, provide advice at any time.\"","\"For now, I believe it would be best to advise him not to abandon hope. The will to live is the most important thing in survival.\"","\"This lady shall remember it. Is there anything else?\"","\"No.\"","\"Then leave.\"","At the order dismissing him, the Demonic Brain bowed and withdrew.","Once he left, Yu So-wol was alone in the room.","She was about to naturally access the gallery when a sudden question occurred to her.","’Come to think of it, he did not ask who this lady’s benefactor was.’","She hadn’t intended to tell him, but the Demonic Brain hadn’t asked either.","That struck her as strange.","The question only occupied her mind for a moment before Yu So-wol accessed the gallery.","Thinking did not suit her.","She could simply leave all matters requiring thought to the Demonic Brain.","She had lived that way until now, and there had never been a problem.","\"I almost died. She’s a genuine calamity. A walking disaster.\"","Meanwhile, the Demonic Brain muttered something close to a lament.","His internal organs had been shaken so badly that a small amount of blood leaked from his mouth.","He roughly wiped the blood away and swallowed some medicine.","Only then did he feel slightly better.","’There is no longer anyone capable of stopping the Heavenly Demon.’","The Heavenly Demon had become far stronger than before.","She had already possessed monstrous power, and now she had attained another enlightenment on top of it.","At the very least, no one in the Central Plains could stop her.","That meant the Demonic Cult could finally achieve the long-awaited ambition of its dreams.","’Not yet. There is still too much to organize.’","The Demonic Cult was a paradise for the abandoned.","Put another way, it also suffered from a great deal of internal discord.","Only after firmly establishing discipline within could it exert influence outside.","For that reason, they would continue waiting quietly for now.","’We must also keep a close watch on the Western Nations.’","If the Central Plains were the only concern, things would be simple.","However, the Western Nations also required caution.","The moment the Demonic Cult acted openly, the Central Plains would be thrown into turmoil, and outside forces would naturally take an interest.","Since ancient times, whenever civil war broke out, external powers had inevitably become involved.","Some madmen even invited them in merely to preserve their own authority.","Surprisingly, such things happened often.","’The problem is how to persuade that monster...’","The Demonic Brain looked around and confirmed that no one was nearby.","Then he stared into empty space.","A familiar-looking window appeared before him.","It was the same gallery Yu So-wol used.","’When she said benefactor, she must have meant Wild Grylls.’","In truth, the Demonic Brain knew Yu So-wol used the gallery.","He even knew that her registered username was Heavenly Demon.","His own gallery history was longer than hers.","It would have been stranger if he hadn’t noticed.","Then why had he remained silent?","└ Heavenly Demon) If matters become impossible, this lady shall go and rescue you herself.","└ Wild Grylls) Really? Aren’t you an extremely busy person?","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady asked an aide, and he said it would be best to give you hope.","└ Wild Grylls) Ma’am? ;;","└ Heavenly Demon) Is there a problem?","└ We’ve decided to call that giving someone false hope.","└ The Heavenly Demon is surprisingly stupid. Lmaoooo.","└ Does she just have no understanding of how the world works?","└ It’s not exactly that. Her thought process is simply different from an ordinary person’s.","\"...\"","Because it was enough for him alone to know this embarrassing truth.","The Demonic Brain sighed before he could laugh.","The Heavenly Demon, revered by countless people, was a gallery addict?","Even a beggar asking for alms would throw away his bowl in disbelief.","At first, he hadn’t believed it either.","Yu So-wol had risen to the highest position through sheer martial power alone.","It was impossible to imagine someone like that wasting time in an online gallery.","However, the Demonic Brain was one of the Heavenly Demon’s closest aides.","He was also exceptionally intelligent, so it hadn’t taken him long to figure it out.","The decisive incident had been the Emperor’s assassination.","She had suddenly gone to the imperial palace, beheaded the Emperor, and returned.","How could he possibly fail to connect the events?","The imperial family had concealed the truth by presenting it as an ordinary power struggle, but the Demonic Brain knew what had really happened.","’What in the world was she thinking when she wrote all these posts...?’","An even greater problem was the content of the Heavenly Demon’s posts.","She carelessly scattered the realizations she had attained without thinking.","Fortunately, her peculiar old-fashioned style caused users to mock her as an old fossil instead of taking her seriously.","However, if those same words had been written in a secret martial arts manual instead of the gallery, the entire Central Plains would have been overturned.","It was similar to how something approaching true literature occasionally appeared among ordinary gallery posts.","’This is something I must carry to my grave.’","Separate from Yu So-wol’s gallery use, the Demonic Brain was also an outstanding gallery addict.","Judging by his posts, more than half of them were devoted to insulting her.","If she ever discovered his identity, his head would fly.","Did that mean he would quit the gallery?","***","Title: I’ve Been Wondering About Something","SmartDemon","There are people in this world who seem stupid and intelligent at the same time.","My superior is like that.","I can’t tell whether she has no thoughts or simply refuses to think.","Maybe she’s intelligent but just doesn’t use her brain.","└ There are quite a few people like that. Lmao.","└ A lot of people simply have strange standards.","└ The important thing is their personality. Does she pay well?","└ SmartDemon) The boss isn’t greedy for money, so she pays well. Lmao.","└ What’s your boss like? A man or a woman?","└ SmartDemon) A woman.","└ Is she pretty?","└ SmartDemon) She is pretty, but she’s a little stupid, so she’s not my type. ;;","└ What is your type?","└ SmartDemon) A beautiful and intelligent woman.","└ You were from the Central Plains, right? What about the Zhuge Clan?","└ SmartDemon) Who are they? Are their women beautiful?","└ Tell us your qualifications first. Lmao.","└ SmartDemon) Is being from the Demonic Cult acceptable?","└ Of course not, you crazy bastard. Lmaoooo.","└ SmartDemon) Damn. Lmao.","Of course not.","A dog was more likely to stop eating its own filth.","The Demonic Brain chuckled.","After using his mind so intensely every day, emptying it always felt refreshing.","Of course, he didn’t completely stop thinking whenever he used the gallery.","There had recently been one registered user causing considerable commotion.","’For now, I should keep a close watch on Wild Grylls...’","He had no intention of helping directly.","Yu So-wol might not think often, but she wasn’t oblivious.","He intended to pretend ignorance as much as possible while merely observing Wild Grylls’ actions.","Yu So-wol was already watching him anyway.","Despite all the talk about the Forest of Four Seasons, the Demonic Brain remained unconvinced.","He would revise his assessment of Wild Grylls only after more definitive evidence appeared.","***","Title: Please Send Me Home","Wild Grylls","I miss my mom.","He was somewhat pitiful.","Should he help?","└ Is your mother doing well at home?","└ Wild Grylls) I’m an orphan.","└ ...","└ Wild Grylls) But I think I’ll be seeing her soon. I should give her a hug when I get there. Lmaoooo.","└ Ah.","└ Aah...","└ Aaaaaah...","└ Wild Grylls) Why is everyone reacting like that?","└ Stay strong, dude...","He truly was pitiful."]},{"title":"Chapter 9","paragraphs":["The Forest of Four Seasons (4)","I have no thoughts.","Because there is literally nothing on my mind.","Ever since I returned to the cave, I’ve just been sitting there, completely spacing out.","I still can’t believe the reality I’m in right now. I wish this were all just a dream.","But no matter how much time passes, nothing changes. This damned place is the Forest of Four Seasons, and this is where I woke up.","There was no way my mental state wouldn’t fall apart.","So I spent the entire day writing depressing, self-pitying posts on the gallery.","Title: The Five Stages of Death (Live Updates)","[Bullshit. I’m looking around a bit more.]","Denial","[Why me? The hell did I do to deserve this?]","Anger","[I’ll be your slave for life. Someone please come pick me up.]","Bargaining","[Please send me home. I want to eat the leftover kimchi stew from yesterday.]","Depression","Those are the actual titles of Grylls’ posts in real time lol.","Only Acceptance is left now.","ᄂ True lololol","L StarlightPrincess) You’re such a terrible person.","_ Science, lol.","L What’s kimchi stew?","_ Dunno.","_ StarlightPrincess) That’s unfortunate.","ᄂ It’s not like he’s terminally ill.","L StarlightPrincess) Then what is it?","_ More like he’s living on borrowed time?","About the same as me, honestly.","One kind user had even made a timeline of my mental breakdown.","Seeing it actually made me chuckle.","To be honest, I was already thinking it was about time to move on to the acceptance stage.","Sitting around sulking wasn’t going to help.","I still had no idea why I had to suffer here of all places, but I couldn’t keep escaping from reality forever.","\"...It’s not like there’s absolutely no way out... right? Right...?\"","The gallery had explained it.","The entire Forest of Four Seasons was surrounded by barriers.","Break through one, and another appears.","Even the barriers you’ve already broken eventually regenerate in a different pattern.","The same applies not only to the ground, but also underground and in the sky.","Once you enter...","You never get out.","First, I need to figure out how big this forest actually is.","If I ended up settling here, I’d better get familiar with my surroundings first.","The cave was right nearby, but getting lost within sight of it would be beyond pathetic.","The problem was...","Apparently that happened pretty often.","I’d need to be careful.","Let’s head to the river first. I need to check whether the water’s safe to drink.","I hadn’t been in the right state of mind to check yesterday.","Back then, I was too busy wanting to cry.","The water itself was probably drinkable.","What I really wanted to know was...","What lived in it.","This forest was crawling with monsters the size of anacondas and bears as big as houses.","Who said the riverbank was any safer?","Even man-eating fish wouldn’t surprise me.","I could literally die while taking a drink.","If it’s safe to drink, I can make the cave my base.","It had already been two days.","Other than the Mad Dog who originally lived there, nothing else had shown up.","Well...","There had been that owlbear.","But let’s pretend that didn’t count.","I got away fast enough.","Besides, the cave was easy to defend.","I’d probably be staying there for the foreseeable future.","Maybe I should just survive on Wall-Fasting Pills?","That was something I’d need to think about.","I stood up.","For now, checking the river came first.","I’d worry about everything else after I got back.","Or maybe I’d just make a poll on the gallery.","Only users with permanent nicknames would be allowed to vote, of course.","There were way too many people whose attitude was,","\"Not my problem, so why should I care?\"","Not collective wisdom...","Collective stupidity.","Whooooosh—","\"Whoa... what’s this?\"","The moment I arrived at the stream I’d noticed yesterday, I couldn’t help but stare.","Was there some dangerous beast?","No.","Man-eating fish?","No.","It was something else entirely.","The scenery beyond the stream.","Yesterday, it had been a desert.","***","Title: Guys, check this out.","Wild Grylls","(Photo of snow-covered mountains beyond the stream.)","Yesterday it was a desert.","Today it’s snowy mountains.","Wonder what it’ll be tomorrow lol.","L Definitely the Forest of Four Seasons! Confirmed!","L Wait... what the heck is that...?","L ...What are you even supposed to say in a situation like this?","ᄂ StarlightPrincess) Just cheer him on.","_ SwordMaster) Excuse me, but... you’re not a criminal, are you?","L Wild Grylls) Does stealing money from my mom’s wallet as a kid count?","L SwordMaster) Didn’t you say you were an orphan?","L Wild Grylls) She was around back then.","ᄂ SwordMaster) ;_; Sorry...","L Wild Grylls) I’m used to it lol.","_ SwordMaster) I stole from my parents’ wallet too haha...","L Wild Grylls) Then why aren’t you coming already?","L SwordMaster) Busy with work.","L Wild Grylls) Doing what?","L SwordMaster) House security. Haha.","L So... unemployed? lol","ᄂ Seriously, what’s gonna happen to Grylls?","_ At this point, I have no idea lol.","ᄂ He’ll have to survive on his own.","L Shouldn’t we give him disaster relief funds? lol","ᄂ Heavenly Demon) The mountains are beautiful.","_ CheongguPrincess) They really are. Almost as pretty as my face lol.","L Heavenly Demon)?","L ?","L ?","L ?","_ CheongguPrincess) What? If you’ve got a problem, come fight me.","ᄂ Heavenly Demon) Where do you live?","Even getting challenged to a duel had become normal.","I let out a dry laugh.","Yesterday, everything beyond the stream had been a desert.","Today...","It was an enormous mountain range blanketed in pure white snow.","For a second I wondered if I’d somehow come to the wrong place.","But that made no sense.","A desert right next to snowy mountains?","The boundary was perfectly clear.","The environment hadn’t gradually changed.","Everything beyond the stream was simply...","Different.","Is someone messing with me?","I sighed and walked over to the stream.","Judging by all the minnows swimming around, the water quality looked excellent.","At least there was one piece of good news.","Later, I’d bring the water bottle the Heavenly Demon had given me.","Still...","Better check things first.","I started by testing the depth.","Splash.","The moment I stuck my hand in...","Confusion hit me before the coolness did.","For a second I thought my eyes were playing tricks on me.","But the farther I pushed my arm in...","The deeper it kept going.","I couldn’t touch the bottom.","The water was so unbelievably clear that it looked much shallower than it actually was.","This should be enough.","It wasn’t bottomless.","You could probably cross it if you really wanted to.","Of course...","There was absolutely no reason to cross into the snowy mountains.","Unless I was trying to kill myself.","\"Ribbit.\"","\"Hm?\"","I’d just pulled my arm out of the water when I heard an odd sound.","It had come from nearby.","I turned toward it.","\"Ribbit.\"","\"...A frog?\"","A frog.","A golden frog.","It sat atop a rock in the middle of the stream.","Whatever else it was...","Its entire body glittered with a metallic golden sheen.","And somehow that only made it seem more dangerous.","Animals with colors that vivid usually had one thing in common.","Poison.","I’d better stay away.","Poison was the last thing I wanted to deal with.","Even if it wasn’t poisonous...","The thing was about the size of a small dog.","It was seriously unsettling.","\"RRAAAAK!\"","\"Huh? Wait—\"","Just as I turned to leave...","The golden frog suddenly stood upright on its long hind legs.","Then it leaned its head all the way back.","It made a disgusting noise, almost like a person gathering phlegm in their throat.","A moment later, it snapped its head forward.","\" Ptooey! \"","Piiing!","A sticky golden glob shot out of its mouth like a bullet.","Straight at my face.","I barely managed to dodge.","The viscous golden projectile grazed past me.","A split second later...","It struck the tree behind me.","Sssssssss!","\"Holy shit.\"","The tree...","Melted.","So it wasn’t poison.","It was acid.","But I didn’t have time to admire it.","The frog had already leaned its head back again to reload.","Getting away took priority.","I bolted before it could spit again.","\" Ptooey! \"","\"Whoa!\"","Another near miss.","If I hadn’t ducked, it would’ve nailed me in the back of the head.","Fortunately...","The frog didn’t chase me.","It seemed to consider the stream its territory.","\"Huff... huff...\"","I ran for my life all the way back to the cave before finally catching my breath.","What kind of suffering was this?","I’d finally found clean water...","Only to get bullied by a damn frog.","Unbelievable.","The stream’s too deep to approach safely...","If only I had a bow.","Not that I’d know how to use one anyway.","That frog definitely hadn’t been there yesterday.","Maybe...","Did it only attack because I’d put my hand in the water?","Now I wasn’t even sure whether I could drink safely.","Worst-case scenario...","The frog might spit into the river itself.","***","Title: Guys, I found a golden frog.","Wild Grylls","No picture.","I was too busy running for my life.","This bastard spits acid.","Anyone know what it is?","L A frog that spits acid? What kind of frog is that? lol","L Sure, it’s the Forest of Four Seasons, but that’s a bit much lol.","L No picture means it’s 99% fake lol.","ᄂ AllFather) Did you happen to find it in a river?","L Wild Grylls) Do you know what it is?","L AllFather) Yes. Its official name is the Golden Poison Frog. It’s an extremely rare species found only in exceptionally clean water. Its poison is so potent that many people have died trying to capture one. Please be careful.","L Wild Grylls) Wait... it wasn’t acid? It was poison??","L AllFather) The poison is simply that powerful.","Amid all the usual pointless comments...","One user with a permanent nickname replied.","AllFather.","He was one of those users who only appeared occasionally to leave a comment before disappearing again.","He barely made any posts himself.","When he did, they were almost always about magic or alchemy.","Most of them were filled with technical jargon, so I usually ignored them.","He gave off serious professor vibes.","He also tended to speak politely, so I did the same.","L Wild Grylls) Yeah. I found it in the river. It spat at me the moment I put my hand in the water.","L AllFather) Approximately how large was it?","L Wild Grylls) About the size of a dog.","L AllFather) It must have grown larger because it’s in the Forest of Four Seasons. They’re normally only about the size of a finger joint.","This place really did have every bizarre creature imaginable.","A frog whose venom was so potent it looked like acid.","And with the entire river serving as its fortress...","It was practically the equivalent of an archer firing from atop a castle wall.","More than anything... I just want to be able to drink water safely.","If I showed up there too often...","That thing might start waiting for me on purpose.","That would be a serious problem.","Even while I was thinking it over, notifications kept pouring in.","Lately, every post I made seemed to attract a flood of comments.","L AllFather) If you manage to capture the Golden Poison Frog, I’ll pay you 20,000 gold. I’d like to study it.","L Isn’t that just a roundabout way of telling him to go die?","L If you catch it, I’ll give you 50,000 gold lol.","L Wild Grylls) I kind of have to catch it... Otherwise I can’t get any water. Any other advice?","ᄂ AllFather) I’m afraid not. It’s such a rare species that very little is known about it. The only confirmed fact is that it’s primarily active in the morning. You may also need an antidote.","ᄂ Then just go drink water in the evening lol.","L Wild Grylls) Evenings are more dangerous ;;","ᄂ What comes out at night?","L Wild Grylls) It’s dangerous because I don’t know what might come out.","There was no obvious way to deal with it.","In the end, I had no choice but to solve the problem myself.","This was the first obstacle standing between me and a secure source of drinking water.","To overcome it, I would need to prepare thoroughly.","Before that, I should return the compasses.","I planned to return all of them to their original owners except the one the Heavenly Demon had given me.","First, I made a public post so everyone would see it.","Five minutes later, I began sending trade requests.","The first person I contacted was the user named StarlightPrincess .","Maybe it was because she practically lived on the gallery all day, but she accepted the request almost immediately.","[Wild Grylls: Hello. I sent you a trade request because I wanted to return your compass.]","[StarlightPrincess: Oh. Okay! You really don’t have to return it, though...]","[Wild Grylls: The one the Heavenly Demon gave me is enough. Carrying the rest around would be difficult.]","[StarlightPrincess: I understand. Let’s both do our best.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. I hope you recover soon.]","It seemed she really was sick.","She had a kind personality too.","Next was PraiseTheSun , the user I suspected was a dark elf.","[Wild Grylls: Hello. I sent you a trade request to return your compass.]","[PraiseTheSun: Keep it.]","[Wild Grylls: I still have a conscience. I should return it.]","[PraiseTheSun: I don’t take pocket change like that.]","[Wild Grylls: ;;;]","That was so casual it almost made me feel embarrassed.","Still, since they had helped me, I ought to repay the favor.","When I said I would compensate them later if I found something valuable, I received an unexpected reply.","[PraiseTheSun: I like you. Need anything else? Looks like you could use a shield.]","[Wild Grylls: I do need one, but I’ll buy it properly. I sold something called a Steel-Scale Snake.]","[PraiseTheSun: I don’t take pocket change.]","[Wild Grylls: Wait ;; You’re a dark elf, right?]","[PraiseTheSun: Yeah.]","[Wild Grylls: Are all dark elves rich?]","The dark elves I knew were a race opposed to ordinary elves.","They shared the same roots, but their dispositions were completely different.","Unlike peace-loving elves, they did not hesitate to use dirty tactics.","Even so, they did not cross certain lines.","Their beliefs were closer to the idea that one had to cultivate strength in order to preserve peace.","Perhaps because of that, though, they tended to lack social skills.","Of course, that was merely what I knew.","I could not apply my own assumptions to this world.","Even the elves here were far removed from peace.","They were practically defined by imperialism.","[PraiseTheSun: There are a lot of rich ones, I guess? Cetan produces tons of gold and resources. Isn’t that common knowledge?]","[Wild Grylls: I’m from another world, so I don’t really know.]","[PraiseTheSun: That wasn’t just a character gimmick?]","[Wild Grylls: It’s real...]","Whether they believed me or not did not matter.","I was trapped in a forest where I could not meet anyone anyway.","My place of origin was meaningless.","PraiseTheSun seemed to understand that and casually moved on.","[PraiseTheSun: Anyway, dark elves are a kinder and more easygoing race than those insane, old-fashioned elves. Got it?]","[Wild Grylls: That sounds very emphatic. Was it different in the past?]","[PraiseTheSun: It used to be the opposite. But after we settled in the desert and became rich, everyone grew more generous. We used to have awful tempers because we were constantly discriminated against.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s realistic.]","[PraiseTheSun: Still, don’t underestimate us. Surviving in the desert made us damn good at fighting.]","[Wild Grylls: I wasn’t planning to. Is there anything in particular I should be careful about?]","[PraiseTheSun: Call us darkies and you’re dead. No, I’ll curse you to death.]","[PraiseTheSun has registered a trade item.]","[PraiseTheSun: I’ll give you this, so send me anything that’s good for the body. I don’t have much time, so hurry up and take it.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. I won’t forget this favor.]","[PraiseTheSun: Sure. Stay safe.]","Were they in roughly the same social position as Black people back on Earth?","Usually cheerful, but terrifying the instant someone touched a sore spot.","Here, it was racial discrimination in the literal sense of discrimination between species, so I needed to be careful.","I should learn about these things gradually.","Even though the gallery was anonymous, openly making discriminatory remarks did not suit my personality.","Besides, I was in a situation where I needed to build goodwill.","If all I did was make people dislike me, I would only be hurting myself.","Was everyone on the gallery kind?","Or were users with permanent nicknames simply nicer?","I disconnected from PraiseTheSun.","The moment the connection ended, I checked the item they had sent me.","\"...?\"","I could not help but stare in confusion.","The item glittered brilliantly.","It was shaped roughly like a shield, but its entire surface was covered in gold.","A literal golden shield.","Just how obscenely rich did someone have to be to casually give away something like this?","...I wonder if it performs well.","I turned the gleaming golden shield over in my hands before equipping it.","It was lighter than expected and comfortable to carry, though I should probably test how durable it was.","I had no intention of testing it with the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","I had a feeling that would only damage the shield.","\"Next is CheongguPrincess, I guess?\"","What a peculiar username.","Judging by the name alone, she seemed to be a woman.","However, ninety percent of the people who lived on the gallery were abnormal.","What kind of person would it be this time?","[CheongguPrincess: Then cheer for our Chae-U. That’ll be enough.]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t know much about this world. What kind of team is Chae-U?]","I knew this world had things resembling sports.","However, I did not know the details.","It was an entirely different world populated by a wide variety of races.","It was bound to be completely different from what I knew.","[Wild Grylls: Hello. I sent you a trade request to return your compass.]","[CheongguPrincess: Hellooo. Just keep it.]","Her reply was similar to PraiseTheSun’s.","She said she did not need the compass back.","For a moment, I wondered whether the gallery was filled with nothing but kind people.","But after thinking about it, perhaps it was only natural.","These were the people who had willingly given me compasses the moment I made my post.","That was all the more reason to strengthen my relationships with them.","[CheongguPrincess: Oh my gosh! You don’t know Chaemes United, the most famous and prestigious club in all of Mephisto?! You’ve wasted half your life!]","[Wild Grylls: The half I have left is hanging by a thread.]","[CheongguPrincess: Ah! Sorry! You were living on borrowed time, weren’t you!]","She was not wrong, but hearing her say it so bluntly was depressing.","How had my life ended up like this?","Just as CheongguPrincess’s bluntness began to dampen my mood—","[Wild Grylls: I have a conscience, so I should return it. I just don’t have anything I can give you right now.]","[CheongguPrincess has registered trade items.]","[CheongguPrincess: I’ll give you these, and from now on, you’re a Chae-U fan.]","[Wild Grylls: What did you send me?]","[CheongguPrincess: Jerseys of the most famous players, Neves and Vannir! The material is excellent, so wear them around. I’ll send two home jerseys and two away jerseys.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh. Okay...]","[Wild Grylls: What exactly is that?]","[CheongguPrincess: There’s a cheap imitation called Chaemes City, so ignore them! They’re funded by Cetan’s filthy gold money. They have no tradition. None at all.]","I felt slightly bewildered.","Still, I happened to need clothes, so this was fortunate.","I planned to buy soap with money, so that was not a problem.","But I needed something else to wear while my clothes were drying.","For now, I could still endure it.","As more time passed, however, my need for extra clothing would only increase.","[CheongguPrincess: Chaemes United is a club with a proud two-hundred-year history. I guarantee you’ll be completely obsessed with them soon, Mr. Grylls.]","[Wild Grylls: First, I need to check whether it’s even a sport I know. It might be different from what I’m familiar with. Either way, thank you very much for the clothes.]","[CheongguPrincess: Don’t mention it. But there’s one thing I need to ask of you.]","Why did this stranger give off such a familiar feeling?","A dry laugh escaped me.","CheongguPrincess ended the conversation after saying she would upload a highlight reel later and that I should watch it to calm my mind and body.","Once the conversation ended, I checked the clothes she had sent me.","They were jerseys with large names printed across them.","I have no idea what language this is.","Unfortunately, I could not read the names.","Hadn’t they said the gallery had an automatic translation feature?","The emblem on the chest, however, looked rather impressive.","Just as she had claimed, it gave off a distinct sense of history and tradition.","It was not only the design.","The white and blue colors were blended tastefully, making the jerseys look quite beautiful.","They were not ideal colors for the wilderness, but what I needed most was clothing, so it did not matter.","The material is good too.","It was also highly elastic.","They would probably prove useful in many ways.","I smiled briefly, then immediately opened the gallery to check the latest posts.","CheongguPrincess had said she would upload something soon.","I intended to leave a comment thanking her when she did.","[Chaemes United Special Highlights Collection]","The instant I saw the post, I clicked it without hesitation.","\"Huh?\"","My eyes widened as I watched the video she had uploaded.","\"This is soccer.\"","Why did soccer exist here?","Then do they have baseball too?","Every so often, a lunatic would appear on the gallery.","Could that be why?"]},{"title":"Chapter 10","paragraphs":["The Forest of Four Seasons (5)","There were many different races in the world, but whenever people were asked which race was the most specialized in combat , they all gave the same answer.","The demons.","Even the demons themselves acknowledged it.","Horns growing from their heads, blue-toned skin, and inverted eyes that sharply distinguished them from other races.","Mana they could naturally wield thanks to their innate physiques.","Magic of overwhelmingly greater power than that of other races.","All of these traits combined had earned them the name \"the devil race,\" and true to that name, they were fiercely devoted to their desires.","***","Title: I’ll Teach You Continental History","In the past, demons caused all the trouble.","Now it’s the elves.","History lesson over!","L Looking at history, demons were absolute thugs.","L There’s a reason a Hero appears in every era lol.","L If nobody keeps these bastards in check, the world is screwed lol.","L What kind of lives do demons even live?","Because they were so faithful to their desires, they had been infamous for their cruelty in the distant past.","Their tyranny had been so severe that a Hero appeared in every generation to kill or restrain the Demon King .","The Demon King was the ruler of Mephisto, the nation of demons, while the Hero was an elite warrior personally cultivated by humanity.","A noble character.","Outstanding talent.","Devout faith.","And overwhelming divine power granted in proportion to those qualities.","Because of these circumstances, the past had been filled with repeated clashes between the Demon King and the Hero, resulting in no small number of casualties.","But perhaps the demons eventually grew tired of that long conflict.","Or maybe they simply got bored.","L It’s not like they actually came to their senses. There was once a guy who killed a player for scoring an own goal lol.","L Holy crap, that’s insane lolol.","L Is that why they stopped calling it a \"suicide goal\" and changed it to \"own goal\"?","_ That’s why player protection is extremely strict in Mephisto.","***","Title: When Did the Demons Finally Come to Their Senses?","They suddenly got quiet at some point.","L They calmed down when they got bored of fighting and invented that weird ball game.","L Hey, don’t call it weird! Say that to a demon and they’ll tear you limb from limb.","L Those bastards are surprisingly serious about ball games lol.","The demons desperately craved a form of combat that did not involve fists.","They wanted something as exciting and tense as battle.","They had grown tired of simply punching and kicking each other.","So they put their battles against the Heroes aside and conducted study after study.","Eventually, they created an entire culture.","Ball games such as soccer, baseball, basketball, rugby, and American football.","In other words—","Sports.","At first, even the demons themselves thought it was ridiculous.","Why play with balls when they could simply fight?","There were already gladiators who fought each other, so why choose ball games of all things?","However, as time passed and society and law developed, violence gradually became taboo.","More importantly, there were far too few forms of entertainment.","When people gained peace of mind, they naturally sought amusement.","Because of that social trend, along with the limitations of an era lacking proper entertainment, the demons inevitably began to take sports seriously.","Thus, the demons—who were passionately devoted to every source of dopamine except drugs and gambling—became completely obsessed with mere \"ball games.\"","***","Title: Here’s How Serious These Bastards Are","You can mock demons for being weak in a fight and they’ll just laugh it off.","Why?","Because they know they’re stronger.","They’re naturally powerful enough to rival elves.","But ball games?","Call them weak at those and they’ll charge at you like they genuinely intend to kill you.","Especially soccer. Their pride was shattered when humans won the championship lol.","ᄂ How do you know that?","L I teased my demon friend while we were playing futsal and he broke my arm.","With demons potentially invading at any moment while blasting magic everywhere, there was no reason for other races to accept their culture.","Ironically, however, the first race to adopt demon culture was humanity.","One might ask why humans, who had suffered the greatest losses during the long wars against demons, would do such a thing.","The answer was simple.","Humans had short lifespans.","That meant their generations changed far faster than those of other races.","The generations that remembered the demons’ past atrocities gradually disappeared.","Eventually, only generations who remembered them as idiots obsessed with ball games remained.","As interaction with the demons slowly increased and humans began adopting their culture, humanity came up with a clever strategy.","ᄂ He brought it on himself lololol.","_ Did he at least pay your medical bills?","ᄂ Yeah, he did. But he warned me not to say that to any other demons. Apparently, I might actually die.","L Just how serious are they about this? lololol.","Naturally, sports had originally been a culture enjoyed only by demons.","The other races had shown no interest.","***","Title: An Unavoidable Trap from the Demons’ Perspective","Human: If we have a problem, let’s settle it through ball games. You’re already insanely strong anyway.","Demon: Fair enough lol.","Human: But you know how pathetic it would look if you started causing trouble just because you lost, right?","Demon: Why would we lose? lol.","And ten years later, the humans completely crushed them.","Human: We won, you losers lol.","Demon: Screw this. It’s war.","Human: Wow, you’re starting a war because you lost a ball game? Have you got no pride?","Demon: Ah, damn it... This pisses me off, but I can’t argue with that.","L Lololol, there’s literally nothing they can do.","_ Does diplomacy really work like that?","L It’s summarized, but that’s genuinely what happened lol.","The demons were a race whose pride rivaled that of the elves.","They had a history of tormenting neighboring nations using their natural strength, but that had been during a more barbaric age.","After spreading the culture of sports across the world, their reputation gradually improved.","Their pride, however, remained unchanged.","Humans cunningly took advantage of that pride, provoking it little by little to gain benefits.","The demons had effectively trapped themselves in a contradiction, so they had no choice but to grit their teeth and focus on diplomacy.","L That’s a fact.","L It only worked because their strength was roughly equal lol.","L But what were the elves doing?","ᄂ Those bastards just stood back with their arms folded until it was all over lol.","L That’s because Mephisto is close to the human kingdoms.","L Elves are useless as always.","ᄂ And now those same damn elves are causing trouble, right?","L What the hell did we humans ever do wrong?","L Our ancestors founded the country in the wrong place lol.","L We’re surrounded by nonhuman nations on all sides lolol","***","Title: One Important Fact","Without the Hero, the demons would still have started a war.","Of course, most of this was spoken half-jokingly.","Sports remained sports.","Its popularity, however, rose to the heavens because it allowed different races to overcome their natural differences and compete fairly.","Mana could not be used.","Victory depended solely on physical ability and skill.","Most importantly, sports embodied the chivalric spirit appropriate to the age.","Sportsmanship.","That romantic ideal captivated people as well.","***","Title: What Are Dwarves Even Good At?","They’re too short for soccer and basketball.","They don’t have the physique for rugby or American football.","Even baseball is difficult because their strike zone is weird.","What can they even do?","_ PassingDwarf) We make the balls, asshole.","ᄂ Do you earn a lot?","L PassingDwarf) We make a shitload whenever there’s a major tournament.","_ Did dwarves make the balls in ancient times too?","L I heard they used human heads as balls back then.","L What the hell ;;","***","Title: Something Interesting About Beastfolk","The race that loves both the quietest sport, baseball, and the roughest sport, American football, the most.","Why?","L SuspiciouslyFurry) What are you talking about? In baseball, they smash people’s heads with bats.","L That’s a gang fight, you idiot lololol.","L Bench-clearing brawls lololol.","L Beastfolk are built tough, so they’re fine even after that lol.","Dwarves were disadvantaged by their stature and could not participate in many sports directly, but they still gained plenty of related opportunities.","Balls, uniforms, and all kinds of equipment.","Given the technological level of the age, every form of precision craftsmanship was entrusted to dwarves.","As industrialization and commercialization rapidly progressed and various tournaments began to be held, Mephisto transformed into a nation of culture.","Sports could make people feel joy, anger, sorrow, and pleasure simply by watching.","At the same time, they were a drug capable of driving people insane.","Popular sports differed from nation to nation and race to race, but the fact that Mephisto had invented them never changed.","For that reason, sports were deeply woven into everyday life in Mephisto.","A form of entertainment enjoyed by everyone, regardless of age, sex, or social status.","\"No! How could he miss that?! Are you kidding me?!\"","The same applied even to Mephisto’s highest-ranking figures.","A woman with the blue skin and inverted eyes unique to demons, yet possessing exceptional beauty.","Her glossy hair was as black as midnight, while the curled horns growing from her head gave her a strangely captivating charm.","And finally, she had a figure capable of setting countless men’s hearts ablaze.","There was not a single flaw to be found.","\"Wow. Even I could’ve scored that.\"","She was Keirin Rondel Archive , princess of Mephisto and heir to the title of Demon King.","She cursed as she watched the soccer match being displayed through a magical broadcasting orb.","After the creation of sports, Mephisto had invented various forms of magic to properly industrialize them.","The broadcasting magic Keirin was currently watching was one such invention.","Its coverage extended across an enormous area.","\"That piece of garbage cost one hundred billion yura? Are the people running Chae-U blind?\"","Keirin clicked her tongue and furrowed her elegant brow.","Her expression was filled with displeasure.","As the princess of Mephisto, she was revered by countless people.","Thanks to her innate strength and background, she faced almost no political pressure.","If something displeased her, she could apply pressure whenever she wished.","But doing so in sports would cause a massive scandal.","I know there’s nothing I can do, but it’s still frustrating.","A noble could own a club.","However, the moment they used political influence, they would be expelled immediately.","It was not formally written into law, but it was an unspoken rule.","Sports were a culture enjoyed not only by nobles, but by everyone.","Unless it involved something unavoidable, like war, not even the highest-ranking members of society could completely control it.","They could exert some influence through policy, but interference beyond that was impossible.","[The match is over! Chaemes United suffer a two-to-one defeat at home!]","[It’ll be a festival in Moss Village tonight. They’ve taken another step closer to their long-awaited promotion to the Challengers League!]","[Meanwhile, Chaemes United are now barely holding on to their position in the table. How will Manager Horen respond to—]","\"Damn it.\"","Click.","Keirin irritably shut off the broadcasting magic.","They had thrown away a match they had practically won because someone got sent off.","She covered her face with both hands for a long moment before slowly lowering them.","Then, with a blank expression, she accessed the gallery.","[Chae-U are mid-table trash! Chae-U are mid-table trash! Chae-U are mid-table trash!]","[The Cheonggu bastards are trembling~ The Cheonggu bastards are trembling so hard~ The Cheonggu bastards are trembling~]","[???: Better start sucking up now, huh?]","[Cheonggu fans eliminated lololol.]","The moment the match ended, lunatics flooded the gallery.","It happened every time.","Keirin let out a hollow laugh and made a post.","***","Title: Revealing My Asshole","CheongguPrincess","(Picture of an emblem bearing a deer symbol.)","This is my asshole.","L Lololol, did Cheonggu lose today?","L CheongguPrincess) Those motherless bitches conceded two goals in stoppage time lol.","L No wonder the lunatics came crawling out.","After making the post, Keirin rose from her seat.","Her head felt far too hot.","She needed to cool down.","Before that, I should clean the room.","She looked around.","Chaemes United jerseys, replica trophies, and countless other pieces of Chae-U merchandise filled the space.","It was exactly the kind of room someone utterly obsessed with soccer would decorate.","And that was precisely what she was.","Snap!","Keirin snapped her fingers.","Every item disappeared, leaving behind a completely barren room.","This place had originally been designed as a training hall.","It was a private training facility constructed solely for Keirin.","She looked around the empty hall several times before lowering her gaze.","Instead of a dignified dress, she was wearing an almost painfully ordinary jersey.","The name printed on it belonged to a former legend of Chae-U.","Snap!","Another snap of her fingers transformed the jersey into a beautiful black dress.","All of it had been done through magic.","Normally, a mage would need to chant an incantation.","Keirin had no such need.","She could manifest magic with a simple gesture.","After carefully checking that nothing was out of place, she walked toward the exit.","A door protected by numerous security spells and locking mechanisms stood there.","Clunk!","Keirin disengaged every lock and stepped outside.","A middle-aged butler was waiting with several knights.","\"You’ve worked hard, Princess. Have you finished your training?\"","\"Yes. You have worked hard as well.\"","\"Not at all. It is my duty to serve you, Princess.\"","The butler bowed deeply as he answered.","Keirin walked past him and gently patted his shoulder.","It was her way of acknowledging his efforts.","Emotion immediately appeared on the butler’s face.","A warmth that could not be found in the current Demon King.","That warmth drew people toward her.","She had every reason to become arrogant as the next heir to the title of Demon King.","Keirin’s personal strength also ranked among the five greatest on the entire continent.","Despite that, she was neither arrogant nor unkind.","Her heart was gentle as well.","One might wonder whether such a small gesture really mattered.","However, it was necessary to remember that these people were demons.","Besides, Keirin only spoke stiffly. She was kind and considerate not only toward the butler, but toward everyone.","Her Highness seems to be in a poor mood today. Did she fail to gain anything from her training?","The butler thought as he followed behind Keirin.","After serving her for many years, he had learned to read her emotions to some extent.","Today, she was in a terrible mood.","An exceptionally terrible one.","At times like this, the wisest course of action was to remain silent.","She might be kinder than most demons, but Keirin was still a demon.","If someone irritated her, magic would come flying.","Even emotional-control training, which she only does once or twice a week, must be difficult.","Demons were a warlike race, rivaling even beastfolk in that regard.","They enjoyed the act of competing to determine victory and defeat.","In the past, that nature had manifested as violence and caused tremendous damage to those around them.","But things were different now.","As violence became taboo, controlling one’s emotions grew increasingly important.","This was especially true for those of high status, since a single impulsive outburst could ruin everything.","For that reason, emotional-control training was extremely important.","And because of that, it was also difficult and painful.","Damn it. Seriously. How the hell do you concede two goals in stoppage time?","Keirin had indeed been practicing emotional control.","Her method, however, differed from the usual one.","As an ardent Chaemes United supporter, simply watching a match sent her emotions surging up and down without warning.","In the past, she had struggled to control herself and smashed the training hall whenever she got the chance.","That was no longer the case.","Now she had reached the point where she could simply think, Sigh. You useless bastards. Of course you’d do that, and move on.","Whatever else might be said, her mental fortitude was slowly reaching a level comparable to that of a Saintess.","\"Why am I a Chae-U fan?\"","After returning to her bedroom, Keirin lay on the bed and thought back on the past.","Why had she become a fan of soccer, and Chaemes United in particular?","Originally, she had lived a life far removed from soccer.","No matter how widely the culture had spread across the world, she was still a member of the upper class.","Soccer, in particular, had spread upward from the lower classes, so the aristocracy had harbored a fair amount of hostility toward it.","However, not even the upper class could ignore the wealth generated by culture.","Culture itself was also impossible to suppress.","The moment someone tried to stop it, it only spread further.","Without it, things probably would have been even harder.","Keirin had been educated to believe that soccer was something watched only by ignorant commoners.","Yet many clubs were owned by nobles.","Only royalty and a handful of particularly old-fashioned aristocrats truly disliked it.","Even they viewed sports in a generally favorable light.","It was soccer alone that drew their hostility.","Because of that, Keirin had once looked down on soccer as well.","Then, little by little, she became obsessed with it.","The cause was none other than the gallery .","Everything changed when she happened to gain access to it.","Knowledge she had never encountered while being raised like a flower in a greenhouse.","And the strange, addictive quality found only in soccer.","For Keirin, who had been born a demon, it was no different from trying a new kind of drug.","Naturally, she began supporting Chaemes United, the club representing her home region.","She even created the gallery username CheongguPrincess .","Damn it. It’s frustrating that I can’t even attend matches in person.","Keirin did not express that frustration in reality.","There were political reasons.","One might wonder how something as trivial as soccer could become a political issue.","Strictly speaking, it was closer to a generational conflict.","Demons might not live as long as elves, but their lifespans were still considerable.","As a result, generational turnover was slow.","Many members of the older generation who remembered the demons’ brutal past were still alive.","That older generation firmly controlled the existing power structure, creating a politically delicate situation.","One generation regarded glory stained with violence as a form of honor.","The other had embraced a new form of entertainment called sports.","As the two generations clashed, nobles naturally had no choice but to pay attention.","Since soccer was the most popular sport of all, it inevitably became entangled in politics.","Why did I do that... I only did it because I hated seeing Chae-City grow...","On the surface, Keirin was regarded as someone belonging to the generation distant from soccer.","That was because of one of her policies.","She had imposed certain restrictions on Cetan’s gold money.","Part of the reason was that those damned dark elves were notorious for swallowing famous clubs with their obscene spending.","But the biggest reason was the Noisy Neighbor .","Chaemaster City had once been a third-division club.","Then it received an injection of gold money and rose into a powerhouse almost overnight.","It had even won the biggest tournament in the world last year.","Meanwhile, Chae-U continued to struggle.","Keirin’s pride had been thoroughly crushed.","Naturally, it made her blood boil.","That was why she had spoken up just once.","***","Title: Poll—Who Do Chae-U Fans Hate the Most?","The Medes FamilyPrincess Keirin","L I know why people hate the Medes Family, but why Princess Keirin?","L She made the acquisition process much stricter. Otherwise, Chae-U could’ve enjoyed that sweet gold money too.","***","Title: Basically, It Went Like This","Medes Family: We’re selling Chae-U~ Huge bargain sale!","Cetan: Oh! We’ll buy it! Here’s the money!","Keirin: Hell no! Not happening! Policy enacted immediately!","Medes Family: Oh no. The policy means we’ll have to raise the price lol.","Cetan: Fuck this, we’re not buying.","ᄂ Lololol, now I understand perfectly.","L But doesn’t Keirin’s position make sense too?","L Opinion is split about fifty-fifty. Still, to Cheonggu fans, she’s an enemy they want to tear apart lol.","L Doesn’t Keirin hate soccer too?","_ There’s no official statement, but she probably does.","For Keirin, it was enough to make her explode in frustration.","Her love for soccer went beyond even her love for Chae-U.","If she were ever allowed to cut loose, she would attend matches every week.","She might even become a hooligan and cause trouble now and then.","Since she could not do that, she secretly bought jerseys and merchandise to soothe herself.","Of course, watching the matches only made her angry again, but that was beside the point.","Just wait until I become Demon King. I’ll attend matches openly while wearing the jersey.","With soccer at its core, sports had become an area not even the Demon King could recklessly interfere with.","The moment the ruler touched it, they would effectively be declaring hostility toward the people.","That was both the terrifying power of culture and one of its side effects.","Was that not why demons and other races alike had become completely absorbed in it?","Countless forms of magic had been invented merely to develop that single culture.","Broadcasting magic was one example.","Amusingly enough, Mephisto was moving closer and closer not toward victory through conquest, but toward victory through culture.","None of that matters. I just wish they’d stop making such terrible signings.","Keirin sighed inwardly and made a gloomy face.","She no longer looked like the ever-dignified princess of the demons.","She looked like nothing more than a troubled Chae-U supporter.","The gallery was the best place to soothe feelings like these.","There was still plenty of time before the next match anyway.","Wild Grylls... Why did this human end up in the Forest of Four Seasons?","Normally, she spent the days before a match writing about Chae-U or posting nonsense.","Recently, however, that had changed.","Among the endless posts and countless kinds of people, Wild Grylls’ posts stood out.","He was the person who claimed to have fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","At first, she had not believed him.","She could not have believed him.","But as time passed, she found herself paying more and more attention.","The biggest reason was that his posts received overwhelmingly more recommendations than others.","He says he came from another world? What a joke.","Whether it was a character gimmick or the ramblings of a lunatic, it was still interesting enough to hold her attention.","She had nothing else to do in her free time anyway.","There were still several days until the next soccer match.","So, partly to pass the time and partly to help him, she had sent him a compass.","Then—","[CheongguPrincess: Then cheer for our Chae-U. That’ll be enough.]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t know much about this world. What kind of team is Chae-U?]","\"What?!\"","Keirin was horrified.","How could anyone not know the famous Chae-U?","Someone living in a remote countryside village might be excused.","But Grylls was a gallery user.","Ninety percent of gallery users were abnormal, but among them, sports fans were unquestionably the most conspicuously abnormal.","Sports fans were not merely insane.","Their minds had rotted beyond repair.","Some had even rotted so completely that they attained enlightenment and became Buddhas.","\"He doesn’t know Chae-U? Then I’ll have to teach him.\"","Keirin began preaching the greatness of Chae-U and even gifted him several jerseys.","Grylls accepted them, albeit somewhat reluctantly.","Keirin did not stop there.","Deciding that she should upload a special highlight reel, she posted a collection of Chae-U highlights on the gallery.","The gallery had a storage function and allowed users to upload videos from outside sources.","That was also why sports highlights could be posted at regular intervals.","Not long after she uploaded the Chae-U special","***","Title: Starting Today, I Am a Chaemes United Fan","(Photo of a thumbs-up directed toward the jerseys laid on the floor.)","Thank you, CheongguPrincess.","Thanks to you, I don’t have to worry as much about clothes anymore.","L Ahhh. The whole world is Chae-U.","ᄂ Of all teams, it had to be Chae-U lololol.","L He’s alone anyway, so does it really matter?","L Better than walking around naked.","L From this day forward, this is the Chaemes United Gallery.","L KingLeor) Why would you give him that garbage? It must smell awful.","Satisfying.","Extremely satisfying.","Keirin smiled proudly as she read Grylls’ post.","As of today, Chae-U had gained one more supporter.","He might be trapped in the Forest of Four Seasons, but a fan was still a fan.","More than anything else, that pleased her.","Now she could support him as much as she wanted.","If a fan dies, Chae-U will be sad too. I need to support him properly so he doesn’t die.","If a Chae-U fan became sad, then Chae-U would be sad as well.","And that might even affect their performance.","It was a one-track line of reasoning, but people were like that.","Once they became deeply obsessed with something, their thoughts naturally grew simpler.","Just as Keirin was about to close the gallery in satisfaction, a comment appeared that immediately irritated her.","Her elegant brow furrowed.","She knew this permanent-name user.","He was a supporter of Leor, Chae-U’s greatest rival.","He was also the user Keirin hated most.","Mocking Chae-U by calling them \"Cheonggu\" whenever he had the chance was only the beginning.","He also had a talent for scraping at her nerves in countless other ways.","L CheongguPrincess) You’re here again? You really must have nothing better to do.","_ KingLeor) As if you’re any better lol. So, did we win or not?","\"You bastard.\"","Keirin swore.","Chae-U had recently lost three-nil to Leor.","The score could only be described as completely one-sided.","That was precisely why the user could mock her.","Those bastards used to be mocked as mid-table trash...!","Ten years earlier, Leor had been a fallen royal house.","But after changing managers, it regained its former prestige.","Meanwhile, Chae-U continued its endless decline.","Changing managers had made no difference.","L CheongguPrincess) Hehe. Once our owner changes, we’ll beat you too.","_ KingLeor) Nope. Keirin is still there~","L Lololol, look at him scraping her nerves.","L After the Medes Family, it’s Keirin lol.","L This rivalry is intense lololol.","_ But isn’t Leor more famous worldwide?","L What the fuck did you just say?","ᄂ I only stated a fact lol.","How could someone be so skilled at getting under her skin?","Keirin clenched her fist.","Unable to control her emotions for a moment, mana began seeping out around her.","She barely managed to suppress it.","Nothing good would come from getting angry now.","She struggled to calm herself.","A sudden fandom war erupted.","\"Hmm... I should probably just keep my damn mouth shut.\"","Grylls silently watched from the sidelines.","It was an exceptionally wise decision."]},{"title":"Chapter 11","paragraphs":["Golden Poison Frog (1)","There was a slang expression: \"the comments got gutted.\"","Put another way, it meant the whole thing had turned into a complete mess.","I had only made the post to express my gratitude, but a few people barged in, and the comment section descended into chaos almost instantly.","It started with CheongguPrincess, followed by KingLeor suddenly crashing in, along with countless anonymous users.","Everyone hurled insults and made jokes about each other’s parents.","The notification chime rang without pause.","Doesn’t the head moderator usually step in when this happens?","As far as I knew, the head moderator intervened when things became too heated.","There had been a similar rule in the pinned notice.","Even if sports fans were the ones arguing, once it devolved into personal attacks, the discussion could no longer be considered sports-related.","L DontAbandonTheHero) Stop it! If you keep spamming, I’ll ban you!","_ CheongguPrincess) That bastard started it first!","_ KingLeor) She’s the one talking nonsense.","L DontAbandonTheHero) Even so, don’t fight under someone else’s post! I’ll open an arena thread, so fight there!","_ CheongguPrincess) Okaaay.","_ KingLeor) Okay lol.","The moment I thought that, the head moderator appeared.","They ordered everyone to stop fighting under my post and take it to the arena instead.","Everyone obediently disappeared.","At last, I was freed from notification hell.","Not long afterward, a new post from the head moderator appeared on the gallery.","[Arena: Which Team Has More Tradition?]","I refreshed the page once, and comments immediately began pouring in.","Nothing good would come from going in there.","I had heard that posts encouraging conflict between nations were bannable, but this seemed to be allowed because it was about sports.","Of course, the head moderator would probably intervene personally if things became too heated.","They seemed fairly competent at their job.","I should focus on my own work.","Now that I had returned all the compasses, I began devising a way to deal with the Golden Poison Frog.","First of all, the river where it lived was a natural fortress in itself.","The water was so clear that it was difficult to judge the depth, and the current was fairly strong as well.","If I entered it, I would probably die from a single spit attack.","That meant a ranged weapon was essential.","A bow would be difficult... A crossbow is probably my best option.","I did not know how to use a bow.","A crossbow, at least, should be relatively easier to handle.","I currently had around 650 gold in my gallery balance.","It was the money I had earned from selling the Steel-Scale Snake.","I had no idea whether that would be enough to buy a crossbow, let alone the specific type I wanted.","For now, I decided to make a post.","***","Title: Crossbow Question","Wild Grylls","I’m planning to catch a frog.","Is there a harpoon-type crossbow?","Something where the bolt stays connected to the crossbow so I can reel the target in after hitting it.","ᄂ SwordMaster) Why do you need a crossbow?","_ Wild Grylls) I need it to catch the frog. The river’s too deep to approach carelessly.","_ SwordMaster) Can’t you just fire sword energy at it?","_ Wild Grylls) ;;;","L SwordMaster) Or you could just walk on the water.","_ Wild Grylls) Sir?","_ PassingDwarf) The kind you described can be made by modifying one.","L Wild Grylls) About how much would that cost?","_ PassingDwarf) Since it’s dwarven-made, around 500 gold. That okay?","Was this guy joking with me?","I was so dumbfounded that a dry laugh escaped me.","Then again, considering the level of swordsmanship knowledge SwordMaster had posted, he might actually have been serious.","Only after I repeatedly emphasized that I was an ordinary person did the conversation finally settle down.","ᄂ Heavenly Demon) Why not master all the internal cultivation methods this Lady has taught you before attempting to catch it?","L Wild Grylls) I still need water to survive, ma’am.","L Heavenly Demon) This Lady can provide you with more than enough water.","L Wild Grylls) Then I won’t be able to ask for your help when I truly need it.","\"What the hell...\"","Why was it so expensive?","Was it studded with diamonds or something?","The price far exceeded my expectations.","I had been told that around 300 gold was enough to cover a commoner’s living expenses for a month.","This went well beyond that.","Maybe it was because it was dwarven-made, just like in fantasy novels.","I had no idea whether that logic applied in this world too.","As I had said before, I intended to ask for help only when I truly needed it.","It was like keeping a special opportunity in reserve.","Until then, I needed to be self-sufficient.","Otherwise, I would have to earn money and buy what I needed from the auction house.","Besides, a crossbow could prove useful in many different situations.","L Wild Grylls) Why is it so damn expensive? Is it plated in gold or something?","L It’s dwarven-made. Of course it’s expensive lol.","_ Isn’t that actually on the cheap side because it’s only a crossbow?","L Crossbow prices vary wildly depending on the maker.","L Crossbows are probably second only to swords in that regard.","_ PassingDwarf) Don’t forget the modification fee. This is genuinely cheap. I’m only offering it like this because I feel bad.","L Wild Grylls) What do you feel bad about?","_ PassingDwarf) For telling you to go become fertilizer. I didn’t know your situation was that serious.","L Wild Grylls) Hmm. How much does a normal crossbow cost?","L PassingDwarf) I don’t know much about human-made ones.","ᄂ Probably around thirty gold.","L A normal bow is around ten gold.","L Wild Grylls) What kind of insane premium is that?","_ PassingDwarf) If you don’t like it, don’t buy it.","L Wild Grylls) Hey now. I never said I wasn’t buying it.","L Lololol, look at that immediate change in attitude.","Either way, this was an opportunity.","PassingDwarf might be the only person capable of providing the exact type of crossbow I wanted.","It was expensive, but if dwarven goods were known for their reliability, then the price might be worth paying.","Even if it turned out to be a scam, I could simply refuse to buy from him again.","If things went badly, I could ask someone else for a crossbow.","L Don’t tell me everything else is also written in the World Tree Watermelon Manual lol.","L Wild Grylls) I’m only using a crossbow because this is urgent. I don’t know how to use a bow.","L LetsGrowTrees) I see. In that case, why not practice archery and learn about the greatness of elves at the same time?","L What greatness? lol.","ᄂ There are plenty of people better at archery than those damn elves lol.","ᄂ Here we go again. The elves are getting active ;;","L LetsGrowTrees) But generally speaking, the bow is the symbol of elves. Let me ask you in return: when you think of archery, which race comes to mind?","ᄂ Damn, that sounds annoying, but she’s right, so I can’t argue.","_ Those damn elves really are good with bows lol.","_ What good does that do? They don’t have a proper frontline, so they get wiped out anyway lol.","Despite being steeped in imperialism, elves apparently still being associated with bows was common knowledge.","At least that part matched what I knew.","I left a comment under the increasingly noisy post.","L LetsGrowTrees) A bow is still superior to a crossbow. This is also proven in the World Tree Watermelon Manual.","L What the hell is with this elf?","ᄂ She’s making that World Tree Watermelon Manual joke again.","L Historically speaking, she’s not wrong...","ᄂ Wild Grylls) My country was really good at archery too.","ᄂ LetsGrowTrees) Were your ancestors perhaps elves?","L Wild Grylls) No, no ;;","L Lololol, look at her. Not a single prejudice in sight.","ᄂ I can’t tell whether that’s good or bad lololol.","L Wild Grylls) Also, the world I lived in only had humans.","L LetsGrowTrees) A world with nothing but humans? That’s impossible!","_ He said he came from another world. Try to be understanding.","L Let it slide. He’s pitiful.","L It’s just a gimmick lol.","While I waited, it seemed PassingDwarf had finished modifying the crossbow.","I immediately sent him a trade request.","A crossbow made by a dwarf.","I wondered how good it would be.","I sincerely hoped it would justify the price.","They still refused to believe that I truly came from another world.","It did not matter much.","Whether they believed me or not, all I had to do was survive here.","ᄂ But was your country really that good at archery?","L Wild Grylls) Yeah. Extremely good. Not me personally, though.","L Was there a reason? Some kind of racial trait?","L Wild Grylls) Because there were a lot of countries above and below us that we wanted to shoot at lol.","L Lolololololol.","L Is this bastard insane? lololololol.","_ PassingDwarf) Hey. I finished the modifications. Send the trade request.","[PassingDwarf has registered trade items.]","[PassingDwarf: I included the harpoon bolt you asked for, plus several other bolts. Just know that the harpoon bolt’s range is really damn short.]","[Wild Grylls: How short?]","[PassingDwarf: Its maximum effective range is around fifty meters.]","Around fifty meters.","At those words, I thought about the stream where the Golden Poison Frog lived.","It was narrow enough to be called a stream rather than a river.","Its depth was the real problem.","Still, considering the range of the frog’s spit, fifty meters was cutting it close.","Ideally, I should hide and launch a surprise attack.","What’s this?","There was a brown bottle sealed with a cork.","The cork told me what it was.","Alcohol.","I remembered PassingDwarf saying before that he would give me a drink, so I should not kill myself.","I had not expected him to actually send it.","For all his rough talk, he had a surprisingly soft heart.","I’ll save this for later.","I planned to use the alcohol as something similar to an anesthetic or painkiller.","Being drunk could dull pain to some extent.","I carefully placed the bottle against the wall so it would not break, then inspected the crossbow.","It had a mostly black frame.","Perhaps because it had been made by a dwarf, even the design looked impressive.","The bolt is connected to it.","The harpoon-shaped bolt was linked to the crossbow by a thin rope.","I had a rough understanding of how it was supposed to work.","I should test it first.","A crossbow was difficult to make, but as far as I knew, using one was not particularly complicated.","I placed my foot into the stirrup-like part at the front of the crossbow.","I had heard that was how it was supposed to be used.","[Wild Grylls: All right lol. I’ve added the money too.]","[PassingDwarf: I included a pair of gloves too, just in case.]","[Wild Grylls: How much are those? I’ll pay extra.]","[PassingDwarf: Stop trying to get ripped off and just take them ;;]","He had already given me toilet paper for free, so I felt bad accepting anything else.","Somehow, I had ended up receiving gloves as well.","Considering that touching the frog carelessly could cause serious trouble, they were quite an appropriate gift.","If I found any valuable medicinal herbs later, I should give them to him.","Or perhaps leather would be better.","Since he was a blacksmith, leather would probably be more useful than herbs.","Let’s see. He sent it in a box.","Once the trade was complete, a box appeared.","I opened the lid of the neatly shaped container.","The first things I saw were the crossbow and the gloves.","Behind them was a bottle.","It was so unexpected that I stared at it in confusion.","I set the crossbow on the ground, secured it with my foot, and pulled the string to cock it—","Clunk.","\"Hm?\"","...Or at least, that was what was supposed to happen.","Why wasn’t it working?","I was slightly flustered.","I pulled on the string, but it would not move.","Instead, my entire body jerked with the effort.","At first, I thought it might have caught on something.","But when I pulled harder, the string slowly began to rise.","\"Grrrrraaaagh!\"","Only after shouting with effort did I barely manage to cock it.","I panted heavily, unable to hide my disbelief.","What kind of crossbow was this that even loading it required so much strength?","Was this normal?","There were superhumans in this world who could shatter mountains with their bare bodies, so it was not impossible.","I sighed and loaded a bolt.","I would start with the harpoon bolt.","I needed to conserve the others, so I planned to practice with the reusable harpoon first.","...It even has a stock, so aiming should be easy.","It was also fairly light for its size.","That made it easy to aim.","I stepped outside the cave and pointed it at a tree some distance away.","If I fired it at the hard stone wall of the cave, the harpoon might break.","A tree was a better target.","Hold my breath...","Thwang!","The moment I pulled the trigger, the sound of air being torn apart reached my ears.","The draw weight was so powerful that the gust stirred my hair.","Thud!","The harpoon flew across the distance and struck the center of a straight tree.","No—","It did not merely lodge itself in the trunk.","It pierced straight through it.","The power was terrifying.","That Golden Poison Frog would not stand a chance against this.","It probably would not even realize what had hit it.","Now I understand why it was so expensive.","I clicked my tongue in amazement at the power, which far exceeded my expectations, then retrieved the harpoon.","Because it was attached to the rope, recovering it was not difficult.","Still, I need to practice.","Part of me wanted to hunt the Golden Poison Frog immediately.","But there was a saying that the more urgent something was, the more carefully one should proceed.","Since reloading took an absurd amount of time, I would only have one chance.","I needed to kill the frog with that single shot.","If I failed, I would have no choice but to turn around and run for my life.","The moment its poison hit me, I was as good as dead.","I had to prepare thoroughly if I wanted to drink as much water as I pleased from now on.","It definitely had nothing to do with being blinded by AllFather’s offer of twenty thousand gold.","Even if only because I feel filthy, I’m definitely taking a bath.","After going two days without washing, I felt unbearably grimy.","It was fortunate that the weather was only moderately warm.","If it had been humid and sweltering, it would have been unbearable.","I continued practicing until sunset.","I even became slightly more accustomed to pulling the string back.","As the sky began to darken, I returned to the cave.","With the money I have left...","After buying the crossbow, I had roughly one hundred gold remaining.","I planned to buy as much as I could with it.","The most urgent items were snake and insect repellents.","I had been lucky so far, but I could easily be bitten by a venomous snake or insect while sleeping.","I also needed antidotes and various medicines.","An antidote was especially essential because of the frog.","The auction house has almost everything, but... it’s all so expensive.","The ridiculous fees were holding me back.","Being able to ignore normal distribution channels was certainly convenient, but the prices were still outrageous.","That did not mean I could simply refuse to buy anything.","Gritting my teeth, I purchased one bottle of antidote.","There was always a chance of being scammed, so I carefully read through the reviews beforehand.","For the repellent... I’ll buy this one.","By the time I finished purchasing everything, I had only twenty gold left.","I did not feel particularly regretful.","Not when these items might extend my life.","I sprayed the repellent around the cave entrance and near the place where I slept.","I had no idea whether it would truly work, but I could only hope.","I had read those reviews carefully too.","Crunch. Crunch.","\"Ugh. This tastes like shit.\"","I did not forget to eat several Wall-Fasting Pills for dinner.","The intensely bitter taste of medicinal herbs spread through my mouth.","I would have to survive on these for a while, so I had no choice but to endure it.","At least I had something to eat.","\"Ughhh...\"","After eating the pills, I tried to sit in the lotus position.","It was not time to sleep yet.","The moment I crossed my legs, pain shot through me as if my joints were being twisted apart.","Even so, I stubbornly endured it.","Was this the posture people used for mana cultivation and internal cultivation techniques?","The Heavenly Demon had offered to teach me, so all I needed to do for now was practice sitting properly.","Will I get used to it after about a week?","Flexibility did not improve overnight.","I would need to keep practicing for several days.","Still, I had nothing else to do before going to sleep, so I had plenty of time.","If I were at home, I would probably be playing games nonstop.","I’m glad I at least have the gallery.","I browsed the gallery while practicing the lotus position.","In truth, the gallery played an enormous role in keeping me sane.","Humans were creatures that struggled to endure loneliness.","There was a reason they were called social animals.","Was it Robinson Crusoe ?","I remembered reading a story about a man stranded on a deserted island who treated a ball like a person.","That was how essential communication was to humans.","For now, the gallery was filling that need.","I should get some sleep soon.","Time passed quickly while I explored the gallery.","I finally uncrossed my legs.","Because I had been reading posts while sitting in the lotus position, I had almost forgotten the pain.","Of course, the instant I became conscious of it again, an overwhelming wave of agony struck me.","Enduring the feeling that my joints were being torn apart, I prepared my sleeping area.","The daytime was warm, but the temperature dropped at night, so a fire was essential.","Crackle! Crackle!","I used the ignition stone the Heavenly Demon had given me and some wood from outside to start a fire.","The cave felt slightly warmer.","On the first day, I had been so exhausted that I had not even noticed the cold.","Besides, I had nearly died after being bitten by the Mad Dog.","I added several pieces of firewood, then made a post on the gallery.","***","Title: End of Survival Day 1","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a single line scratched onto the wall.)","(Photo of a blazing campfire.)","That marks the end of Survival Day 1.","Time to sleep.","_ Heavenly Demon) You have endured much. Rest well.","L SwordMaster) Sleep well.","L So today counts as Day 1?","ᄂ Seems like it. If the updates suddenly stop...","L Ugh ;; That would feel awful.","_ StarlightPrincess) Let’s both keep trying. I’ll be waiting for Day 2.","_ Living on borrowed time versus terminally ill.","L My heart is swelling with emotion.","_ Thank you for supporting Wild Grylls until now.","L StarlightPrincess) You people are truly awful.","Right.","What the hell did I expect from those idiots?","Just to be clear, I meant the anonymous users, not the permanent-name users.","Most of the permanent-name users encouraged me.","The anonymous ones, though...","No explanation was necessary.","Still, it’s better than nothing.","I chuckled and closed the gallery.","Then I lay down on the hard stone floor.","If I caught the Golden Poison Frog tomorrow, should I buy a blanket first?","A pillow might be nice too.","Perhaps because I had gone through another exhausting day, those thoughts did not last long.","Drowsiness began to overtake me.","As my eyes slowly closed and the chirping of insects gradually faded—","I want to go home.","With that desperate wish in my heart, my consciousness completely disappeared."]},{"title":"Chapter 12","paragraphs":["Golden Poison Frog (2)","Normally, falling asleep in the wilderness without any protection was extremely dangerous.","Just yesterday, I had nearly died after being attacked by the Mad Dog in my sleep.","But once someone stayed awake all night, their physical condition inevitably deteriorated.","If sleep was unavoidable, the best option was to prepare as many defenses as possible.","That was why I had spent so much money on snake and insect repellent.","I had roughly blocked the cave entrance with branches and rocks, and I had left the sword right beside me just in case.","Thanks to that, I managed to spend the night safely.","***","Title: A Strong and Powerful Morning!","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the cave with faint light shining inside.)","If you ask me who I am, I am Wild Grylls!","L You survived lol.","L Last time, you got bitten by the Mad Dog.","ᄂ So this is Day 2 now?","L Wild Grylls) Yeah. But one side of my face is stiff. I’m screwed.","L That happens when you sleep on a cold floor lolol.","ᄂ Hang in there lololol.","L Wild Grylls) My whole body aches too. This is bad ;;","Maybe it was because I had slept on the hard stone floor.","Or perhaps it was because I had no pillow.","Either way, my entire body ached.","As if that were not enough, one side of my mouth had gone numb and crooked.","The dawn must have been cold enough for dew to form.","I hurriedly rekindled the firewood, which had almost completely burned out and retained only a little warmth.","Right now, warmth was essential.","It was fortunate that I had used the clothes CheongguPrincess gave me as a blanket.","Otherwise, things could have been dangerous.","Even so, isn’t it way too cold? Did it rain during the night?","The day I was bitten by the Mad Dog had not been this chilly.","After warming myself somewhat, I stepped outside the cave.","The moment I did, I realized it had indeed rained before dawn.","Does the temperature really drop this much just because it rained?","Fog had also settled over the forest, making it difficult to see.","Shivering, I went back inside the cave.","It was so cold that I even put on one of the jerseys CheongguPrincess had given me.","It was surprisingly warm.","For now, I planned to remain inside until the fog cleared.","After that, I would hunt the Golden Poison Frog.","The time is... six in the morning. I woke up way too early.","The sun set early in the forest, so naturally I had no choice but to sleep early as well.","Fortunately, the gallery prevented me from completely losing track of time.","I should eat a few Wall-Fasting Pills for breakfast and wait until the weather cleared.","Until then, I should practice sitting in the lotus position.","My body ached, but that was probably because it had stiffened during the night.","Some light stretching should make it better.","After stretching, I groaned and forced myself into the lotus position.","Strangely enough, it was much easier than yesterday.","Yesterday, it had felt as though my joints were being twisted apart.","Now, it merely hurt a little.","That’s good for me, but...","That was not all.","Despite the aches, my body felt full of energy.","Could it be because of the Wall-Fasting Pills the Heavenly Demon had given me?","She had said they were made from a variety of medicinal herbs, so it seemed likely.","Grrrrrgle!","Ah.","That aside, my stomach had been hurting often.","The worst part was the diarrhea, which made cleaning up an enormous problem.","Fortunately, I had the toilet paper PassingDwarf had given me.","Without it, I would have suffered through several crises already.","I cleaned everything up thoroughly so the smell would not spread.","I would need to build some kind of toilet later.","I should start preparing.","I had gathered most of what I needed to hunt the Golden Poison Frog.","The most important item was the crossbow.","Then there was the Heavenly Demon’s sword and the golden shield PraiseTheSun had given me.","Could I carry all of that?","Yes.","I had separated fibrous strands from trees and woven them into something resembling rope.","It’s only temporary, but it’s sturdy enough.","It was not perfect, but that was fine.","I would strap the shield to my back and hang the sword at my waist.","The crossbow was too large, so I would carry it in my hands.","With that, all preparations were complete.","I had even purchased an antidote, so I was ready for an emergency.","I need to remember to block with the shield.","Before leaving, I made a post on the gallery.","This hunt could become my final one, so I wanted to leave a record.","***","Title: Heading Out!","Wild Grylls","(Photo of me holding the crossbow.)","Twenty thousand gold.","I’m coming for you.","ᄂ Oh. He’s finally going lololol.","L What if we don’t hear from him afterward?","ᄂ Then he died, obviously lol.","L Aww, he died TT","L StarlightPrincess) Please try to encourage him, everyone.","L Heavenly Demon) If you find yourself in danger, initiate a trade with this Lady immediately.","L He probably won’t even have time to trade lololol.","ᄂ One hit and he’s finished~","L Do you seriously think AllFather will pay him twenty thousand gold? lol.","...","That last comment was surprisingly sharp.","Even if I caught the Golden Poison Frog, would AllFather really give me twenty thousand gold?","It would not matter much even if he did not.","I had to kill the Golden Poison Frog if I wanted access to clean water.","Receiving twenty thousand gold would be nice.","If he took the frog and disappeared without paying, I would simply cut ties with him afterward.","Or I could just dump the corpse on him.","Since it was poisonous, handling it would probably be as difficult as preparing pufferfish.","One mistake could kill me.","Rather than taking that risk, I would prefer roasting insects and eating those instead.","If I disposed of the corpse carelessly, I also had no idea what effect it might have on me or the water.","So giving it to AllFather would solve the disposal problem as well.","It would benefit both of us.","Safety comes first right now.","After checking the comments, I cautiously stepped out of the cave.","The time when the forest was still damp with morning dew had passed, and the sun was now somewhat higher in the sky.","Other beasts might appear, so I had no choice but to move carefully, one step at a time.","If I have enough time, I should build a fence too.","Simply blocking the cave entrance was not enough to make it safe.","If an owlbear smashed through everything, it would be over.","I needed to use the cave’s narrow passage to fight anything that entered.","If I only noticed danger after hearing the cave entrance being destroyed, it would already be too late.","So the best option was to gradually build a fence using nearby trees.","It would take a while, but that was fine.","Then I’ll need an axe and a dagger in addition to the sword.","Since I planned to use the cave as a permanent settlement, I needed all kinds of tools.","Fortunately, the gallery made purchasing things easy.","As long as I had money.","If I killed the Golden Poison Frog and received twenty thousand gold, I intended to buy everything I needed.","As for food... I should hunt for it myself whenever possible.","Because of the ridiculous fees, buying food from the auction house was a luxury.","It was also difficult to trust what was being sold.","It might have been different if they had things like fried chicken or pizza, but this world had nothing like that.","One might suggest buying ingredients instead, but very few people sold them.","Because of the auction house’s brutal fees, almost nobody bothered listing basic foodstuffs.","Even when they did, the expiration dates were extremely questionable.","But I absolutely need to buy salt.","No matter how expensive it was, salt was essential.","It was something humans needed to survive.","Hadn’t someone once said that one measure of salt was worth one measure of gold?","That was how important it was.","On Earth, most food was already seasoned, so it was easy to overlook.","That was not the case in this world.","Judging from the general level of civilization, it seemed to be somewhere between the medieval and early modern periods.","Salt would be extremely valuable.","Rooooar—","While thinking about everything I needed for settlement, I eventually arrived at the stream.","Perhaps because of the rain before dawn, or for some other reason, the current seemed stronger than it had been yesterday.","Even so, the water remained so clear that it was almost transparent, and the riverbed was plainly visible.","How am I supposed to lure out that frog?","Now that I had arrived, I realized I had no idea how to draw it out.","I could not simply wait forever.","Should I put my arm into the water like yesterday?","If I did that, bringing the crossbow would have been pointless.","I needed to attack before it noticed me.","Since it was poisonous, I had to be even more careful.","Splash!","While I was still thinking, I heard something burst out of the stream.","I turned toward the sound.","Something golden, about the size of a dog, was soaring high through the air with a fish as large as a salmon clamped in its mouth.","A moment later, the frog—its entire body covered in gleaming gold—landed on a rock in the middle of the stream.","The fish’s tail was still flapping outside its mouth, so it seemed to have just finished hunting.","Lucky me.","Just as AllFather had said, it was active in the morning.","I hid in the bushes and quietly aimed the crossbow.","I would only get one chance.","If I missed, there was no telling when another opportunity would come.","Keeping my nerves under control, I slowly lined up the shot.","The distance was greater than what I had practiced yesterday.","Still, this was a crossbow personally modified by a dwarf.","As long as I aimed properly, I should be able to hit it.","Besides, the frog was almost the size of a dog.","There was little risk of missing.","\"Ribbit.\"","\"...\"","The moment it finished its meal, I held my breath.","Fwing!","Then I pulled the trigger.","The harpoon-shaped bolt shot forward with tremendous force, dragging the attached rope behind it.","There was a slight wobble, but the harpoon flew straight toward the frog.","Thud! Splash!","The bolt struck the frog’s body.","The impact knocked it into the stream.","\"Yes...! Huh?\"","My celebration lasted only a moment.","I barely managed to keep hold of the crossbow as it nearly tore itself from my hands.","I could not tell whether the frog was still alive despite being impaled or whether the current was simply dragging it around, but its violent struggling nearly made me lose the weapon.","And so began an unexpected fishing session.","Instead of holding the crossbow, I grabbed the rope connected to the harpoon and pulled.","It was fortunate that I was wearing gloves.","Otherwise, the rope would have cut deeply into my bare hands.","\"Grrrrraaaagh!\"","Gritting my teeth, I hauled on the rope.","Fortunately, it did not take long before the frog was dragged out of the stream.","Once I confirmed that it was on dry land, I clasped my hands together.","They did not merely ache.","They burned.","Ugh. At least there aren’t any wounds.","When I removed the gloves, I found deep marks across my palms but no actual cuts.","I repeatedly massaged my hands.","Then I carefully pulled the rope closer and examined the frog pierced by the harpoon.","Its long tongue and the fish it had just swallowed were both hanging out of its mouth.","It was completely motionless.","It was definitely dead.","\"Hehehe.\"","This dog-sized bastard was worth twenty thousand gold.","Twenty thousand gold was equivalent to approximately two hundred million won.","No matter how absurd the auction-house fees were, there would still be more than enough I could do with that much money.","Still, I needed to handle it carefully.","I was wearing gloves, but there was no such thing as being too cautious.","\"Ribbit.\"","\"Hm?\"","What?","Was this thing still alive?","I tilted my head at the sound.","But even after checking again, the frog remained dead with its tongue hanging out.","Besides, the sound had not come from it in the first place.","If it wasn’t this one...","With a sinking feeling, I turned my head toward the stream.","\"Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.\"","\"Ribbit. Ribbit.\"","\"Ribbit.\"","And then I saw them clearly.","Several Golden Poison Frogs were sitting on the rocks.","The one I had caught had been the size of a small dog.","These were only about the size of large toads.","The problem was their numbers.","There were so many that they might have been an entire family.","...First, I should take a picture.","Even as I slowly backed away, I took a photograph.","It was not because I was a gallery addict.","I was simply curious how AllFather would react when he saw it.","Would he pay twenty thousand gold for each of them?","Or would he offer less?","More importantly, how was I supposed to get water from now on?","I already felt filthy from being unable to bathe.","\"Hrrraaaak!\"","\"Kraaak!\"","The Golden Poison Frogs all tilted their heads backward at once.","It was the signal that they were about to fire poison.","One frog would have been manageable.","If several fired simultaneously, there would be nowhere to dodge.","I hurriedly pulled the golden shield from my back.","\"Ptoo!\"","\"Ptooh!\"","\"Puh!\"","Golden blobs of poison shot toward me at high speed.","I rapidly retreated while blocking them with the shield.","Perhaps because it was ordinary poison rather than acid, the shield did not melt.","Or maybe the shield itself was simply that good.","I should send PraiseTheSun a message of thanks later.","For now, getting back to the cave came first.","This is such bullshit.","After barely making it back to the cave, I let out a long sigh.","Every obstacle only led to another.","Still, the hunt had not been entirely fruitless.","I had caught what seemed to be the leader of the Golden Poison Frogs.","I would have to comfort myself with the twenty thousand gold.","The drinking-water problem would need to be solved gradually.","***","Title: What a Weak Little Bastard lol","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the Golden Poison Frog impaled on the harpoon.)","Frog bastard eliminated lol.","L Damn, look at the size of that thing lolol.","_ Is that really a frog? lololol.","ᄂ What’s it holding in its mouth?","ᄂ Isn’t that a fish?","_ Wild Grylls) Yeah. I caught it while it was eating the fish.","_ You attacked it while it was eating? lololol.","L That’s seriously underhanded lololol.","L Even dogs aren’t bothered while they’re eating lol.","L Wild Grylls) It’s not a dog, though lol.","_ Heavenly Demon) Were you injured anywhere?","L Wild Grylls) No. I’m fine. The hunt itself was unexpectedly easy.","_ Heavenly Demon) That is a relief. This Lady prepared an antidote in case it was needed, so tell me if you require it.","L Wild Grylls) I’m okay. I already have one antidote, and there’s something else I need to think about.","_ AllFather) Oh! You caught it. May I initiate the trade immediately?","L Wild Grylls) Before that, I’m going to make one more post. I think you’ll really like it.","_ AllFather) Something I would like? How intriguing.","He was going to love it.","I had taken the photograph in advance precisely for this reason.","The gallery had a photo-album function, allowing users to upload any picture whenever they wished.","I posted the photograph of the Golden Poison Frog family gathered peacefully together.","****","Title: AllFather, Look at This","Wild Grylls","(Photo of several Golden Poison Frogs gathered together.)","Do these things normally live in groups?","There were a lot of them.","ᄂ AllFather) Ooooooh...! Forgive my vulgarity, but I find myself becoming aroused below.","L Is this guy really a professor? That was unbelievably vulgar lololol.","As expected, there was not a single normal person on the gallery."]},{"title":"Chapter 13","paragraphs":["Golden Poison Frog (3)","It took me only a moment to realize that even Allfather was borderline abnormal. Then I turned my attention to the drinking-water problem.","It wasn’t as though I had any resistance to poison, and the golden poison frog’s venom was especially deadly.","How deadly did it have to be to make a tree sizzle and melt? If it hit me, I would be finished instantly.","I had bought an antidote just in case, but I had no idea whether it would actually work.","So I planned to make a separate request of Allfather—something more valuable than money.","[Wild Grylls: Hello. You’re Allfather, correct?]","[Allfather: Yes, I am. Thank you for initiating the trade.]","The moment I sent Allfather a trade request, he replied. His manner of speaking was far more refined than that of the others.","Judging by how he had immediately identified the golden poison frog and by the posts he normally wrote in the Gallery, he seemed to be some kind of academic, perhaps a professor.","An extremely wealthy academic, at that. He had been willing to burn twenty thousand gold on a single frog, so I couldn’t even begin to guess what he did for a living.","Then again, I barely knew who anyone here really was.","[Wild Grylls: You need the frog, right? I’ll register it immediately.]","[Allfather: Thank you. As promised, I will register twenty thousand gold. However, are you aware that trades exceeding ten thousand gold transmit your location to the moderators?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. I know.]","Trades worth more than ten thousand gold automatically transmitted the participants’ locations to the moderators because there were too many ways such transactions could be abused.","They could be used to launder illegally acquired profits or purchase war supplies in bulk.","Gold charged into the Gallery could not be converted back into cash, but there were still plenty of opportunities for misuse.","Of course, since I was in the Forest of Four Seasons, it hardly mattered. In fact, having my location transmitted might not be entirely bad.","[Wild Grylls: Before that, may I ask one more favor? If you agree, I’ll lower the price from twenty thousand gold to fifteen thousand.]","[Allfather: Hmm? What kind of favor?]","[Wild Grylls: I need an antidote suitable for the golden poison frog’s venom. As you saw in my earlier post, I’m having trouble securing water.]","There might have been another river nearby. However, that stream was the closest source of water.","As long as the golden poison frog remained there, I could neither wash myself nor obtain drinking water.","Searching for another river would also be extremely difficult, since I might get lost.","[Allfather: I believe I understand your situation. I accept your request. As it happens, I was interested in researching that aspect as well.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. We can consider the remaining five thousand gold payment for the antidote. Would having more specimens make your research easier?]","[Allfather: Naturally. However, golden poison frogs are extremely rare, so please take care not to drive them to extinction.]","I wasn’t so sure about that.","No matter how precious the golden poison frog was, could it possibly be more valuable than my life?","If the antidote worked, that would be a different story. But if it didn’t, I might have to wipe out every golden poison frog in the area.","I had recently learned just how important a stable water supply was. Not being able to wash was driving me insane.","Whenever a transaction exceeded ten thousand gold, the user’s location was immediately sent to the head moderator.","The rule was supposedly meant to prevent abuse, but the head moderator could also abuse it.","I didn’t know the exact conditions or method by which a head moderator was selected, but there must have been previous head moderators as well.","I suddenly became curious about the Gallery’s history, but that wasn’t something I needed to worry about right now.","[Allfather: If you discover any rare plants or animals in the future, or anything you have never seen before, please make a post about it. I will answer to the best of my knowledge.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. I’ll see you next time.]","[Allfather: It is rare to find someone as polite as you in the Gallery, Mr. Grylls. How remarkable. Please stay safe.]","And with that, my trade with Allfather came to an end.","As soon as the transaction was completed, I checked the money deposited into my Gallery account.","A small fee had been deducted because of the size of the transaction, but nearly fifteen thousand gold had still been credited to my account.","I could use it to purchase various supplies from the auction house. I had already considered what I needed.","’Before that, I should ask the head moderator where my location shows up.’","Title: Head Mod, Can You See My Location?","Wild Grylls","I just traded with Allfather. Can you see where I am?","_DontAbandontheHero: Yes! It says you’re in the Forest of Four Seasons! Right in the middle of it, too!","└ Wild Grylls: Ah, f—","└ LMAOOOOO","└ LMAOOOOO","└ Abandon all hope kekekekeke","_ Officially confirmed by the head mod: Forest of Four Seasons, LOL.","I shouldn’t have asked.","I suppressed the despair surging through me.","The Gallery was supposed to be inaccessible from the Forest of Four Seasons, yet I was an exception. It had even clearly revealed my location.","Who the hell was playing this kind of prank on me?","I couldn’t understand it at all.","└ Wild Grylls: You’re seriously not lying?","_DontAbandontheHero: Yes! I swear on my holy sword that it’s true!","_ Grylls, let’s just give up already...","└ You’re going to have to live there.","Those bastards.","Was escaping not even considered an option?","Now that even the head moderator had confirmed it, all I could do was let out a bitter sigh. Even the last shred of hope had vanished.","Escaping would be difficult anyway. The landscape changed constantly even just beyond the stream, severely limiting the area in which I could move.","’Fine. I’ll survive here. But I’m definitely going to escape.’","Even if it took years, I wanted to see civilization again someday.","I immediately wrote another post in the Gallery.","This time, it wasn’t to complain about my situation. I wanted to ask what supplies I would need from now on.","Title: Survival Experts, Help","Wild Grylls","Looks like I’ll have to live in the forest from now on, so I’m planning to buy some supplies.","So far, I’ve thought of an axe, dagger, shovel, hammer, emergency rations, water, soap, medicine, and stuff like that. Is there anything else I need?","└ Use unscented soap if possible. The smell might attract bears.","_ If you know how to set traps, make some around your shelter. No idea whether they’ll work in the Forest of Four Seasons, though.","└ You should definitely gather charcoal. You can use it to filter water or even brush your teeth.","└ That’s useful, but the warmth might attract snakes.","_ Never eat mushrooms unless it’s an emergency.","They weren’t being sarcastic. They sincerely taught me useful survival tips one by one.","I hadn’t known about the charcoal in particular.","As for snakes, I could probably deal with them using repellent. That was why I had spent so much money buying it.","└ Nobody knows what’s in the Forest of Four Seasons, so everything will probably be dangerous.","└ You’ll likely have to learn most things through personal experience.","└ Yeah, that’s probably right.","└ When would anyone ever have a reason to enter the Forest of Four Seasons? Kek.","But those were ultimately only the most basic principles of ordinary wilderness survival.","I was the first person to actually live in the Forest of Four Seasons.","There was already a frog the size of a dog wandering around. The truth was that no one knew what else might be out there.","’Still, I should buy whatever I can.’","One by one, I purchased the items recommended by the adventurers.","It would be best to use this cave as my base.","Finally, I bought a large sheet of paper, a quill, and a bottle of ink.","Since the compass didn’t work, I planned to create a map using nothing but my own sense of direction.","’I should mainly mark the places where the terrain changes constantly.’","There was a good chance places other than the stream changed in the same way. Knowing which areas did so would make it easier to move around.","It would also be wise to mark the zones where dangerous beasts appeared. More precisely, their territories.","Perhaps the reason no other beasts had approached this place until now was because it had originally been the mad dog’s territory.","But that protection would not last forever. The owlbear had already devoured the mad dog’s corpse with great enthusiasm.","There was no guarantee that the owlbear would not come here next. I needed to prepare for that possibility.","\"Hmm...\"","I crossed my arms as I looked at the various supplies I had purchased.","What should I do first?","People said that when you were truly busy, you had so many things to do that you couldn’t even decide where to begin. That described my situation perfectly.","Should I build a fence and secure the area first, or explore the surroundings a little more?","The former would take far too long, while the latter would leave me vulnerable in the future.","’I don’t even know how long building a fence will take.’","This was the kind of situation where I should ask for advice.","I wrote another post in the Gallery.","If it looked like the work would take too long, I would explore the area instead.","Title: I’m Planning to Build a Fence Around My Home. Any Advice?","Wild Grylls","I want to build a fence to prevent intruders from getting in. Any advice?","_Passing Dwarf: Do you even know how to build a fence?","└ Wild Grylls: You just hammer it together, right?","└ Passing Dwarf: ;;;","└ \"Just hammer it together,\" LMAO.","_ That phrasing is killing me, kekekeke.","└ Passing Dwarf: Anyway, what you’re imagining is probably closer to a defensive wall than a fence. You said there’s an owlbear nearby, right?","└ Wild Grylls: Y-Yeah.","└ Passing Dwarf: In that case, you’d be better off setting traps near the entrance. Give yourself at least one or two months to build a wall properly.","└ Wild Grylls: One or two months? I’m making it out of wood.","_ Passing Dwarf: If you don’t believe me, go make one right now.","└ Wild Grylls: Fine, I will.","Thud!","Was he serious?","Even as I looked at the post with suspicion, I got to work. Actions spoke louder than words.","Trees were everywhere nearby, so acquiring materials would be easy. I had also bought an axe specifically for logging.","’This axe is heavier than I expected.’","Even holding it with both hands, I could feel its considerable weight.","I stood in front of a moderately sized tree.","It grew straight upward without bending, making it ideal for building a defensive wall.","Still, one month was ridiculous.","Confidently, I swung the axe.","’As expected of a new axe. It feels great in the hands.’","At this rate, it wouldn’t take long at all.","Passing Dwarf had seriously underestimated me.","\"Huff... Huff...\"","I take that back.","He hadn’t underestimated me. His assessment had been extremely objective.","Panting heavily, I stared at the tree.","Despite chopping at it with all my strength, I hadn’t even cut halfway through.","The outer layers had been manageable, but the closer I got to the center, the harder the wood seemed to become.","’I have a newfound respect for lumberjacks.’","The woodcutters who appeared all the time in fairy tales had actually been incredible people.","No wonder so many of them had several children to support.","I wiped away the sweat pouring down my face and stared at the half-cut tree.","If cutting down a single tree was this difficult, there was no way I could build an entire defensive wall.","Humans truly were helpless when working alone.","In the end, I had no choice but to postpone building the wall.","Just as Passing Dwarf had said, setting traps would be better.","Title: F—, Why Is This Tree So Hard?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a slightly chopped tree)","This is killing me.","└ It’s hard now that you’ve actually tried it, isn’t it?","_ Did you think logging was a joke?","└ You had it easy all this time because other people did the hard work for you, huh? LMAO.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m sorry. I’ll never act cocky again.","└ SwordMaster: Learning a mana cultivation technique would make it somewhat easier.","_ Heavenly Demon: The one above speaks the truth. Hurry and begin by practising the lotus position.","_ Wild Grylls: O-Okay. I will.","_ Did all his confidence just disappear?","_ That’s better than acting recklessly and getting himself killed.","_ Passing Dwarf: See that you do not get cocky again.","└ Wild Grylls: Yes, brother.","└ He suddenly became so respectful, LMAO.","Thanks to them, I was able to settle on a clear course of action.","I would create traps near the cave entrance that only I knew about.","The defensive wall could wait until after I trained in whatever internal-energy or mana cultivation technique they were talking about.","At my current level, it consumed far too much stamina.","’Digging will take a long time too.’","Having completed military service, I knew all too well how exhausting it was to shovel dirt.","It usually took three or four people working together an entire day to construct a single defensive position.","Moreover, considering the size of the owlbear I had seen, I would have to dig much deeper than my own height.","’This is seriously hopeless.’","Nothing was easy.","Humans were far too powerless in the wilderness.","But did that mean I would give up?","Absolutely not.","Little strokes fell great oaks. If I kept working steadily, my efforts would eventually bear fruit.","’First, I’ll dig deeply around the entrance. I can work on the surrounding area later. I can also buy some fabric from the auction house to use as camouflage.’","Thinking about traps gave me another good idea.","Rather than relying only on traps, I could dig up the ground around the entrance and the cave itself.","Like the moats that surrounded castles in the old days, it would be enough as long as it prevented outside intruders from approaching.","For now, I could also use the excavated soil to form a temporary wall.","Later, I could slowly replace it with a wooden one.","’Good. Let’s start immediately.’","Nothing would happen if I only made plans.","I began designing the area around the cave entrance.","I marked where I would dig the moat, where I would pile the earth to make a temporary defensive wall, and finally, where I would leave an entrance for myself.","It was far from perfect, but it should at least help protect me.","Thud!","I drove the shovel into the ground.","Thanks to the rain early that morning, the soil was somewhat soft.","Logging had been difficult, but digging was at least manageable.","It would still take a long time, though.","’Let’s take it slowly, one step at a time.’","The fortress-building project that I had begun with such enthusiasm...","\"Owww... My whole body aches...\"","...rewarded me with crippling muscle pain the following day."]},{"title":"Chapter 14","paragraphs":["Mandrake (1)","It was fairly common to wreck your body while digging. Shoveling itself was work that required a terrifying amount of physical effort.","Without proper technique, it would be impossible to move normally the next day. Fortunately, I had completed military service.","I had at least some experience, so I could still move. Otherwise, I probably would have been bedridden all day.","’Isn’t there anything like a pain-relief patch?’","I massaged my tightly knotted muscles and logged into the Gallery, hoping to find something similar to a medicated patch.","Unfortunately, there was nothing of the sort. It seemed to be one of the limitations of the era.","Instead, I made a post asking whether there was any medicine effective against muscle pain.","Title: What’s Good for Muscle Pain?","Wild Grylls","I pulled a muscle digging yesterday.","_SwordMaster: Mana cultivation is good for muscle pain.","└ Wild Grylls: Mana cultivation can’t possibly cure everything. ;;","_Heavenly Demon: It appears you are unfamiliar with such matters. An internal-energy cultivation method—more precisely, circulating and regulating one’s energy—is indeed effective against muscle pain.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there any medicinal herb instead?","_SwordMaster: You should usually leave muscle pain alone. If you treat it with medicine, your muscles won’t grow as effectively.","└ Heavenly Demon: This is the first time I have heard such knowledge. Are you certain?","└ SwordMaster: Probably? I have a constitution that makes me stronger just by breathing.","└ Heavenly Demon: You are similar to this lady.","└ Wild Grylls: What the hell...?","_ A bunch of shut-ins are talking like that, LMAO.","_ Does such a constitution actually exist?","└ If it did, the government would have recruited them already.","I wished I had a constitution like that.","I let out a sigh.","In the end, it seemed best to endure the muscle pain. It wasn’t so severe that I couldn’t move at all, so I could probably tolerate it.","Still, working today would be difficult. If I pushed myself any further, my urine might turn cola-colored tomorrow.","’Forget the muscle pain. I just want to wash.’","I hadn’t washed in three days, and the grimy feeling was driving me insane. Oil was practically streaming down my face.","But I couldn’t go to the river either.","I couldn’t trade my life for a shower.","At least the forest was cool and not very humid. If this had been a jungle, it would have been unbearable.","’For now, I should buy some water. It feels wasteful, but I have no choice.’","I needed to maintain a minimum level of cleanliness to avoid harming my health. At the very least, I had to wash my hands.","I purchased a large quantity of water from the Gallery auction house.","It was painful to spend the money, but I had no other option until I found another river.","The water arrived with a bucket. Before washing, I tested its quality.","’Since I bought it from the auction house, I can’t just trust it blindly.’","Fortunately, it was exactly as the reviews had described: perfectly ordinary water.","It had been drawn from a well.","I used it to wash my face, hands, feet, and finally the areas where sweat tended to accumulate.","I also used soap. Following yesterday’s advice, I chose one with almost no fragrance.","Once I had roughly cleaned myself, I wiped down thoroughly with a towel I had purchased from the auction house.","It wasn’t a proper shower, but even that made me feel considerably refreshed.","Crunch. Crunch.","\"Ugh... Bitter. So bitter.\"","Then came breakfast.","My face twisted naturally as I chewed the disgustingly bitter fasting pills.","These fasting pills were truly fascinating. I only had to chew a few, yet almost all sense of hunger disappeared.","Just as the Heavenly Demon had said, perhaps they really were made from medicinal herbs that were good for the body. I didn’t feel hungry at all.","Of course, considering their tiny size, I couldn’t expect to feel full.","Even so, I was fairly satisfied.","’Meat is a luxury for someone in my position.’","I should be grateful that no carnivorous beast had come to this cave yet.","After finishing breakfast, I looked inside the pouch containing the fasting pills.","There were still plenty left, but they wouldn’t last forever.","I could ask the Heavenly Demon for more, but she had said they were made from valuable medicinal herbs. Asking would only burden her.","’I can’t depend on the Gallery. I need to keep reminding myself of that.’","Ordinarily, accessing the Gallery from the Forest of Four Seasons was impossible.","For reasons unknown, I was able to do so.","Put another way, there was no telling when I might suddenly lose access.","I needed to improve my own abilities in preparation for that possibility.","It was a resolution I made over and over again.","’Today, let’s go in the opposite direction from the river.’","It was the area where I had abandoned the mad dog’s corpse and where the owlbear had appeared.","Because of the owlbear, I hadn’t dared to set foot there for some time.","But that was no longer an option.","Even if it only raised my chances of escape by 0.01 percent, I needed to take risks and explore.","I intended to use this place as a base and create a safe zone around it. I had no intention of living as a complete wilderness hermit forever.","Choosing to live here in the first place was already the worst possible option.","Even if it took time, I still held on to the hope of escaping.","’I’ll take the sword and shield.’","I left the crossbow behind.","It was too large, and in an emergency, it would be less useful than a sword.","Most importantly, reloading after a single shot took far too long. That delay alone could cause serious trouble.","Besides, I needed to practise the basic swordsmanship SwordMaster had posted.","I had been studying it little by little whenever I had time.","’When bracing myself, I put my left leg forward...’","Before setting out, I checked my stance.","A sword-and-shield warrior was an exceptionally well-balanced combat class.","The reassuring weight of the shield gave me such a strong sense of security that I didn’t have to worry about being overwhelmed by an opponent’s presence.","Shields were so absurdly effective that I had once heard ancient gladiators were sometimes forced to fight without them because they were considered too unfair.","’Let’s go.’","With slight nervousness, I stepped outside the cave.","The unfinished hole I had begun digging yesterday remained near the entrance.","Once I returned from exploring, I would have to start shoveling again.","Just imagining it was horrifying.","But I couldn’t simply leave it unfinished.","Being alone was truly miserable.","Title: Heading Out to Explore","Wild Grylls","(Photo of me looking into the forest while holding a sword and shield)","Today, I’m going in the opposite direction from the river.","For reference, it’s where the owlbear appeared.","_Heavenly Demon: Is that not dangerous? You still have many fasting pills, so I believe it would be best to master an internal-energy cultivation method before going.","└ SwordMaster: The Heavenly Demon is right. Wouldn’t it be better to train inside first?","└ Starlight Princess: You’re not actually going to make your life as fragile as a fly’s, are you...?","└ PraiseTheSun: I went through the trouble of giving you that shield. It would be rather upsetting if you died.","_ Passing Dwarf: My crossbow weeps... It weeps...","└ Wild Grylls: Can’t you all just cheer me on...? I’ll run away immediately if an owlbear appears.","└ He’s sulking, LMAO.","_ We can’t help it. We’re genuinely worried about you, LOL.","└ That just means everyone cares about you.","└ The Gallery will be sad if you die.","\"...\"","It felt nice to know that so many people cared about me, just as the comments said.","Was this why people became addicted to browsing the Gallery?","Unlike genuine attention seekers, I desperately needed conversations with other people.","How would I have survived the loneliness if I hadn’t had the Gallery?","’No, that’s wrong. The mad dog would have killed me.’","With that thought, I headed toward the area where the owlbear had appeared before.","When I reached the place where I had discarded the mad dog’s corpse, I found it surprisingly clean.","Some bones, scraps of flesh, and part of the head remained, but it was far better than leaving the entire corpse untouched.","If the owlbear hadn’t dealt with it, the body would have been swarming with maggots and insects while giving off a terrible stench.","’Still, I shouldn’t get close.’","Using the mad dog’s corpse as a landmark, I turned right.","The trees were densely packed in that direction.","Open terrain was somewhat dangerous. If I encountered the owlbear there, I might not be able to escape.","Of course, considering its house-sized body, it could probably knock the trees down while chasing me.","But I still had to increase my chances of survival, even if only slightly.","\"There are quite a lot of trees.\"","As I pushed through them, I made sure to mark the trunks with my sword.","If anything about the terrain felt strange, I intended to turn around immediately without looking back.","Space twisted and tangled here as badly as my own life, so I needed to remain especially cautious.","\"Heave-ho. Huh?\"","When I emerged from the densely packed trees, a clearing spread out before me.","It was quite large and covered with thick weeds.","’...Is a boss monster going to appear?’","In games, places like this were exactly where boss monsters tended to jump out.","Just in case, I walked back toward the trees.","The location might suddenly change, so I had to be careful.","After observing the area for a while, however, I realized that the likelihood of it shifting was low.","The clearing was somewhat large, but I couldn’t find anything visibly unnatural about it.","Most Gallery users concluded that the plants were radishes.","To be honest, they did look like radishes.","Apparently, radishes bore fruit as well.","In that case, wouldn’t it be fine to pull one out?","Judging by the ring of trees surrounding the clearing, perhaps this place was simply unusual.","’Why? Why is the boundary here so distinct?’","It wasn’t unnatural, but the boundary was clearly defined.","Without lowering my guard, I examined the supposed weeds in the clearing.","Upon closer inspection, they weren’t weeds at all. They were fruit-bearing plants.","Bright red fruit hung from them like raspberries.","They might have been poisonous, so I had no intention of eating them.","Instead, I took a photo and posted it in the Gallery.","Title: Anyone Know What This Is?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a plant bearing raspberry-like fruit)","Does anyone know what this is? There are tons of them here.","└ Aren’t those raspberries?","└ They look more like radishes. Look at the leaves.","└ Radishes bear fruit?","_ They do, but I think these look a little different.","└ Allfather: Oh? You must not pull those out carelessly. This is only a guess, but they may be mandrakes.","└ Wild Grylls: What’s a mandrake?","└ Allfather: A plant that screams when its root is pulled from the ground. Hearing the scream will not kill you, but it will cause severe damage to your hearing.","└ Doesn’t hearing the scream kill you?","└ That’s what I heard too.","_Allfather: That is a distorted version of the truth. A mandrake’s scream induces temporary confusion, but it is not fatal.","└ Then where did the story about people dying come from?","└ Allfather: Human greed. Mandrakes are exceedingly rare plants. Many people have killed one another while trying to claim them. In most such cases, their actions were treated leniently because they had supposedly been affected by the confusion.","_ Humans are scarier than the mandrakes. ;;","└ Typical damn humans.","_ Why are humans suddenly getting blamed?","└ Whenever something like this happens, it always turns out to be humans, LOL.","└ Damn, this bastard’s being racist against an entire species.","In any case, pulling one out would only be somewhat noisy.","It wouldn’t put my life in danger.","Still, hearing damage would be troublesome, so I needed to prepare properly.","└ Seriously. Does he think mandrakes are weeds? LOL.","└ It’s the Forest of Four Seasons. They might actually be real.","└ It won’t be too late to decide after he pulls one out.","└ If those really are mandrakes, that’s an incredible find.","└ Wild Grylls: Are mandrakes expensive?","└ What kind of question is that? They’re one of the main ingredients used to make elixirs.","└ They’re also insanely difficult to harvest, so the auction house would go wild if you listed one.","└ Allfather: (Photo of the plant) (Photo of a human-shaped root)","_ Allfather: It should be easier if you compare it with these.","While everyone argued back and forth, Allfather uploaded some pictures.","I compared them with the plant in front of me.","Its outward appearance was identical to the one in the photograph, but the fruit was different.","The fruit in Allfather’s picture was green, whereas the ones before me were red.","’Are the fruits ripe?’","Just in case, I purchased a pair of earplugs from the auction house.","They looked similar to ones from Earth.","The description claimed they were also used by soldiers, though I didn’t know much about that. As long as they sealed my ears tightly, that was enough.","Since the root was supposedly shaped like a person, it shouldn’t be difficult to identify.","└ Wild Grylls: Do I just pull it out? There’s no chance I’ll hear the sound.","_ Allfather: If you are fully prepared, simply pull it out firmly, just as you would pull up a radish.","└ Wild Grylls: Okay.","So I only had to grab it and pull with all my strength.","I immediately got to work.","Now that I was wearing earplugs, I should be fine even if it screamed.","The product description claimed they could even block the sound of cannon fire.","That might have been an exaggeration, but the reviews suggested they were highly reliable.","After letting out a nervous breath, I pulled with all my might.","\"Heave... ho!\"","Pop!","I felt it catch on something halfway through, but I managed to pull it out without much trouble.","I immediately examined the plant’s root.","According to the Gallery, mandrakes were shaped like humans.","Not exactly human, but close enough to resemble one.","\"Huh?\"","However, what I had pulled out was far stranger than that.","To be more precise, it looked like an actual person.","It didn’t merely have a humanoid shape. Its proportions were exactly the same as a person’s.","Its arms and legs were clearly defined, and even its facial expression was distinct.","It even had fine, beard-like hairs growing along its chin.","Rather than merely resembling a person, it looked as though someone had copied an actual human appearance onto the root.","To make matters stranger, it stood with its arms crossed, looking unbearably dignified.","’And why is it so red? Is this a mandrake or red ginseng?’","It resembled a mandrake, but there were far too many differences.","I would have to ask the others directly.","Flash!","Just as I was about to log into the Gallery, the root, whose eyes had been closed, suddenly snapped them open.","Because its entire body was red, I didn’t realize at first that it had opened its eyes.","Only when it slowly uncrossed its arms did I finally notice.","\"Huh?\"","\"Huuuuup...!\"","While I stood there in confusion, the root began drawing in an enormous breath.","That was when I felt something was wrong.","I hurriedly tried to release it, but the situation Allfather had warned me about unfolded first.","[UWOOOOOOOOOOOOH!]","A scream—no, a monstrous roar—pierced straight through the earplugs.","Without them, my hearing wouldn’t merely have been damaged. My eardrums would have burst.","I grimaced and stumbled backward.","Because I had clapped both hands over my ears, I ended up dropping the mandrake.","Was it going to burrow back into the ground?","I cautiously opened the eyes I had squeezed shut.","Why was it just standing there?","It had merely let out one roar before crossing its arms again.","Because it looked so much like a person, it seemed to be staring up at me with a deeply displeased expression.","According to Allfather, it should have continued screaming until it was replanted.","So what exactly was this?","Rumble—!","While I was still wondering, an earthquake suddenly struck.","I nearly lost my balance.","First a monstrous roar, and now an earthquake.","That didn’t seem like a good sign.","’Let’s just grab this one and leave.’","I hurriedly seized the mandrake.","To stop it from roaring again, I forcefully clamped my hands over its mouth.","The root itself was so thick that covering its mouth was difficult, but using both hands made it possible.","\"Mmph! Mmph! Mmph!\"","Apparently, it hadn’t expected me to gag it, because it began struggling violently.","That was what it got for standing there with its arms crossed.","All I had to do was return to the cave.","Without wasting another moment, I started moving.","Pop! Pop!","\"Huh...?\"","What the hell were those things?","I stopped before I could take another step.","Red, human-shaped figures were emerging from the ground all around me.","The entire clearing churned as though corpses buried in a graveyard were rising from the dead.","The creatures emerging from the earth looked exactly like the mandrake that had just roared.","There were men, women, children, and elderly figures mixed among them, but since every single one was red, they were undoubtedly mandrakes.","’I’m screwed.’","This was bad.","No, it went beyond bad. It felt ominous.","Still holding the mandrake, I turned my back on them.","I had a rough idea of what they were about to do.","Hadn’t the golden poison frogs done something similar only yesterday?","The difference was that I could block the frogs’ poison with my shield.","Sound was another matter.","My only option was to run as far away as possible.","Worse still, I was using both hands to keep the mandrake’s mouth shut.","\"Hiss!\"","\"Huuup!\"","By the time I reached the densely packed trees—","[UWOOOOOOOOOOOOH!]","An enormous shock wave slammed into my back.","***","Title: What Should You Do After Being Hit by a Sound Attack?","Wild Grylls","A whole group of mandrakes screamed at once. Does anyone know how to treat this?","└ Heavenly Demon: A sound attack and a scream? Were you struck by a Lion’s Roar?","└ Wild Grylls: Something similar.","└ Heavenly Demon: How badly were you injured?","└ Wild Grylls: My ears keep ringing.","└ Heavenly Demon: Then it seems you were struck properly. Have you lost your hearing, or is there blood coming from your ears?","_ Wild Grylls: Fortunately, no. I was wearing earplugs.","└ Heavenly Demon: Then your hearing is unlikely to have suffered permanent damage. With sufficient rest, you should recover quickly. However, you will likely suffer from tinnitus for a while, so I shall obtain medicine for you.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you. Have you ever been hit by a Lion’s Roar, Heavenly Demon?","└ Heavenly Demon: I have. This lady tore out the bastard’s throat so that he would never shout again for the rest of his life.","└ Wild Grylls: Sh-Shiver...","└ What the hell did you do to make a whole group of mandrakes scream?","_ Wild Grylls: I pulled one out, and when it roared, all the others came out of the ground on their own.","└ ??? I’ve never heard of that happening.","└ Are you sure those were mandrakes?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll upload a picture.","Title: Is This Really a Mandrake?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a battered red mandrake)","It really does look like a person, but why is its body so red?","└ What happened to it? Its face looks like it got beaten to hell.","└ Wild Grylls: It kept making noise, so I grabbed it by the head and slammed it into a wall. I also stuffed dirt into its mouth.","└ That’s seriously cruel, LOL.","_ Silence magic—physical edition, LMAO.","_ Aren’t mandrakes plants? Can they even feel pain?","└ They’re closer to monsters, so they do feel pain. But this is the first time I’ve heard of someone beating one until it shut up, LOL.","└ Do mandrakes normally look like that, though?","└ I heard they resemble people, but that thing is practically human.","└ At that point, isn’t it just a monster rather than a mandrake?","└ Normal mandrakes look vaguely human, which makes them unsettling. That one looks exactly human, so it feels even stranger.","└ Maybe it’s some kind of hundred-year-old mandrake?","└ LOL, what is this, wild ginseng?","└ I looked it up in a book. Apparently, red mandrakes are a superior species of mandrake.","└ What book did you check?","_ An encyclopedia of medicinal herbs. It says they’re incredibly rare.","└ How rare?","_ It says they’re even more valuable because they’re a superior species.","└ LOL, wasn’t that book written by some quack?","└ LMAO.","└ It was written by a highly respected scholar. ;;","└ Don’t elixirs use mandrakes as an ingredient? Could that thing be used too?","└ Yeah. That’s why only magic towers are allowed to cultivate mandrakes.","└ If that’s a superior species, how powerful would it be?","While everyone continued arguing over the red mandrake—","└ Allfather: Oh. By Aragon, no. I believe that is a fully matured mandrake.","Fatheremon—no, Allfather—responded with something close to outright shock."]},{"title":"Chapter 15","paragraphs":["Mandrake (2)","└ An adult?","└ You mean a fully grown mandrake?","_ Allfather: Yes. Once a mandrake finishes growing, its body turns red. I even wrote a paper on the subject.","_ Then what are the mandrakes we’ve known until now? Are you saying they were immature?","_ Allfather: According to my past research, yes. Did it pause before roaring?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. When I pulled it out, it was standing there with its arms crossed. Then it roared afterward.","└ Allfather: That makes it even more certain. Just as human infants do little more than cry, mandrakes are the same. Their grotesque appearance is likely because they have not finished growing.","Allfather’s explanation was roughly as follows.","For a mandrake to mature, it needed soil so rich in mana that it practically overflowed, as well as an environment free from outside threats.","However, lands rich in mana were extremely rare, and the mandrake was highly likely to lose out to other competing organisms.","If the conditions were any less ideal, humans, monsters, or wild beasts would inevitably chew, eat, or tear it apart before it could grow.","In other words, a mandrake could only reach adulthood if every condition was perfectly met.","Artificially raising one was practically impossible as well, because it had to be continuously supplied with an enormous amount of mana.","└ I get that it’s a fully grown mandrake, but is it more effective than an ordinary one?","└ Allfather: Yes. A single adult specimen can be used to create a highest-grade elixir. Considering that a normal highest-grade elixir requires ten mandrakes, that is remarkable.","└ He struck medicinal gold.","└ Grylls is about to make a fortune again.","└ Are you planning to sell it?","I wasn’t sure.","At the question of whether I intended to sell it, I looked at the mandrake.","It had made such a racket that I had slammed it against the wall several times, after which it became quiet.","Though \"quiet\" was probably less accurate than \"unconscious.\"","I wasn’t sure whether it was even appropriate to sell something like this.","’Maybe it would be easier to think of it as hundred-year-old wild ginseng.’","I researched mandrakes a little more to find out exactly what they were.","From what I learned, they were one of the main ingredients used in elixirs and countless types of potions.","Their roots, leaves, and stems could all be used as medicinal herbs, so practically no part went to waste.","They were plants seemingly born for the sole purpose of becoming potion ingredients.","Alchemy was essential, however, if one wanted to draw out their full effectiveness.","’Should I give it to SwordMaster?’","He had given me an elixir before, so this seemed like an appropriate way to repay him.","If I harvested more later, I could give some to the Heavenly Demon and the other regular users.","It would be especially good for the Heavenly Demon, since she was an elderly woman.","Hadn’t she even given me a valuable medicinal herb when my body was in terrible condition?","PraiseTheSun had also given me a shield for free, so I intended to return the favor without asking for payment.","First, though, I would repay SwordMaster.","I could always harvest another mandrake later.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m not selling it. I’m going to give it to SwordMaster. He gave me an elixir before, so I want to repay him.","└ SwordMaster: I don’t need it.","└ Wild Grylls: Think of it as a health supplement.","└ SwordMaster: I’m already healthy.","└ Wild Grylls: There’s nothing wrong with becoming even healthier, is there?","└ SwordMaster: I don’t want to become any healthier than I already am. ;;","_ Wild Grylls: Why not? Why wouldn’t you want to become healthier...?","└ Someone who doesn’t want to be healthy, LOL.","└ Why doesn’t he want it? LMAO.","└ Ah, whatever. He just doesn’t want to be healthier, LOL.","└ I really don’t understand, LMAO.","└ Allfather: Even if an adult mandrake were simply decocted and consumed, it would greatly increase one’s mana.","└ SwordMaster: Hearing that makes me want it even less.","└ Wild Grylls: Why in the world...?","_ Starlight Princess: Excuse me, but could you give that mandrake to me? I will compensate you generously.","It was Starlight Princess.","She was the person who posted every day praying for a complete recovery.","Come to think of it, there was someone who needed it far more than SwordMaster did.","I replied to her comment.","I still couldn’t understand it.","Were there really people in this world who didn’t want to become healthier?","SwordMaster might not have been as old as the Heavenly Demon, but he still seemed close to adulthood.","Despite having the occasional eccentricity typical of a Gallery user, he was generally quite composed.","’If he refuses that firmly, I can’t force it on him.’","That left the Heavenly Demon.","She had promised to give me both an antidote and medicine effective against tinnitus, so I could trade it to her in exchange.","Just as I was about to send her a trade request, another comment caught my eye.","└ Wild Grylls: You gave me a compass before, so you don’t need to compensate me. But can a mandrake actually treat your illness?","└ Starlight Princess: It should improve my condition to some extent. Mandrakes contain yang energy.","I remembered.","When I had found the New Moon Spirit Herb, Starlight Princess had said that she needed yang energy.","Considering that her posts praying for a full recovery had continued for so long, there was a high chance that her illness was quite severe.","The Heavenly Demon seemed to have reached the same conclusion.","└ Heavenly Demon: If your illness requires yang energy, do you suffer from the Nine Yin Severed Meridians?","└ Starlight Princess: According to the physician, yes. Are you familiar with it as well, Heavenly Demon?","_ Heavenly Demon: Of course I am. It is the most famous of all severed-meridian conditions. How could I not know of it?","└ Starlight Princess: Then you must know its symptoms as well.","└ Heavenly Demon: How unfortunate. Stay strong.","└ Wild Grylls: Is it a serious disease?","└ Heavenly Demon: It is an illness that exchanges a heaven-reaching talent for one’s lifespan. Even those who survive for a long time rarely live past twenty.","└ Starlight Princess: You know it well. Recently, my body has grown so weak that I can no longer leave my bed. I suppose I am beginning to enter the dangerous stage.","└ Wild Grylls: ;;;","└ Is she suggesting they die together? LOL.","└ Talk about dragging someone down with you, LMAO.","└ I’m actually curious which of them will die first.","└ You really are an awful person. ;;","I felt like I needed to give it to her immediately.","Her illness was far more serious than I had expected.","Perhaps because a cure was difficult to find, her posts praying for complete recovery had continued without end.","She had said she needed a medicinal herb on the level of the New Moon Spirit Herb to be fully cured, so finding one must have been like plucking a star from the sky.","I was a little taken aback, but then realized that she was joking and gave a bitter smile.","She had probably made the remark to break the uncomfortable atmosphere.","It was a kind of self-deprecating joke.","Whenever I saw situations like this, I was reminded that good health truly was the most important thing.","Health was an asset that could not be exchanged for anything else.","└ Wild Grylls: I didn’t realize it was that serious. I’m sorry.","_ Starlight Princess: It’s all right. You’re also someone who could die at any moment, Mr. Grylls.","└ Wild Grylls: Ma’am?","└ Starlight Princess: I’m joking.","└ That didn’t sound like a joke, LOL.","└ Wild Grylls: In any case, would an adult mandrake be effective against the Nine Yin Severed Meridians?","_ Allfather: I cannot say for an ordinary mandrake, but an adult specimen should have some effect.","└ Starlight Princess: Even some effect would be valuable. Mandrakes are already rare plants to begin with.","└ Heavenly Demon: It seems it is not potent enough to cure the Nine Yin Severed Meridians completely.","└ Is there no cure for it?","└ There is. Usually, there are three methods. One is to take medicine, another is for a physician to open each meridian individually, and the last is for a man to directly transfer his energy into her.","└ The first two sound fine, but what’s with the last one? Is it what I think it is?","└ Yeah. But the man also has to be sufficiently powerful.","└ Oh. I’m strong. Could I do it?","└ How strong are you?","_ I beat everyone in my village at arm wrestling. LOL.","└ LMAOOOOO.","This lunatic had just sexually harassed a patient.","I stared at the comments with a thoroughly unimpressed expression.","Because the Gallery guaranteed anonymity, people often threw around obscene remarks like that.","It might have been tolerable in a lighter atmosphere, but doing it at a moment like this made me feel genuinely uncomfortable.","└ Starlight Princess: Come if you are confident. However, if you fail to meet the requirements, I will cut it off. Keep that in mind.","└ Cut it off? You mean his johnson?","└ Starlight Princess: What else did you think I meant? If you dislike that option, shall I cut off your head instead?","_ I’m sorry. I will never act cocky again.","Apparently, she was used to dealing with this sort of thing, because Starlight Princess struck back even harder.","The third method could be discarded for obvious reasons, while the second was closer to surgery.","And an exceptionally difficult surgery at that.","Even Earth’s medicine, with all its advanced science, would struggle with such a procedure. How much harder would it be here?","In practice, the first method was the only realistic answer.","But that method was also incredibly difficult.","_ Heavenly Demon: The Nine Yin Severed Meridians can only be cured by consuming spiritual treasures such as a Solar Fire Carp, a Ten-Thousand-Year Fire Carp, or a Solar Flame Herb.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ve never heard of any of those. Are they rare?","└ Heavenly Demon: They are comparable to the New Moon Spirit Herb you gave me.","└ Wild Grylls: So they’re incredibly rare.","_ Heavenly Demon: This lady was exceedingly fortunate. That is why you are both my fateful opportunity and my benefactor.","└ Wild Grylls: I was lucky too, though. Anyway, would even an adult mandrake be unable to cure her completely?","_ Allfather: It may not be entirely impossible. The problem is the quantity.","└ Wild Grylls: The quantity?","└ Allfather: Yes. An adult mandrake may not quite qualify as a true spiritual treasure, but it belongs to the tier immediately below one. Therefore, if six or seven adult mandrakes were refined into a single elixir, she should recover.","Six or seven?","That sounded manageable.","I thought back to the place where the adult mandrakes lived.","I had been fleeing in such a panic that I hadn’t counted them carefully, but there had been far more than ten.","No.","Forget ten.","There had been at least several dozen of them.","In any case, there were a lot.","’And once I pull them out, I can just beat them until they quiet down.’","I turned my head and looked at the adult mandrake.","It was still hanging limply, unconscious.","I had heard that even if it looked dead, it would become fresh and lively again once planted in soil.","Of course, I had no intention of planting it. I was going to give it to someone else.","Pulling it out again would only cause more trouble.","For now, I should tell them.","While I was at it, I might also be able to get something I wanted from Starlight Princess.","└ Starlight Princess: Huh?","Apparently not.","It seemed she had been too stunned to leave a proper comment.","_ Starlight Princess: To think I would need that many... It would be difficult to obtain all of them, wouldn’t it?","_ Allfather: I have only seen three in my entire life. Even if one were found, someone would probably have consumed it already.","_ Starlight Princess: That’s unfortunate. Ah, you never even said you would give one to me, Mr. Grylls. I suppose I became too greedy.","└ Wild Grylls: There are tons of them here, though.","└ Starlight Princess: You’re lying, aren’t you? If you’re trying to tease me, it won’t work.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m serious. I told you earlier that a whole group of mandrakes screamed at once.","└ Starlight Princess: You mean all of them were adults?","└ Wild Grylls: Every single one was red.","└ Starlight Princess: I won’t believe you until you show me a picture.","└ Wild Grylls: Give me a moment.","Adult mandrakes were practically scattered everywhere around here.","That was what I meant by my comment.","After that, she didn’t respond for quite some time.","I wondered whether she had temporarily closed the Gallery to do something else.","Taking a picture was easy enough.","I roughly packed my equipment and headed toward the mandrake colony.","It wasn’t far away, but I remained cautious in case a wild beast suddenly appeared.","\"Huh?\"","When I arrived at the colony, I stared at the changed landscape in confusion.","Its location hadn’t shifted.","However, several adult mandrakes had climbed out of the ground even though no one had pulled them up.","They were looking around as though standing guard.","Apparently, reaching adulthood had also granted them intelligence.","’This makes things a little difficult.’","The moment they noticed me, the sentries would roar.","Then I would be struck by the same Lion’s Roar as before.","I had no choice but to wait until they returned underground.","Still, this was enough proof.","Title: Adult Mandrakes Standing Guard","(Video of adult mandrakes standing guard)","I wasn’t lying. Starlight Princess, please watch the video and respond.","└ Why is this actually real? LMAO.","└ Why the hell is it real? LOL.","└ Do mandrakes normally act like that?","_ Of course they don’t, LMAO.","└ Allfather: Oh! Adult mandrakes standing guard...! This is worthy of an academic paper! Are all those plants mandrakes?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. I took one of their friends earlier, so it looks like they’re standing guard now.","└ Allfather: Would you be willing to observe them continuously?","└ Wild Grylls: I’m sorry, but I don’t have that kind of free time.","└ Allfather: What a shame.","While I was speaking with the academically passionate Allfather, Starlight Princess finally left a comment.","└ Starlight Princess: Those are all adult mandrakes... correct?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ Starlight Princess: It looks as though there are dozens of them buried in the ground.","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ Starlight Princess: What exactly are you?","I pondered her question.","Would she tell me to stop joking if I said I was from the Miryang Park clan?","But I didn’t have any proper answer to give her.","I had no idea why I had ended up here either.","While I hesitated, comments began pouring in.","└ Correct answer! A man with the lifespan of a fly!","_ Correct answer! A castaway in the Forest of Four Seasons!","└ Correct answer! A beggar!","└ Correct answer! A motherless bastard!","└ DontAbandontheHero: Correct answer! A strange person!","└ Wild Grylls: F—, forget the others. What’s with the head mod?","└ DontAbandontheHero: I was bored! By the way, the person who insulted your parents has been banned for one hour!","└ But Grylls really doesn’t have a mother. Why ban him?","_ DontAbandontheHero: It sounds wrong! And even if someone has no parents, telling them that can still hurt deeply!","└ Wild Grylls: You’re even worse.","└ DontAbandontheHero: Ah! I’m sorry!","└ LMAOOOOOOOO.","The money Allfather had given me was enough.","I would only ask for food in an emergency.","There was only one thing I currently needed.","Perhaps it was second only to food in importance.","└ Wild Grylls: Starlight Princess, your family is wealthy, right?","└ Starlight Princess: You could say that.","└ Wild Grylls: Then if I send you mandrakes, can you immediately turn them into an elixir?","└ Starlight Princess: It would take some time, but yes. I am highly knowledgeable in alchemy.","└ Wild Grylls: Then I have one request.","This worked out perfectly.","Starlight Princess could provide exactly what I needed most.","The fact that she was also skilled in alchemy was the icing on the cake.","As expected, these people were ruthless.","I chuckled, then asked Starlight Princess again.","└ Wild Grylls: So, do you want them? I can give you the first one for free, but the next ones won’t be free.","└ Starlight Princess: What do you want? I’ll give you anything I can obtain. Do you need money?","└ Wild Grylls: No. I don’t urgently need money right now.","└ Wild Grylls: Once you recover completely, could you supply me with elixirs? I never know when I might get injured. It would feel wrong to only receive things, so I’ll give you mandrakes from time to time.","└ Starlight Princess: I will give you an elixir every time we trade mandrakes. If I can recover completely, I would give you my position, my wealth, or even my body.","_ Wild Grylls: Would you like to come to where I am? LOL.","└ Starlight Princess: Ah. That would be a little...","└ Wild Grylls: You’re a bad person.","└ Even she’d rather die than enter the Forest of Four Seasons, LOL.","└ Imagine finally curing yourself only to commit suicide by going there, LMAO.","_ Judging by the fact that she can offer elixirs, she must genuinely be rich.","└ Not potions but elixirs? She’s definitely a noble.","This was enough.","All that remained was to give her the mandrakes.","To do that, I first had to capture them.","I stared at the mandrakes standing guard.","’They call it guarding, but the security isn’t that strict.’","Even if they were monsters, they were still plants.","Moreover, their vigilance had already decreased compared to earlier.","As plants, they had no choice but to return underground eventually.","I waited until only one remained.","Pop! Pop!","Several mandrakes burrowed back into the ground.","When the last one began preparing to descend as well, I saw my chance and sprinted forward.","The mandrake noticed me, flinched in surprise, and opened its mouth wide.","I had to catch it before it roared.","But the distance between us was too great.","Fortunately, I had prepared for this.","I picked up the fist-sized rock I had found earlier.","\"Uwo...!\"","Whoosh!","Just before it could scream, I threw the rock.","I had played baseball in the past, so my aim was accurate.","Thud!","\"Guehk!\"","The rock struck the mandrake directly in the head, forcing a strange cry from its mouth.","Now all I had to do was grab it.","Before long, I caught the mandrake with both hands.","And then—","Thud! Thud! Thud!","Holding the stem attached to its root, I punched it repeatedly.","I couldn’t allow it to make another sound.","I also forcibly stuffed dirt into its mouth.","If its mouth was packed full, it wouldn’t be able to scream.","Thanks to my efforts, the mandrake soon went limp.","It had lost consciousness.","’Is this really the proper way to catch one?’","Well, all’s well that ends well.","A perfectly executed improvised method wasn’t much different from the orthodox approach.","’I should give some to Starlight Princess and one each to the others.’","With this, I should be able to repay at least some of the favors I owed."]},{"title":"Chapter 16","paragraphs":["Health (1)","There were many things in the world that money could buy, but there were also many things it could not.","Health, the heart, time, and so on. Most were abstract concepts, yet they occupied an enormous place in a person’s life.","Among them, health was especially important because it was often directly tied to life itself.","No matter how high one’s status, how vast one’s wealth, or how great one’s fame, all of it was meaningless without good health.","Most people lived without understanding the importance of their health, only realizing it after it was too late.","And by the time they tried to cling to it, the opportunity had already passed.","Even an emperor who reigned with absolute dignity was no more than an ordinary human before illness.","Worse still, once one’s health deteriorated, it was rarely easy to restore.","As the ages passed and medicine and technology advanced, new methods of preserving health emerged, but they remained limited.","Sometimes, when one part of the body felt uncomfortable, the actual problem lay somewhere entirely different. Others were simply born with ailments.","From the moment people were born, their health was destined to decline little by little.","Humans were beings who received the promise of death at the same moment they were granted life.","Yet cruelly, there were some for whom that cycle was exceptionally short.","Some were sentenced to death from the moment they were born.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","A woman lying in bed erupted into a fit of violent coughing.","She hurriedly covered her mouth with a handkerchief.","Her hair and eyes were as white as snow, and her skin was deathly pale.","Her entire appearance evoked untouched snow, giving her an air of mystery.","\"Haa...\"","After coughing harshly, the woman slowly lowered the handkerchief from her lips.","Dark red blood stained the pure white cloth.","Her condition looked grave even at a glance, but she appeared unconcerned as she held the handkerchief out to the side.","A young brown-haired maid stood beside her.","\"Mary. Take care of this for me.\"","\"My lady.\"","The brown-haired girl looked anxiously between the handkerchief and the woman.","Her large eyes resembled those of a deer.","The white-haired woman seemed to read the emotion in those innocent eyes and gave a faint smile.","Or rather, she attempted to smile.","No smile actually appeared.","Her expression remained rigid and cold, as though frozen in place.","\"Wouldn’t it be better to inform His Grace again?\"","\"It happens often. Don’t make a fuss.\"","\"But lately, you’ve been coughing far too—\"","\"I said I’m fine. Hurry and give me another one.\"","The woman spoke in a cold, blunt voice.","The maid, Mary, hesitated before taking the handkerchief and placing it into a basket atop the drawer.","The basket was filled with bloodstained handkerchiefs.","It showed just how much blood she had coughed up.","\"...We’re running low on handkerchiefs. I’ll bring more.\"","\"Fine. Bring tissues if there aren’t any.\"","\"Yes, my lady.\"","Even as Mary left the room, she could not tear her worried gaze away.","The white-haired woman merely stared back without expression.","Once Mary had finally gone outside, the woman turned her head forward.","The room was filled with a chill as cold as her face.","\"Haa...\"","The woman, Selena, let out a long sigh and leaned back against the bed.","Her expression was still stiff, but a trace of gloom had entered it.","She raised one arm and stared at her wrist.","It was so slender that it looked as though it might snap from the slightest touch.","Her skin was so unnaturally pale that it appeared powdered white.","As the blood on the handkerchief had made obvious, Selena’s health was extremely poor.","In truth, even calling it extremely poor was an understatement.","’I don’t have much time left.’","Selena thought this without changing her expression.","A congenital, incurable illness.","It did not merely shorten her lifespan. It openly predetermined it.","She was guaranteed to die by the time she reached adulthood.","According to a physician from the Central Plains, it was called the Nine Yin Severed Meridians, one of the worst illnesses imaginable.","It was a disease in which an excessive amount of yin energy completely destroyed the body’s balance, gradually ruining it from within.","Its defining symptom was that the meridians—in other words, the mana circuits—became blocked one by one.","Mana circuits were essential for human survival.","They were especially closely tied to the health Selena desired so desperately.","People occasionally collapsed from heart attacks.","Such incidents occurred when the mana circuits near the heart were blocked by disease or declining health.","In the past, nothing could be done once a heart attack occurred, but recently, cardiopulmonary resuscitation at least made emergency treatment possible.","’The gods are too cruel.’","But the Nine Yin Severed Meridians was different.","If only one particular region were blocked, like in a heart attack, that would have been one thing.","This was practically the same as having every mana circuit in the body blocked.","The vessel had a fixed capacity, yet it contained so much that even the vessel itself began to shatter.","In exchange, it granted strength far beyond that of an ordinary person.","Back when Selena had still been able to move freely, she had been called a genius.","In magic especially, she was said to possess talent that no one else could rival.","Her mind was also exceptionally sharp, to the point that even her father, Theodore, sought her advice.","’All of it is meaningless.’","As time passed, everything began to feel increasingly pointless.","She had been born into the most prestigious ducal house in the Messiah Empire and possessed extraordinary talent, yet she was still dying helplessly.","Before poor health, everything else seemed small and pathetic.","As the days passed, there was only one thing she desired.","To leave her bed and run proudly on her own two feet.","Selena knew perfectly well that it was impossible.","Despite receiving every form of support available, her health showed no sign of improving.","There were three methods of treating the Nine Yin Severed Meridians.","One could consume a spiritual treasure overflowing with yang energy, receive direct treatment from a physician, or take yang energy directly into the body.","The first method was practically impossible, even with the ducal family’s authority, wealth, and intelligence network.","They had monitored the black market constantly, but all they ever found were drugs, human trafficking, and similar filth. There were no spiritual treasures.","Every physician had abandoned the second method.","The operation was impossibly difficult, and none of them had the confidence to deal with the consequences if it failed.","As for the third method...","She would rather die.","She would bite her tongue before sleeping with a man she had never met.","She had no desire to prolong her life at the cost of her chastity.","’Besides, men capable of it are rare.’","To ensure success, the man would need to be someone worthy of being called the strongest.","However, most of the people frequently mentioned in discussions about the current strongest were women.","There was Kadir, known as the King of Magic, but he was already old.","Worse still, rumors described him as an eccentric, which made the idea deeply unpleasant.","’I don’t want to die like this, but...’","Death frightened her.","That was why she had gathered every piece of knowledge she could find.","She taught herself alchemy and medicine in hopes of extending her life even a little.","Yet the more knowledge she accumulated, the more firmly she reached the same conclusion.","There was no cure.","Could anything be more despairing?","There had been a time when she cried until her voice gave out.","Her parents also felt the full weight of their helplessness, and their expressions worsened with each passing day.","Little by little, emotion disappeared from Selena’s face as well.","She had reached the stage where she was slowly accepting despair rather than clinging to hope.","She could no longer remember the last time she had laughed without restraint.","’It’s still better than doing nothing.’","Even so, she hated the idea of simply giving up and waiting for death.","Selena raised her head and looked into the air.","A window appeared before her eyes.","The Gallery, which she had only begun accessing after accepting her death.","’I used to hate even looking at it.’","Anyone could access the Gallery as long as they met the conditions, regardless of age or gender.","That was precisely why many people avoided it.","Some disliked places stained so heavily by human desire.","Selena had once been one of them, but her thoughts changed after her health deteriorated.","\"So much time has passed.\"","She became absorbed in the Gallery at around the same time her condition worsened dramatically.","Unable to leave her bed, she spent all day browsing it.","At first, she merely lurked because she had nothing else to do.","Then, thinking she should at least leave some kind of record behind, she began posting messages counting down the days.","It had already been five months.","Put another way, her health had been worsening for five straight months.","’Not everyone there is terrible.’","When she was first criticized and mocked, she had thought, Of course. What else did I expect?","But as time went on, people seemed to realize that it was not an act and began sincerely encouraging her.","The head moderator was strange, but fundamentally just. Any abuse that crossed the line earned an immediate ban.","Thanks to that, Selena could now access the Gallery with a more relaxed heart than before.","People became endlessly free the moment they accepted death.","Selena gradually grew accustomed to the Gallery, that pit of human desire, and evolved into an excellent user herself.","A small portion of her dried-up emotions even returned.","Amusingly, most of those emotions were envy or resentment.","’Those idiots get to live with perfectly healthy bodies, so why am I...?’","It was deeply ironic.","Even so, she could not stop using the Gallery.","Recently, an especially unusual regular user had appeared, making it impossible not to pay attention.","’Wild Grylls... Why did this person fall into the Forest of Four Seasons?’","Anyone who explored the Gallery long enough would eventually witness things that defied common sense.","Recently, someone had appeared who claimed to have fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","The Forest of Four Seasons was a region where space changed constantly and access to the Gallery was impossible.","Yet he could connect without issue and had provided proof multiple times, attracting more attention than anyone else.","└ Wild Grylls: Three fasting pills.","_ Have you ever eaten meat? LOL.","└ Wild Grylls: No...","└ Want some?","└ Wild Grylls: Change your username first, LOL.","Title: Anyone Want to Bet on How Long Grylls Lasts?","I say about two weeks. LOL.","└ Even two weeks is generous.","_ He might die tomorrow.","_ A true fly’s lifespan.","└ I think the gods hate Grylls.","└ Wild Grylls: You awful bastards. I’m going to survive until the end.","_ So what are you eating today?","At first, Selena had merely thought of him as someone pitiful.","Her opinion changed after trading with him.","He could have simply kept the compass without consequence, yet he insisted on returning it.","At the very least, that meant he was not a shameless person.","’And the fact that his life is as fragile as a fly’s gives me a strange sense of kinship.’","Selena was terminally ill, while Grylls had the lifespan of a fly.","That peculiar comparison had gradually become established within the Gallery.","Occasionally, arguments broke out over which of them would die first, but those comments quickly disappeared.","The head moderator had probably decided that such discussions went too far and banned the users involved.","They were weighing human lives against each other, so they deserved it.","’If the first herb he had discovered had been something else...’","Selena had this thought every time she read one of Grylls’s posts.","The rare medicinal herb he had discovered by chance—the New Moon Spirit Herb.","Unfortunately, the New Moon Spirit Herb specialized in stabilization rather than any particular type of energy.","She could not describe how disappointed she had been.","Had it been an herb overflowing with yang energy, she would have pursued it by any means necessary.","’Would the Heavenly Demon have been in danger then?’","She could infer the answer from the behavior of the Heavenly Demon, who had presumably received the New Moon Spirit Herb.","The Heavenly Demon was one of the Gallery’s more famous regular users.","Selena was therefore familiar with her general behavior.","’For someone with such overwhelming self-esteem to treat him that respectfully, she must have received the New Moon Spirit Herb.’","The Heavenly Demon was famous for constantly posting nonsense.","No matter what others said, she continued without the slightest concern.","Through those posts, Selena had been able to infer her personality.","She was someone with exceptionally high self-esteem and confidence.","Her self-esteem in particular was strong enough to be obvious.","Anyone who posted whatever nonsense they pleased while ignoring everyone else clearly followed their own path.","’Was \"Gal!\" a word from the Central Plains meaning to rebuke someone?’","Yet during the incident involving the New Moon Spirit Herb, that same person had openly displayed urgency.","After receiving it, she even began treating Grylls with exceptional respect.","It was clear that the Heavenly Demon had been unwell and had received help from him.","’This Grylls person... seems like a bit of a pushover.’","Selena analyzed Grylls with her usual expressionless face.","His personality could be summed up in a single saying:","Treat others well, and they will treat you well in return.","His actions reflected that principle too.","Even though receiving help was crucial after being stranded in the Forest of Four Seasons, he still tried to repay every favor to the very end.","’There really are all kinds of strange animals in the world.’","Selena checked Grylls’s posts frequently.","Partly because his fly-like lifespan gave her a strange sense of kinship, but more than anything, because she felt uneasy.","If his posts suddenly stopped, it would most likely mean that he had died.","’That only makes me more curious.’","She became increasingly curious.","What strange animal would he encounter next, and how would he overcome the hardship it brought?","Thanks to him, she even began leaving comments despite rarely doing so before, and her days became somewhat enjoyable.","Tiny ripples had begun to spread across Selena’s heart.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","Splatter!","If only her body had not continued worsening with each passing day.","A sudden coughing fit seized Selena, and she hurriedly covered her mouth with her hand.","Mary had gone to fetch more handkerchiefs, leaving Selena with no other choice.","\"...\"","Fighting off the dizziness, she lowered her hand and looked at it.","Seeing blood pooled in her palm rather than on a handkerchief made death feel even more vivid.","It was a sign that she was finally nearing her limit.","Click—","\"My lady, I brought the handkerchiefs... My lady?!\"","Mary returned at just the right moment.","The instant she saw Selena, she rushed toward her in alarm.","\"...Mary.\"","\"I’ll call the attending physician immediately. There’s so much blood today...\"","\"No. It’s all right. There’s no need anymore.\"","\"My lady?\"","At Selena’s refusal to summon the physician, Mary stared at her with a look of dreadful realization.","Selena read the meaning in her face and nodded.","\"I truly don’t think I have much time left.\"","\"M-My lady, you mustn’t give up so quickly...\"","\"I know quite a bit about medicine myself. I understand my body better than anyone.\"","At one point, Selena had studied every piece of medical knowledge she could find in order to survive.","But she had gained nothing from it.","All she had obtained was certainty that her life was coming to an end.","Mary stared at Selena with trembling eyes, but Selena remained resolute.","\"Thank you for the handkerchiefs. You should go rest as well. I’ll call if I need anything.\"","\"...My lady.\"","\"I want to be alone. Go.\"","At Selena’s cold dismissal, Mary reluctantly left the room.","Even until the last moment, she did not stop looking back with concern.","Selena felt warmth in her heart at the girl’s kindness.","Her expression, however, remained as cold as ever.","’I should ask Father to adopt Mary.’","It would be both her final request and a reward for the girl who had stayed by her side until the end.","With that thought, Selena leaned back against the bed.","The dizziness had eased slightly, but her body was growing heavier.","Even taking a single step outside the bed had become difficult.","’Is Mr. Grylls... all right?’","As death drew closer, one particular person came to mind.","If Selena could be described as drawing infinitely closer to death, then Grylls was someone who constantly wandered directly before its gates.","She forced her dimming eyes open and accessed the Gallery.","’An adult... mandrake? What is that now?’","As expected of Grylls.","He had discovered yet another strange thing.","It was a plant rather than an animal this time, but that only made it more interesting.","’Mandrakes are known to contain yang energy...’","Would one improve her condition, even slightly?","With that thought, she left several comments and learned something astonishing.","’It might be possible to treat me with adult mandrakes.’","There was a condition, however.","An absurdly difficult one.","She would need at least six adult mandrakes.","Seeing even one in an entire lifetime was difficult, yet she needed six.","It was nothing more than false hope.","Just as she was about to give up completely, a comment appeared that she could not ignore.","└ Wild Grylls: There are a ton of them here, though.","└ Starlight Princess: Huh?","She had been so startled that she left a strange reply.","At first, she could hardly believe it.","Even for the Forest of Four Seasons, wasn’t that too much?","But after seeing the post and video Grylls uploaded shortly afterward, her thoughts changed.","’Maybe...’","Perhaps with Grylls’s help, she could escape this hellish illness.","Selena had made elixirs before.","She had devoted her entire life to curing herself, after all.","As luck would have it, Grylls wanted elixirs rather than money.","If she recovered completely, supplying him with elixirs whenever he needed them would be easy.","’Was this how the Heavenly Demon received his help too?’","Did Selena suspect he was a fraud?","Not at all.","The Heavenly Demon herself was living proof, openly treating him as a benefactor.","Of course, Selena did not know whether adult mandrakes would truly be effective against the Nine Yin Severed Meridians.","But she was desperate enough to grasp at any straw.","’Can Mr. Grylls capture them all in time?’","She was not merely at risk of dying in a few days.","She could die as soon as tomorrow.","Had Grylls discovered them even a little earlier, she might have had more time.","\"Harvesting mandrakes should take a long time... Will he be all right?\"","Just as anxiety began to overwhelm Selena, a trade request suddenly arrived.","For an instant, hope flared within her.","Had he already gathered all of them in such a short time?","Then she shook her head.","’He is probably only sending the one he caught earlier.’","That was the reasonable conclusion.","She should not raise her hopes unnecessarily.","Suppressing her expectations, Selena accepted the request.","[Wild Grylls has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","It was Grylls.","Selena stared at the trade window and blinked.","[Wild Grylls: Hello, Starlight Princess. I gathered seven adult mandrakes.]","[Starlight Princess: Huh?]","The moment she accepted, Grylls’s words left her completely stunned.","She only blinked with her usual expressionless face, but she was stunned nonetheless.","’No. He already gathered all of them? How?’","She had expected it to take at least a full day, but he had completely defied her expectations.","[Starlight Princess: You already gathered them all? Is that even possible?]","[Wild Grylls: They quiet down if you punch them before they scream. I also stuffed dirt into their mouths, so they should be safe.]","[Starlight Princess: ;;;]","Selena felt deeply conflicted.","She blinked twice.","Was that truly how one was supposed to harvest mandrakes?","Normally, the best method was to use silence or sleep magic.","’Is this what the Gallery calls magic—physical edition?’","In any case, he claimed to have gathered them all, so she only had to accept them.","Selena swallowed hard and continued the conversation.","Although her expression remained stiff, her written responses were far more varied.","[Starlight Princess: What if you’re lying?]","[Wild Grylls: Then you can stop trading with me next time.]","It was an absurdly gullible way of thinking.","If it turned out to be false, then so be it.","Selena let out a faint breath of disbelief before returning to her expressionless state.","Still, the corners of her lips rose ever so slightly.","No wonder the Heavenly Demon was so devoted to him.","Even if he occasionally did strange things, he was fundamentally kindhearted.","[Starlight Princess: Are you truly all right with this? These are incredibly valuable. Are you sure you can give all of them to me...?]","[Wild Grylls: You seemed very sick.]","[Starlight Princess: Thank you. Truly. But this is so sudden that I don’t think I can give you an elixir immediately. Is that all right?]","[Wild Grylls: Just send me a trade request later. That’s fine.]","[Starlight Princess: Thank you. Thank you so much.]","The tiny ember of hope that had remained within her slowly began to grow into a flame.","Selena filled her heart with hope, then suddenly became curious.","Grylls was someone who, like her, stood closer to death than almost anyone.","It would not be strange if he died tomorrow.","[Starlight Princess: Mr. Grylls, may I ask you one thing?]","[Wild Grylls: What is it?]","[Starlight Princess: What would you do if you knew you were going to die tomorrow?]","There was a famous saying:","Even if the world ended tomorrow, I would still plant an apple tree today.","It was such a predictable answer that it had become almost tiresome.","Selena expected Grylls to say something similar.","His reply, however, was completely different from what she had imagined.","[Starlight Princess: Then what would you do?]","[Wild Grylls: I’d think about what I need to do to live today.]","[Wild Grylls: Why would I think about dying tomorrow?]","Think about how to live today.","Those words pierced deeply into Selena’s heart.","Once, she too had desperately wanted to live.","But this cursed body had shattered that desire.","Afterward, she had done nothing but wait for the day she would die.","’But now...’","She stared blankly at her lap.","The trade had just ended, and several crimson mandrakes now lay there.","’I want to live.’","Ding!","Without hesitation, Selena pressed the call bell.","The moment she did, Mary, who had been waiting outside, hurried into the room.","\"Do you need something, my lady?\"","\"Mary. Take me to the laboratory.\"","\"The laboratory?\"","\"Yes.\"","Selena made another request of the bewildered maid.","\"Bring these too.\"","She pointed at the adult mandrakes.","Mary tilted her head as she looked at them.","\"What are those ugly plants? Where did they come from?\"","\"Hmm...\"","Selena considered how to explain, then quietly opened her mouth.","\"It’s a long story.\"","For now, she had no choice but to brush the question aside."]},{"title":"Chapter 17","paragraphs":["Health (2)","This was her final hope—her last desperate struggle.","That was Selena’s resolve when she arrived at her private laboratory.","Her laboratory was equipped with everything one might find in a Magic Tower’s research facility.","It was evidence of just how desperately she had struggled to find some way to heal her body.","Her health had deteriorated so severely that she could barely enter the laboratory anymore, but today was different.","\"Mary. You only need to do exactly what I tell you. Understood?\"","\"Yes! I’ll do my best!\"","\"It isn’t anything diffi—cough! Cough! Cough!\"","When a violent cough suddenly burst from her throat, Selena hurriedly covered her mouth with a handkerchief.","Mary flinched and rushed toward her, but Selena raised a hand to stop her.","\"Haa...\"","Once the fit had passed, Selena slowly lowered the handkerchief from her lips.","A pool of black, dead blood had gathered in it.","Usually, the handkerchief merely became damp.","But for enough blood to collect into a puddle meant—","If not today, then tomorrow.","She did not have much time left.","Selena clenched the handkerchief tightly.","The blood pooled inside slowly spread through the cloth.","Then she looked at the worried Mary and nodded.","With her body in this condition, Mary would have to serve as her hands and feet.","\"We don’t have time, so let’s begin immediately. First, bring me that extractor over there.\"","\"Yes!\"","\"Next, connect the extractor to the charger, and...\"","Selena continued giving Mary one instruction after another.","Mary fumbled at first, perhaps because of the urgency, but she made no mistakes.","Though not quite on Selena’s level, Mary was rather intelligent herself.","Considering that she had been born a commoner, her ability was quite remarkable.","Perhaps I should consider sending Mary to the Academy.","Before long, Mary had finished preparing everything exactly as Selena instructed.","All that remained was to extract the essence from the mature mandrakes.","After the extraction, they would need to dilute and refine it with various medicinal herbs so that the human body could withstand it.","\"Next, you need to—cough! Cough! Kgh!\"","Just as they were approaching the final stage, Selena erupted into another coughing fit.","She did not even have time to raise the handkerchief to her mouth before black blood poured from her lips.","\"Y-Your Ladyship!\"","\"Kgh... H-Hurry...\"","\"B-But...!\"","\"Hurry... Do it...! Cough!\"","\"Y-Yes!\"","She was struggling to breathe from the coughing and the blood filling her throat.","Selena forced herself to endure it and continued giving instructions.","She had come too far to give up now.","She desperately clung to her vision as darkness began creeping into its edges.","\"Y-Your Ladyship! Th-There’s a problem!\"","\"What... cough! What problem?\"","\"Th-That thing...!\"","As if matters were not bad enough, something had gone wrong with the mandrake.","Selena struggled to steady her ragged breathing and looked toward it.","Just as Mary had said, the mandrake that had been unconscious moments earlier was beginning to twitch.","It was waking up.","That was extremely troublesome.","I was in too much of a hurry to bring the flowerpot...!","A mandrake had to remain unconscious during extraction to prevent an accident.","If the extraction began while it was conscious, its scream could even destroy the extractor.","Normally, one would use magic to silence it or plant it in a flowerpot to keep it calm.","But Selena’s body had deteriorated so badly that she could no longer use magic.","And in her haste, she had forgotten to bring a flowerpot.","It was truly a moment of crisis.","Fortunately, only one of the mandrakes was waking up.","As Selena wondered what to do, a brilliant idea suddenly came to her.","He said it would quiet down if you hit it, didn’t he?","It was the method Grylls had taught her.","He had said that after punching the mandrake, it had quickly gone silent.","It was rather barbaric and had not been scientifically proven, but this was an emergency.","\"Mary! Cough! Beat it until it stops moving!\"","\"What? You want me to hit it?\"","\"Yes! Hit it! If punching it is too difficult, grab the stem and smash it against the floor! Cough! Cough!\"","Her breathing had somewhat steadied, but blood sprayed from her lips whenever she spoke.","Mary stared back and forth between Selena and the mature mandrake in bewilderment.","She looked unsure of what she should do, but ultimately decided to obey Selena’s command.","Grab!","\"Hm?\"","The moment Mary seized the mature mandrake by its stem, it quietly opened its eyes.","The creature had fine hairs growing around its chin like a beard.","Thud! Smack! Slam!","\"Kuegh?! Kuek! Kueeegh!\"","It had no choice but to close its eyes again.","Mary had grabbed it by the stem and repeatedly smashed it against the floor.","It screamed during the process, but not loudly enough to cause confusion or disorientation.","\"I-It worked!\"","\"Then let’s begin the extraction... cough! Start extracting it.\"","\"Yes!\"","Following Selena’s instructions, Mary began extracting the mandrake essence.","As the process started, the mature mandrakes inserted into the extractor gradually shriveled.","Drip. Drip.","Golden liquid fell one drop at a time into the glass bottle connected to the machine.","As Selena watched the liquid, hope began to rise within her.","Just looking at the brilliantly glowing essence already made her feel healthier.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","\"Your Ladyship, here’s a handkerchief...\"","\"No. I’m fine now.\"","Of course, that feeling was merely wishful thinking.","After coughing, Selena looked down at her clothes.","They were now drenched in dark-red blood.","Every time she coughed, what seemed like an entire bowlful of blood poured from her mouth.","Drip—drip—","As time passed, nearly all the essence had been extracted from the mature mandrakes.","Their bodies had shrunk until they were barely the size of a baby’s palm.","Even their formerly crimson color had turned pure white.","Every last trace of essence had been extracted from them, leaving them completely devoid of vitality.","\"I think it’s almost finished. What should I do next?\"","\"All that remains is... cough! Cough! Hup...!\"","Selena’s eyes widened.","She could endure the coughing itself.","The problem was the suffocation that came afterward.","She tried desperately to control her breathing, but nothing worked.","Her vision began to black out, and pain washed over her as though even her brain had stopped functioning.","No. I can’t...!","Even Mary’s frantic cries sounded like distant echoes as Selena’s consciousness began to fade.","Barely holding on, Selena reached out.","Her hand stretched toward the essence they had only just finished extracting.","She gestured for Mary to give it to her immediately.","Drinking the essence without refining it was practically suicide.","But with her life hanging by a thread, Selena was in no position to be selective.","Gulp! Gulp! Gulp!","Realizing what Selena wanted, Mary poured the essence directly into her mouth.","Selena felt the blazing energy of the essence flow down her throat.","Could something so hot truly heal her?","It was hope flaring back to life like a dying ember.","She could not give up.","I-I need to circulate my mana...","Even as her consciousness faded, she forcibly attempted to circulate her mana.","However, there was no way her mana circuits, which had long since become completely blocked, would respond.","It was bitter and unfair, but Selena refused to give up.","The final thread of her survival instinct continued to drive her onward.","Then, just before her consciousness was severed completely, she heard—","Thump!","The vivid beating of her heart.","***","\"Your Ladyship! Lady Selena! Wake up! Your Ladyship!\"","Mary shook Selena’s shoulders as she lay collapsed on the floor, trying to determine whether she was conscious.","Selena had originally been sitting in her wheelchair, but she had lost consciousness and fallen.","Had Mary not been there, Selena might have struck her head and suffered a serious injury.","But Selena showed no sign of waking, leaving Mary with no choice but to panic.","I-I need to call someone first!","Standing around in panic would accomplish nothing.","As a precaution, Mary turned Selena’s head to the side.","If she vomited blood again, it might flow backward into her airway.","Mary then rose to her feet and was about to run out of the laboratory when—","Crack!","A strange noise pierced her ears.","Mary froze.","The sound had not come from the laboratory equipment.","It had come from Selena.","Mary turned toward her with an anxious expression.","Crack! Crack!","\"Wh-What...?\"","Mary was utterly bewildered.","A bizarre phenomenon was unfolding before her eyes.","Selena’s skin was as white as snow.","However, it was an unhealthy whiteness.","Her mana circuits had become so thoroughly blocked that even her blood could no longer circulate properly.","But now, that skin was slowly peeling away, and new skin was growing beneath it.","It was no longer deathly pale.","Instead, it was fair and luminous, as though it had simply never been exposed to sunlight.","Most remarkable of all were the blood vessels slowly becoming visible beneath her skin.","It was proof that Selena’s previously blocked mana circuits had begun circulating again.","Crack! Pop!","And it was not only her skin.","Selena’s bones and muscles were also visibly changing.","Her body had been afflicted by the Nine Yin Severed Meridians, leaving her incapable of even ordinary exercise.","But now, the energy inside her—in other words, her mana—had begun to harmonize, changing everything.","The immense mana was reconstructing a vessel capable of containing its power.","In the language of the Central Plains, this phenomenon was known as Reforging the Bones and Cleansing the Marrow.","Normally, such a transformation could occur only when vast mana was accompanied by profound enlightenment.","However, Selena’s body had suffered from the Nine Yin Severed Meridians.","The mana itself had always been abundant. It had merely failed to achieve harmony, while her talent supplied the enlightenment she needed.","Crack! Pop!","Every trace of her sickly appearance vanished, and the curves of a mature woman became pronounced.","Her snow-white hair repeatedly fell out and regrew, but before long, it stabilized at its original length.","The pure white strands shone like moonlight, enhancing her beauty even further.","The final change was her face.","She had already been beautiful, but after undergoing Reforging the Bones and Cleansing the Marrow, her beauty blossomed to an entirely different level.","Although many aspects of her body had changed, Selena’s condition could be summed up in a single word.","She had obtained a far more \"healthy\" body than before.","\"Mm...\"","As the brief yet seemingly endless transformation came to an end, Selena regained consciousness.","When Mary heard Selena groan, she snapped out of her daze and urgently asked,","\"Your Ladyship! Your Ladyship! Are you awake?!\"","\"...Mary?\"","\"Yes! It’s me, Mary!\"","\"What in the world happened... Huh?\"","Selena unconsciously sat up, only for her eyes to widen.","Since she had been lying down, the first thing she could inspect was her own body.","And the first thing that caught her attention was her chest.","It was naturally the first part she saw when she lowered her head, making it impossible to overlook.","Were my breasts always this large?","Selena tilted her head while touching her chest.","Her body had once been pitifully frail.","She had believed it possessed none of the charms of a woman.","But now, soft mounds of flesh filled her vision and rested beneath her hands.","In terms of size alone, they were large enough to inspire envy in others.","It isn’t only my chest. My arms, too...","As though entranced, Selena examined her arms.","They were no longer skeletal but properly filled out like those of an ordinary person.","Even her skin was no longer deathly pale. It was white with a distinctly healthy glow.","The faint outline of blood vessels could be seen beneath it, giving her complexion genuine color.","\"...\"","\"Your Ladyship? Could you say something...?\"","Spring!","Mary had just spoken carefully when Selena suddenly leapt to her feet.","Mary was startled at first, but then stared in shock when she realized Selena had stood up on her own.","\"Your Ladyship! You shouldn’t overexert your—!\"","Tap-tap!","Mary could not finish her sentence.","Selena, standing firmly on both legs, had suddenly begun to run.","She did not walk.","She ran.","She had skipped learning to walk and started with sprinting instead.","And she was barefoot.","Mary felt as though her heart had dropped into her stomach.","\"Your Ladyship! Where are you going?! Your Ladyship!\"","Selena paid no attention to Mary’s frantic cries behind her.","She simply ran.","She ran and ran and kept running.","From time to time, she heard startled exclamations from the mansion’s servants.","Selena ignored them.","She merely continued running.","I can run. I can actually run!","She did not stop.","Even when she occasionally stumbled, she continued onward.","When had she last run like this?","She could not even remember.","No.","Perhaps she could not remember because she had never run before.","Even walking had once been difficult for her, yet now she could run without strain.","Feeling as though she had gained the entire world, Selena dashed out of the mansion.","Her expression, stiffened from years of illness, remained rigid, but the corners of her lips had visibly risen.","\"S-Selena?! Y-You...!\"","\"Dear! Where are you going?!\"","Selena’s parents, who had just returned, recoiled in shock upon seeing her.","It was an understandable reaction.","Their daughter, who had been unable to leave her bed, was now running around like a wild horse.","To make matters worse, her clothes were covered in dried blood.","To put it bluntly, she looked like a madwoman.","\"Haa!\"","Ignoring them, Selena stopped in the mansion courtyard and steadied her breathing.","Despite running so much, she did not feel tired at all.","The only thing she could clearly hear was the beating of her heart.","I’m not coughing, either.","Even the cough that had plagued her for her entire life had completely disappeared.","She could not feel anything wrong with her body.","The absence of pain felt so unfamiliar that it was almost uncomfortable.","My mana is circulating perfectly as well.","More than perfectly.","It was moving incredibly quickly.","In the past, it had always felt as though everything inside her was completely blocked.","Now, the mana that had achieved harmony flowed through every corner of her body.","Nothing hurts.","A miracle had occurred.","What else could she possibly call it?","Selena closed her eyes and raised her face toward the clear sky.","Thank you, Mr. Grylls.","He was the person who had given her both a miracle and a new life.","A benefactor who had willingly helped her despite never having met her face-to-face.","What kind of person was he?","She found herself growing increasingly curious about him.","Her facial muscles relaxed naturally, and a happy smile appeared on her face.","\"Selena!\"","\"Dear! Are you all right?!\"","\"Your Ladyship!\"","Just as Selena was savoring the new life she had obtained, her parents and Mary called out urgently from behind her.","Hearing their voices, Selena opened her eyes and turned around.","The family she loved more than anyone was staring at her with worry.","\"Yes. I’m perfectly fine now—bleargh!\"","Splash!","Selena abruptly lowered her head in the middle of speaking.","Something poured from her mouth.","It was black, dead blood.","And it was not merely one bowlful.","She vomited enough to fill at least two bowls.","\"Urgh! Kuegh!\"","Thud! Plop!","Blood was not the only thing she expelled.","Black, congealed lumps also fell from her mouth.","They were impurities that had not yet been discharged during Reforging the Bones and Cleansing the Marrow.","Her previous physical condition had been so terrible that the accumulated waste had clumped together into solid masses.","\"Ah...\"","\"D-Darling! Pull yourself together!\"","To her family, who knew nothing of what had happened, the sight was beyond horrifying.","Selena’s mother fainted, and her father barely managed to catch and support her.","Even Mary, the last one still standing, turned deathly pale at the grotesque sight.","\"Cough. Cough. Ugh.\"","Selena’s brow twitched.","The stench from the rotten blood and impurities pouring out of her mouth was unbearable.","She wanted to grimace, but her facial muscles still did not move very well.","I need a bath.","Now, she could bathe without Mary’s assistance.","The thought alone filled Selena with anticipation.","But first, she needed to clear up her family’s misunderstanding.","Selena approached her confused family and spoke quietly.","With the blood still smeared around her mouth and her usual expressionless face, she looked rather terrifying.","\"Mother. Don’t worry. I’m healthy now—bleargh!\"","Selena vomited black blood with a perfectly blank expression.","At the bizarre sight, her family recoiled in horror once again.","\"Ahhh...\"","\"P-Pull yourself together! You cannot leave me as well!\"","She still had a long way to go.","***","Meanwhile, in the gallery—","Title: Grylls, thanks.","Passing Dwarf","(Photo of mature mandrakes being steeped in alcohol)","Looks like I’ll finally get to drink some infused liquor again.","└ Wild Grylls: You insane dwarf bastard! You turned something that expensive into alcohol?","└ Passing Dwarf: Is there a problem?","└ Wild Grylls: I told you that thing was insanely expensive! And you used it to make liquor?","└ Passing Dwarf: It’s mine. You mad?","└ Wild Grylls: From now on, sharpen your knives with gold, you damn bastard.","└ He told him to sharpen his knives with gold, lololol.","└ Can’t blame him for getting pissed, hahahahaha.","└ Come on, you can’t resist infused liquor, lololol.","The gallery was peaceful once again."]}]);
